  [21248101] = "This is one of the worst time travel dramas I've ever seen! This is depressing to watch...",
  [21248102] = "I recognize that the director is trying to do something different, but can you at least write an interesting plot?",
  [21248103] = "If I ever time traveled to this place, I'd choose death.",
  [21248104] = "Forced time travel, forced farce, forced tragedy. Would anyone find this show fun to watch?",
  [21248201] = "Honestly, the production values are okay, but this plot is too rushed. I can't follow it.",
  [21248202] = "Is this the big-budget blockbuster we were promised? All that money down the tubes. I can't believe they actually released this...",
  [21248203] = "I give full marks to the production. The set details are meticulous. But what about the plot? It has no logic to it at all.",
  [21248204] = "This scared my niece to tears. If this is realistic, then give me a fantasy ancient society, please.",
  [21248301] = "I like it. Everyone's been too dumb-downed by bad time travel. It's time everyone saw the brutal reality.",
  [21248302] = "The plot is a little hard to swallow, but the costumes are so beautiful. I can watch this every day just for that!",
  [21248303] = "Really worth a watch. Just some of the acting is a little awkward. Maybe that's just the way people really were back then?",
  [21248304] = "This is a pretty good effort. Finally something that doesn't just go for cheap thrills. Worthy of praise.",
  [21248401] = "I haven't seen a drama this good in a long time. I stayed up all night binging it!",
  [21248402] = "Hahahahaha, this princess had it too tough. I really feel for her, but guess I'm better off living in the modern era.",
  [21248403] = "Is this the show that's blown up the internet lately? Naturally I couldn't stop watching!!",
  [21248404] = "I didn't want to like this to begin with, but there's no avoiding the truth. It's really amazing!!",
  [21249101] = "The plot is trite. These types of movies are a dime a dozen, and none of them are any good.",
  [21249102] = "Can you maybe learn a thing or two from some other directors. If a thriller's not shot well, it falls on its face.",
  [21249103] = "Really BAD movie. I wouldn't pay a nickel for those special effects, and the acting is horrible.",
  [21249104] = "Can we not jump around the timeline so much? Just tell the story! Why make it so sophisticated no one can understand?",
  [21249201] = "It's bad, but I guess it takes guts to shoot it like this...",
  [21249202] = "Is this really a thriller? Why do I want to bust out laughing the whole time? As a comedy, I think it was quite successful.",
  [21249203] = "I don't know what to say. I haven't been able to sleep well lately, but I fell asleep in the theater for the first time ever...",
  [21249204] = "I can't even eat popcorn to this movie. What is even the point of filming it?",
  [21249301] = "It's got its faults, but overall I think it did the trick. It succeeds in spite of its flaws.",
  [21249302] = "I watched it all in one sitting. That male lead's acting is so good, although I did find the ending a little ambiguous.",
  [21249303] = "I'm officially a fan of this male lead. Who knew there was such a diamond in the rough out there? Love it!",
  [21249304] = "It's trying to say a lot. I can see the director's got some talent, but is still a little green. I look forward to more.",
  [21249401] = "I cried! I thought this was a horror/thriller, but the ending had me in tears, like I was watching myself as a child...",
  [21249402] = "Best film of the year!! Absolute classic! A must-see!",
  [21249403] = "This film is a shoe-in for the awards. Anybody with a heart will cry when they see it. I'll leave it at that, I've gotta go get a tissue...",
  [21249404] = "I hear it's already done several hundred million at the box office, and it's worth every penny. There's not many masterpieces like this coming out these days!",
  [21250101] = "Apparently now fighting as a couple can get you on TV. Who's got enough free time on their hands to watch this stuff?",
  [21250102] = "Can the show runners spend their budget on something a little more useful? Why are they shoving this junk down our throats?",
  [21250103] = "I watched until someone went into hysterics, and it woke my dog up.",
  [21250104] = "This is all because modern life has made our lives too easy, so people have the free time and energy to go on a TV show like this and argue.",
  [21250201] = "These days they'll really put anything at all on TV. I just can't understand it.",
  [21250202] = "The original idea might have been good, but these people aren't even making any sense. They're just screaming hysterically.",
  [21250203] = "I binged the whole season, although that last episode was disappointing. What happened? The show's making money, so you just stopped caring?",
  [21250204] = "I could never go on a show like this. I'd be too embarrassed if I ever got recognized on the street.",
  [21250301] = "It's great to watch while eating dinner with the family. Really lively. The only downside is my wife is learning how to fight better.",
  [21250302] = "Some of the contestants really are unlikeable, but the show itself is fun. Non-stop laughs.",
  [21250303] = "Lol, turns out all husbands and wives fight the same. I think this show happens every day right in my home.",
  [21250304] = "Great show, but I worry if their kids see them fighting so ferociously on TV they'll get scared.",
  [21250401] = "I see a lot of myself in them. While I find it funny, I also realize there are some things I probably shouldn't say. It's really helped.",
  [21250402] = "Turning a fight into a debate is actually pretty clever. That's the way it is in my house. After an argument, we feel a lot better. Gets everything off your chest.",
  [21250403] = "Hahahahaha, I laughed my head off. Don't miss out on this ridiculous show!",
  [21250404] = "Whoever came up with the idea for this show must be geniuses. I laughed so hard my ribs hurt.",
  [21251101] = "They've gotta at least pick someone passable as the host. This person almost makes the show unwatchable.",
  [21251102] = "The show runners don't have their values in order. This is too one-sided, like they're trying to pick a fight between service workers and consumers.",
  [21251103] = "If you spend money, you should get the service you paid for. If I'm the one giving them money, how's it make sense that they can complain?",
  [21251104] = "Some things are just stirring up trouble out of nothing. I do not like this episode.",
  [21251201] = "Some of these things don't seem like a big deal to me. Maybe it really is a matter of one's point of view...",
  [21251202] = "As someone who's worked in the service industry for twenty years, I can say this is useless and changes nothing.",
  [21251203] = "Doesn't seem realistic to me. Anyway, I've gotten plenty of bad service, and complaining doesn't do anything. I feel helpless as a consumer.",
  [21251204] = "They didn't say enough. Point the camera at me, I'll give you enough material for a whole season.",
  [21251301] = "I think the production team really cares. Not many people are willing to listen to what we have to say.",
  [21251302] = "There are some areas that I really never noticed before. I'll do better in the future.",
  [21251303] = "Did anybody notice that host? His smile can light up a room!",
  [21251304] = "How about letting us underaged kids complain about our parents next time? We've got plenty to say!",
  [21251401] = "I couldn't agree more!! Listen well, people. Are you really worth such good service??",
  [21251402] = "Hahahaha, some of those ladies were pretty funny, although it sounds like they're crying on the inside. I'll have to treat them better in the future.",
  [21251403] = "No one's job is easy, but if we all try to understand each other, the world becomes a better place!",
  [21251404] = "Some of these things even make other people upset, to say nothing of the service workers themselves! Feels good to vent!",
  [21252101] = "This documentary is both long and boring. Maybe it's helpful to people who have trouble sleeping.",
  [21252102] = "I didn't get the point at all. I have no idea what I just watched. Rubbish!",
  [21252103] = "I watched the first ten minutes and couldn't keep watching, and there was still two hours left! Goodbye!",
  [21252104] = "I don't want to give any attention to this doc, but so others can avoid making the same mistake, here's my review: It stinks! Don't watch!",
  [21252201] = "The subject is good. Don't know how they made it this boring. Seems like an affront to the hard work of these incense artisans.",
  [21252202] = "For a documentary, they just don't understand how to trim the fat. So many useless shots. Is the director really a professional?",
  [21252203] = "These incense artisans really seem amazing. Too bad they got partnered up with such a rubbish director.",
  [21252204] = "I'll say it again, not just anyone can make a documentary. I'll give one star just to acknowledge it took some guts.",
  [21252301] = "The music is great, so beautiful with the wafting incense smoke. But the pacing is a little slow.",
  [21252302] = "This is the first time I've ever watched a documentary. Pretty interesting. I learned a lot.",
  [21252303] = "A doc worth watching. Turns out the true masters are among the common folk. I'd love to see more of these amazing folk artisans.",
  [21252304] = "They've devoted their lives to incense, and it's harder and harder to make a living at it. We should all pay more attention.",
  [21252401] = "A great doc!! Let the world know about our country's talented artisans! That's the spirit of our people!",
  [21252402] = "If a friend hadn't recommended it, I never would've known about this awesome movie! Worth watching!",
  [21252403] = "The director's unique style really puts you in the scene. Just beautiful!!",
  [21252404] = "I don't think anybody would object to giving this one full marks, right? If anybody dumps on this doc, they must be blind.",
  [21253101] = "They just said a bunch of stuff everyone already knows. Can we get some more substantive programming?",
  [21253102] = "As a cat owner for two years, I think I'd do a million times better than this expert!",
  [21253103] = "What the heck were they even talking about? My cats wouldn't even watch it.",
  [21253104] = "This expert has got to go. I'd rather listen to my own cat. I'd learn more.",
  [21253201] = "Aren't they supposed to recommend some cat food at the end? This commercial is strange.",
  [21253202] = "I tried scolding my cat the way they said in the show, but she just got angry. I think the show owes me a box of bandages.",
  [21253203] = "The content is fine, but isn't the expert's tone a little off-putting?",
  [21253204] = "A lot of what they said doesn't apply to our little prince, but maybe every cat has a different temperament.",
  [21253301] = "After using the expert's suggestions, my little trouble-maker is much better behaved. When's the second episode?",
  [21253302] = "This kitten I just brought home is still small, so I can't use any of this now, but I'll save it for later.",
  [21253303] = "The suggestions in the show are practical, but I've heard a lot of them. I'd like to see a more advanced class.",
  [21253304] = "Argh, I was just a little late getting home, and the toilet paper's shredded again. Is it too late to ask my cat how to make things better?",
  [21253401] = "I saw cats and clicked on it immediately. Aaaaah, I can't take it! I hugged my cat and sobbed!",
  [21253402] = "What am I, a non-cat owner, doing here? Well, whatever, I'm definitely getting a cat now!",
  [21253403] = "Amazing show. I understand so many things that used to elude me. I'm going to get along with our housecat much better in the future!",
  [21253404] = "This show is great, but I want to ask, can you all make a show for the cat to watch? I want him to meet me halfway. ",
  [21254101] = "What's wrong with TV shows nowadays? They actually made a show about studying instead of falling in love? I'm floored.",
  [21254102] = "Sure, the story is cooky too, but I just can't go on watching the faces of the lead guy and girl...",
  [21254103] = "I was stumped the entire time. Can anyone tell me what the guy and girl were thinking? I don't get them at all.",
  [21254104] = "After watching this one, I regret giving the last high school romance show a poor review. After all, it was at least watchable...",
  [21254201] = "Do high school students these days not have it bad enough already? Study machines for 12 hours a day, and even when they watch TV, it's just more studying.",
  [21254202] = "My mom nagged me again: even the kids in TV shows study!",
  [21254203] = "The plot was a little hard to stick with, but the soundtrack was good.",
  [21254204] = "I cried. Such a handsome guy actually studies for the girl. Just ask me out! I'm free!",
  [21254301] = "Hahahahaha, I found it pretty funny. The studying really threw me for a loop.",
  [21254302] = "This is everyday life for us high schoolers. Nailed it. The shows where they're falling in love all the time are too fake.",
  [21254303] = "I really liked this show. Studying together is sweet. I wish someone would study with me.",
  [21254304] = "Finally, a show about studying. When my kid isn't busy studying, I'll let him watch.",
  [21254401] = "This was just so sweet, wasn't it?! If you love someone, you'll grow together! That's the best kind of love!",
  [21254402] = "So they really were studying!! I thought the title was just a gimmick. The plot is so delightful. I can't stop watching!",
  [21254403] = "The lead girl is just so cuuuute! I want to study with her too! I do!",
  [21254404] = "An authentic adolescent love story shouldn't have all those love triangles and melodrama. This sweet, mild romance was just wonderful!",
  [21255101] = "I am very unhappy. I think 16-17 year-olds can make their own decisions. They shouldn't have their freedoms restricted.",
  [21255102] = "Of course kids want to play. This show must be joking wanting to interview them. It's inciting rebellion.",
  [21255103] = "I think this kind of regulation is meaningless. Plenty of underage kids these days just use their parents IDs to play games.",
  [21255104] = "Games aren't the original sin that causes kids to fall. It's their home and family life.",
  [21255201] = "What are these questions the host is asking? I can feel how awkward these kids feel through the screen.",
  [21255202] = "Kids sure have it rough. If they say their real thoughts in the interview, when they get home, they'll be grounded.",
  [21255203] = "I'm sure not all of them love studying this much. There's definitely some of them just trying to be goody-goody.",
  [21255204] = "Kids today are all devious, not honest like we were when we were kids. And to be honest, it's the games' fault.",
  [21255301] = "Restricting kids from getting addicted to games is right, but the implementation is a little rough. It's easy to engender resentment.",
  [21255302] = "I think it's great. I don't play games anyway.",
  [21255303] = "Nothing we can do. Just go outside and play some basketball, kids.",
  [21255304] = "Thinking is different when the shoe's on the other foot. As a parent, I'm very much for it.",
  [21255401] = "Hahahahaha, fantastic. Congrats to everyone that just turned 18 this year!",
  [21255402] = "Finally they come out with this rule. It'll save parents no shortage of grief.",
  [21255403] = "Those angry yet determined little smiles on the kids' faces are just too cute. I hope they have happy childhoods.",
  [21255404] = "There are other forms of entertainment than games. For instance, outdoor sports have their good points!",
  [21256101] = "Give me five cents and I could've made these special effects! How many corners were they trying to cut?",
  [21256102] = "Nothing to commend about the lead actor's acting. The supporting character is some talentless online celebrity. Pass!",
  [21256103] = "Boring to the max. A waste of movie ticket money.",
  [21256104] = "What was that ending? I was loving the beginning, but the ending really let me down. Feel like I was tricked.",
  [21256201] = "The plot was too incoherent, and I completely didn't understand the decision toward the end. Very anti-climactic.",
  [21256202] = "Too bad. A decent movie, but the final ending was way worse than what I was imagining.",
  [21256203] = "A movie with a messed up view of life. No matter how good the other aspects of it are, I have to give it a thumbs down.",
  [21256204] = "Different strokes for different folks, but I didn't like it.",
