  [21471101] = "Are these cats and dogs cafes really a good thing? They're just exploiting animals for profit.",
  [21471102] = "It's just an ad in disguise. I can smell their tricks from a mile away!",
  [21471103] = "I got tricked in here by the clickbait title. What an utter disappointment!",
  [21471104] = "I don't get people who spend money on pet dogs and cats. I get scared of them just by looking at them!",
  [21471201] = "Uhhh... are you sure eating and drinking near cats and dogs won't be a health hazard?",
  [21471202] = "While I love stories about animals, this one is so obvious that it's too fake to watch.",
  [21471203] = "These cats are so thin! Have they been mistreated or something?!",
  [21471204] = "These animals spend the day being petted by guests, and now they have to work overtime for these greedy capitalists?",
  [21471301] = "I laughed so hard at those adorable critters. Seeing them so cute and cuddly just brings a smile to my face!",
  [21471302] = "Quit using cats and dogs for attention! You know I have no defense against such adorable furballs!",
  [21471303] = "Cats and dogs always had a love-hate relationship. I'm a dog person, but I also think cats are adorable.",
  [21471304] = "These animals are so cute! I want both a cat and a dog in the future. That's what life is about!",
  [21471401] = "So cute! My heart is melting! Please share more stories like this one!",
  [21471402] = "I want more! Dogs and cats are the perfect combination!",
  [21471403] = "I don't usually laugh this hard until I do! These critters are just too adorable!",
  [21471404] = "Why debate which one is cuter when you can have both?",
  [21472101] = "It's so gross. I followed the instructions and spat it out as soon as I took a sip. It's disgusting!",
  [21472102] = "The whole process is too tedious. I can feel my blood boiling just from trying to make this stupid drink.",
  [21472103] = "The colors look so intimidating... It's more like breaking a pot of potions rather than a yummy drink.",
  [21472104] = "I followed the instructions, and what I got was so gross that even my dog ran away after smelling it!",
  [21472201] = "It's just an ad in disguise. Don't be fooled by such primitive tricks!",
  [21472202] = "It's a little hard to describe... Maybe it's just me, but I don't think I'll try it again in the future.",
  [21472203] = "It's refreshing in the sense that your head feels like it's going to explode the moment you take a sip.",
  [21472204] = "I'd rather spend the time resting and ordering takeout instead.",
  [21472301] = "It looks delicious! I'm going to try to make it myself when I get the chance next time!",
  [21472302] = "Making a drink yourself is actually quite the stress reliever. The yummy drink is just the cherry on top.",
  [21472303] = "I'm going to learn this drink and make it in front of my coworkers to wow them with my skills!",
  [21472304] = "A few more snacks, and you have a pretty set for your afternoon tea. Can't work hard on an empty stomach!",
  [21472401] = "Where did you find this amazingly simple yet delicious recipe? Even I managed to recreate it!",
  [21472402] = "I'm going to get my boyfriend to make it for me. Oh, wait... I don't have a boyfriend...",
  [21472403] = "Who's going to say no to a cup of delicious self-made beverage in between work? Time to say goodbye to Starbucks!",
  [21472404] = "The third one was the best! It's so good that I could feel my soul leaving my body!",
  [21473101] = "The scene was too chaotic to gain accurate information.",
  [21473201] = "Sometimes there are just people who want to be unreasonable.",
  [21473202] = "That's it? What happened in the end? Now I'm aching for an answer!",
  [21473203] = "The situation was a mess, and any follow-ups were met with difficulties.",
  [21473401] = "There must be a better way to deal with future incidents like this one.",
  [21473402] = "Those who do not abide by the rules should be punished. Kudos to the staff for maintaining order.",
  [21473403] = "It has become necessary to increase publicity efforts regarding prohibited items so that people are informed and understand the law for traveling safely.",
  [21474101] = "It's been so long since that happened, and now they want to fix things. I wonder why they didn't think of it sooner…",
  [21474102] = "With all due respect, the drill is in full swing. It's just still on the cusp. I think this time it won't last long either.",
  [21474103] = "I want to skip this program the moment I see it. Today I can't help wondering if it's really impossible to make anything both rewarding and entertaining.",
  [21474104] = "There have been several violent incidents this month. What is the point of doing this kind of drill? Can this world still be saved?",
  [21474201] = "Since when did this kind of program fill all TV channels? I've really had enough of it!",
  [21474202] = "Is this kind of anti-violence drill really going to make any difference? I think it's more of a comforter…",
  [21474203] = "It strikes me that the problem lies in the camerawork. The contents are tedious and slow-paced, and they make me feel drowsy…",
  [21474204] = "In these circumstances, I think what we need more is joy. This kind of program holds no appeal for us whatsoever.",
  [21474301] = "It's not too late to make amends. I hope this kind of terrible incident will never befall our society again!",
  [21474302] = "The procedures of the drill in the show are pretty scientific. I hope our company can take its cue from that.",
  [21474303] = "Right now, everybody's scared. It's about time someone spreads some positive energy. I hope things will get better for us soon!",
  [21474304] = "Our biggest enemy has always been our fear of the unknown. I'm sure we can get rid of our panic through learning and training.",
  [21474401] = "It surprises me that the drill's not as boring as I imagined. There were many interesting moments too. I highly recommend it!!",
  [21474402] = "Am I the only one who noticed there were many hot guys among the participants in the drill? They're so handsome! I can never see enough of such hotties!",
  [21474403] = "There's no harm in learning more about it. I'll participate in a drill like that as well when I get the chance!",
  [21474404] = "Watching the show, I learned a lot of things I didn't used to know. I hope nobody will have to use those things, but better safe than sorry!",
  [21475101] = "This specialist is so pretentious. They've been talking non-stop for so long but has provided no useful information whatsoever.",
  [21475102] = "If you spent 10 minutes familiarizing yourself with this show, then congratulations; you've wasted 10 minutes of your time.",
  [21475103] = "Did the show crew really know what they were doing? All they ever do is use publicity stunts to whet our appetites. Their show contains nothing useful at all!",
  [21475104] = "It's unlucky of me to see such a pretentious show in the dead of night! I clicked on it by mistake. Go away, bad luck!",
  [21475201] = "Am I the only one who feels that this show's been getting increasingly boring? I used to quite like it.",
  [21475202] = "When I saw the beginning, I thought it'd be pretty interesting, but unexpectedly, it got more absurd with every second. It's not worth watching.",
  [21475203] = "I advise you to shut your brain down before watching this, or you'll discover that the producers didn't use their brains when filming this show.",
  [21475204] = "At first, I thought the show was about science, but in the end, I discovered it was about mysticism. This so-called specialist is fit only to fool kids.",
  [21475301] = "Though some of the viewpoints strike me as a bit far-fetched, overall, the show is fairly interesting. It's worth watching.",
  [21475302] = "My friends asked me how I'd taken a liking to this kind of show lately. I didn't know what to say. Anyway, it's addictive!",
  [21475303] = "I don't know anything about your cases, but there's a reason I'm scared of traveling in an alley. I once saw a giant rat in an alley!",
  [21475304] = "Before watching the show, I was like, what's the point of studying this kind of stuff? It's meaningless! After watching the show, I was like, Awesome!",
  [21475401] = "I offer the show crew my unstinting praise. This is the best show I've seen lately. Absolutely the best!",
  [21475402] = "I can't stop watching this show for a single day! I can't even eat without watching it!",
  [21475403] = "That's so freaking true! Nothing scares me more than traveling alone in an alley! The mere thought of that raises goosebumps on my arms!",
  [21475404] = "I don't know if anybody feels the same, but every time I walk into an alley, I feel like something's staring at me…",
  [21476101] = "Aw, come on. You call this \"news?\" The neighboring channel reported this at least 2 hours ago!",
  [21476102] = "The show evaded many of the problems revealed by the gale. Do media practitioners have any professional ethics?",
  [21476103] = "Why have there been so many disasters this year? Will this kind of day ever end?",
  [21476104] = "It's all nonsense, without a shred of useful information. This is the only show that piggybacks on hot news and is full of bullshit!",
  [21476201] = "The show answered none of the questions we wanted to be answered. I wonder why they produced this show in the first place.",
  [21476202] = "Can you guys please pay more attention to the issue of providing shelter for stray animals? This city is their home as well!",
  [21476203] = "This is my first time seeing a report without even a photo of the scene. Are they expecting their viewers to imagine the details?",
  [21476204] = "Don't you think the host is too frivolous? I can't believe this. Has he no respect for the victims of the disaster?",
  [21476301] = "Schools and factories in our city have closed. Though it feels really good not to have to go to work, I still want things to return to normal ASAP.",
  [21476302] = "I've packed some stuff and had it delivered to the afflicted area. Hopefully, it'll come in handy for some of the citizens there!",
  [21476303] = "Journalists of the show crew who are on the front line, remember to put safety first, and thumbs-up to all crew members working in the field!",
  [21476304] = "Such high-quality news reports are something of a rarity now. It makes me feel like I'm in that area.",
  [21476401] = "Even I, who live in a neighboring area, feel how strong the wind is. Those of you who are in the center of the gale, stay safe!",
  [21476402] = "That journalist girl is so pretty, and she's always on the front lines of the afflicted area. What a beautiful and kind-hearted angel she is!",
  [21476403] = "I'm a grade school student, and I donated all my pocket money to the disaster zone. Hopefully, it'll help the people there drive away the gale monster and clear the stage!",
  [21476404] = "The gale is unfeeling, but people are not! The tougher the situation gets, the more heartwarming moments we'll see!",
  [21477101] = "They keep whetting my appetite with such little information. I've read the whole report, but I don't know more than I did before reading it. All this waiting's killing me!",
  [21477102] = "Isn't this deception? That company has long since made an announcement. The show crew can only fool domestic audiences with this.",
  [21477103] = "So this is what the press in Loveland City is like? These people are masters of exaggeration and will do anything to get attention…",
  [21477104] = "What a stupid show. That incident was ages ago. I can't believe they're still chattering about it…",
  [21477201] = "I don't dare believe a single word of any media. I'll just wait for the truth to be ascertained.",
  [21477202] = "Boycott their products! The scandal they're embroiled in is undeniable. I won't believe a single word of anybody who tries to defend them!",
  [21477203] = "There's no need to say anything. That was a crime, I think. The culprit should be arrested, period.",
  [21477204] = "The show crew is clearly taking advantage of it to get more exposure. The problem is that they're incurably incompetent. Shame on them!",
  [21477301] = "This matter has gone through several twists, and it's now becoming something like a suspense drama. I'll just stay quiet and wait to see how it'll turn out…",
  [21477302] = "I can't wait to see a certain company disgrace itself! I'll stay tuned for this incident, and I hope the show crew won't let me down!",
  [21477303] = "I missed the beginning and have been one step behind ever since. I'm totally confused by this scandalous thing. Can someone please tell me what happened?!",
  [21477304] = "I've been getting juicy stories all day long, and this one is definitely the juiciest of them all!",
  [21477401] = "I knew the show crew would gimme a juicy story as they always did! This time around, I'm taking the show crew's side. Keep digging deeper, guys!",
  [21477402] = "I wonder how the PR of the company will cope with this. Will this incident break up their monopoly?",
  [21477403] = "The specialist's words dissolved my confusion instantaneously! I would still be in the dark were it not for the specialist!",
  [21477404] = "Thanks to this show, I now got something to amaze my friends when chatting with them. For the first time ever, I'm keeping abreast of a current affair!",
  [21478101] = "If someone says the contest was not fixed, I'll be the first one to contradict them! I'll never accept this result!",
  [21478102] = "Is it really okay to preach this kind of values? It strikes me that they might lead domestic children astray.",
  [21478103] = "It strikes me that, at the end of the day, this competition is more about popularity than proficiency. Those fanatical supporters are changing the nature of this contest.",
  [21478104] = "Is it really okay to give them so much attention at such a young age? I'm not so sure about it.",
  [21478201] = "The champion didn't win on his own merits! I smashed my cellphone out of anger when I saw the result!",
  [21478202] = "To be fair, this contest does have some positive meaning, but not much.",
  [21478203] = "I heard the organizers failed to take good care of the contestants' health, and many of them were tired out in the last phase.",
  [21478204] = "Why are our compatriots performing so poorly? It's so maddening!",
  [21478301] = "Domestic universities are not attaching enough importance to the development of these abilities. I hope one day our teenagers will shine on these stages as well!",
  [21478302] = "I've been a computer geek since my childhood but never gained recognition from my parents. With this contest, I finally got something that could change their opinions.",
  [21478303] = "I don't understand any of the codes, but it doesn't make the contestants look any less awesome to me. The future of the world rests on these prodigies!",
  [21478304] = "Everybody sees the glory they get when receiving the prizes but can't see the hard work they've put into honing their skills. They're worthy of it all!",
  [21478401] = "At this moment, I offer my standing ovation to these outstanding teenagers! Technical prowess knows no national boundaries!",
  [21478402] = "Some of the contestants are so handsome! I'm having trouble concentrating on the event! But I love it!",
  [21478403] = "I never thought I, a geriatric, would become a fan of these teenagers. The outstanding never ceases to shine!",
  [21478404] = "These \"hackers\" are a bit different from what I imagined. They're not that unapproachable. Actually, they're kind of adorable. What's going on?",
  [21479101] = "The exhibit was held in haste, and the publicity was inadequate. Eventually, the event came to a perfunctory end with hardly any public attention.",
  [21479201] = "I didn't learn anything. It was a complete waste of time.",
  [21479202] = "This doesn't even count as entry-level. The event is totally pointless.",
  [21479203] = "A failed attempt, hardly worth discussing.",
  [21479401] = "Never thought maths could be so intriguing. I was fascinated.",
  [21479402] = "An exhibit worth seeing. Looking forward to the next one.",
  [21479403] = "The success of the exhibit sparked an animated discussion on the forum. It's been a long time since the last time so many people participated in the same discussion.",
  [21480101] = "It's so maddening! And there is some guy who is such an attention seeker!",
  [21480102] = "It's 100 times more boring than I imagined. May my eyes never be subjected to such lame shows again.",
  [21480103] = "What the heck is this? Each of these nuisances is more annoying than the last. What a bunch of eyesores!",
  [21480104] = "There's nothing intellectual about this show whatsoever. The guests' hunger for popularity is only too obvious.",
  [21480201] = "Is this another poor imitation of that foreign chat show? Would it kill them to think of something new?",
  [21480202] = "Having seen the original one, I can't watch this for a single second. It's kind of a lame parody.",
  [21480203] = "A chat show was never about one or two people's performances. It requires all participants to be expressive. I hope the producers can understand this.",
  [21480204] = "Imported shows are always met with localization issues. This one's no exception, as I expected.",
  [21480301] = "This kind of candid, international conversation is amazing! I love it!",
  [21480302] = "The guests in this season are all ass-kickers. The clashes between their viewpoints are awesome. Looking forward to season 2.",
  [21480303] = "Overall, its merits far outweigh its flaws. Though the editing is kind of problematic, which affects the viewing experience, the contents are superb.",
  [21480304] = "I've recommended this show to many of my friends lately. It's one of the best domestic shows.",
  [21480401] = "My goodness! It's finally airing! I hereby declare this is the only show I'll watch when eating!",
  [21480402] = "If you've never watched this show, do not walk away. I highly recommend it. It's drop-dead fantastic!",
  [21480403] = "This is my first time being so enthralled by a show. I binge-watched all episodes, and I'm still trying to pull myself out of fascination.",
  [21480404] = "I knew this show would be a hit. A good show lacks no audience, but I'll still recommend it to everybody!",
  [21481101] = "I once participated in a drill. The chain of command was a total mess, and an accident could happen at any moment.",
  [21481102] = "Frequent drills will affect people's normal lives. Participation in this kind of activity shouldn't be compulsory.",
  [21481103] = "Are there really people who like to attend such activities? A working day is tiring enough for me…",
  [21481104] = "Am I the only one who feels that this kind of gathering itself involves risks? Are they trying to reduce risks by creating new ones?",
  [21481201] = "If a drill eventually evolves into a real accident, that'd be the most ridiculous.",
  [21481202] = "Leaving aside the many procedures of the drill that were against the regulations, the non-normative approach of first-aid alone would mislead a lot of people.",
  [21481203] = "Is this form really necessary? It costs a lot of manpower and money and might not necessarily work. When a violent incident happens, people will still do what they've got to do.",
  [21481204] = "The mere mention of drills gives me a headache. Why do we have to drill so many times for something that we might not see happen in our whole lives?",
  [21481301] = "The more of this kind of drills, the better. Better safe than sorry. I'm sure this city will get better and better.",
  [21481302] = "Filming such a large event is no easy job. The show crew endured a lot.",
  [21481303] = "I can't believe there are so many unkind comments in the comments area. Medical drills are held for the sake of our safety, aren't they?",
  [21481304] = "I've only just participated in a fire drill, and I learned a lot. I hope there will be a medical drill in our community soon.",
  [21481401] = "You'll never realize the importance of such drills without experiencing an accident yourself. Let's go learn some first-aid skills!",
  [21481402] = "Those nurses are so professional and so dedicated. The medical staff are really… I'm feeling tearful…",
  [21481403] = "It doesn't hurt to learn some extra medical knowledge. I've put it into Favorites. I'll have my family watch it when they got the time.",
  [21481404] = "Be sure to learn some first-aid skills, guys! You must take it seriously! It might save your loved one's life at the crucial moment!",
  [21482101] = "This is the most boring show I've ever seen. I must be crazy to have watched a bunch of middle-aged men pounding their keyboards for so long.",
  [21482102] = "So all those rumors about bald programmers wearing checks are true. I can hardly distinguish them from each other…",
  [21482103] = "I was just trying to find a show to kill time. I didn't bargain on seeing this. Who's going to compensate me for my mental trauma…?",
  [21482104] = "When watching the preview, I thought it was some kind of thrilling teen anime, but after I tapped on it, I saw a typing contest. Does this count as fraud?",
  [21482201] = "Typing codes was never entertaining. This kind of gimmick won't get them what they want.",
  [21482202] = "A lot of shows similar to this one have emerged lately. It's like people from all walks of life are racing to get attention. What a farce!",
  [21482203] = "I thought the later sections of the contest had something exciting to offer, but it turned out this whole event was really purely about pounding keyboards! Does the director have a fetish for pounding the keyboard or something?",
  [21482204] = "This kind of stuff is getting popular now? It seems I've been lagging further and further behind the times…",
  [21482301] = "Seriously? You think I'm the kind of guy who's so frivolous as to watch people have a competition of typing codes? Well, sorry, I really am.",
  [21482302] = "All my friends have been watching it. I got an inkling it'll become the dark-horse show of the year.",
  [21482303] = "Them typing codes gives me Speed vibes. I find excitement building up in me when watching it!",
  [21482304] = "No.2 is really very likely to win. I'll bet all my savings on No.2. Don't screw with me on this!",
  [21482401] = "What an intoxicating show! I don't know why, but I can't stop watching it! Someone help me!",
  [21482402] = "Originally, I didn't want to watch this kind of program at all, but it's amazing! I'd say it's the best!",
  [21482403] = "Their typing speed is beyond human limits! It turns out that watching a typing competition is just as thrilling as watching a car race!",
  [21482404] = "It surprises me that there are people who can actually do that! After watching the show, I felt sublimed, and I realized how humble I was.",
  [21483101] = "Don't fall for it! Before going there, I thought it was some kind of high-end exhibit, but it turned out to be primitive. The photos were of awfully inferior quality. There's nothing worth seeing.",
  [21483102] = "I took my kids there to let them feel the vastness of the universe, but after we came back, they said there's nothing special about the universe.",
  [21483103] = "Those of you who bought tickets intending to feel the romance of the cosmos may drop the idea. It's an utter disappointment. The only upside is that the ticket is cheap, and I can throw it away without feeling upset.",
  [21483104] = "The organizers are so perfunctory. There were only a few decent photos, and it took me only 2 minutes to see them all. Worse still, the bottled water is as expensive as that in a scenic spot.",
  [21483201] = "After seeing the poster, I thought it'd be a great exhibit, but it's kind of disappointing. I wasted a whole morning.",
  [21483202] = "I took two buses, and I thought there was a sea of stars waiting for me at the destination, but it turned out to be a pile of wastepaper. Maybe this is what life is like.",
  [21483203] = "Tips: the promotional video has nothing to do with the actual exhibit. What you see with your own eyes might be different from it.",
  [21483204] = "The only thing I can remember after watching the exhibit is that the beef noodles at the entrance were pretty delicious.",
  [21483301] = "I've been interested in the universe since my childhood. The words \"the universe\" alone make this photo exhibit worth seeing.",
  [21483302] = "We shouldn't live in the present forever. Sometimes we need to fantasize about the cosmos.",
  [21483303] = "I finally understand why people keep using the word \"romantic\" to describe the universe. The starry sky is really so beautiful and so mysterious.",
  [21483304] = "As a shutterbug and a universe enthusiast, I find it doubly thrilling. Can't wait to see the exhibit!",
  [21483401] = "This whole Universe Photo Exhibit thing is drop-dead romantic. Both the scenes and the designs are my favorites. Highly recommend it!",
  [21483402] = "Only by looking up into the universe can we perceive how humble we are. It turns out we're no different from a bunch of frogs gazing at a patch of the sky from the bottom of a well.",
  [21483403] = "I never knew watching a photo exhibit could be so thrilling. It has a kind of breathtaking beauty.",
  [21483404] = "I plan to go and watch it with my friends this weekend. Really looking forward to it. Hoping to discover more mysteries in this mirror!",
  [21484101] = "I thought diaries were part of people's privacy. Though their owners couldn't be found, is it really okay for the show crew to release them without permission like this?",
  [21484102] = "If I were among the owners of the diaries, I'd be pissed off. The show crew is despicable!",
  [21484103] = "I wonder how the owners of the diaries would feel if they happened to be watching this show. They'd definitely feel terribly embarrassed…",
  [21484104] = "Some secrets should stay buried forever. Divulging other people's secrets to get attention will beget divine retribution.",
  [21484201] = "I don't want to pry into other people's personal lives. I'm not going to watch the show.",
  [21484202] = "Privacy issue aside, I'm not even sure if those diaries are real or not. I mean, those people will forge anything for clicks.",
  [21484203] = "If I find out who came up with this \"good\" idea, I'll be the first one to suggest releasing their diaries.",
  [21484204] = "Nowadays, media companies will do anything for clicks. They're so disgusting.",
  [21484301] = "Apart from anything else, the show itself is pretty touching. It's worth watching!",
  [21484302] = "Actually, there's no need to take this matter so seriously. Releasing the diaries is the quickest way to find their owners.",
  [21484303] = "There are some stories that have stayed buried for a long time but shouldn't be forgotten. They deserve to be seen!",
  [21484304] = "Some of the stories are so moving. If they're real, I'd hope they're not; if they're not real, I'd hope they are.",
  [21484401] = "I'm crying!! Some of the stories are so touching. They're like a narrative poem dating back to that era!",
  [21484402] = "A pretty good show. It acquainted us with the life and love of the olden days, tugging at our heartstrings with stories transcending time.",
  [21484403] = "My whole family was reduced to tears, especially my granny. Maybe those who lived through those days are best able to empathize with the stories.",
  [21484404] = "In those days when resources were scarce, people could find happiness and contentment so easily. But now, what is going on with us?",
  [21485101] = "These people are so boring. What's the point of looking forward to the future when we have so many unsolved problems at hand?",
  [21485102] = "Stuff like the future of humanity is way beyond the pay grade of ordinary people like me. Making ends meet is hard enough for us.",
  [21485103] = "I can't understand a single word of theirs. They're so pretentious!",
  [21485104] = "Could any ancient people have thought of what the 21st century would be like? Likewise,  thinking about the future will serve only to add to our vexations.",
  [21485201] = "I thought they'd discuss something interesting, but they didn't. I'm very disappointed.",
  [21485202] = "Not interested in such unrealistic stuff. What does the future of humanity have to do with pathetic wage earners like me?",
  [21485203] = "I don't like those people in the footage. They all look so condescending. They seem to like to use the word \"mankind,\" but actually they have no love for anybody.",
  [21485204] = "There are really people who care about the future of humanity? Well, actually, I'd really like to see the end of the world and human civilization.",
  [21485301] = "It strikes me that there are many other things worth discussing. The show seems to have been censored. It doesn't contain that many sensitive subjects.",
  [21485302] = "I'm glad to see that the hazards in our society were really brought up at the conference. Freedom of speech is the beginning of improvement.",
  [21485303] = "Those who do not plan for the future will find trouble at their doorstep. We can move forward without having to worry about anything, only because some people have worried for us.",
  [21485304] = "I thought the conference would be full of nonsense, but many of the questions turned out to be quite thought-provoking. I apologize for my previous prejudices.",
  [21485401] = "Thank goodness! They're finally relaying the \"Future Conference.\" How I wish I could go there and participate in the discussion!",
  [21485402] = "Those bigwigs do have a different air. They seldom make public appearances. Seeing them on TV makes it all worthwhile!",
  [21485403] = "I'm very hopeful about the future of humankind! There's no difficulty we cannot overcome with our collective efforts!",
  [21485404] = "Whoa! There's really a show crew broadcasting the conference? What a surprise!",
  [21486101] = "I stayed up late waiting for it, but I'm very disappointed. It's not as spectacular as I imagined. There are just a few meteors. It's like Buyer's Show vs. Seller's Show!",
  [21486102] = "What's the point of this photo exhibit? All the photos look so similar and dazzle me.",
  [21486103] = "Is it really possible to see a meteor shower amid the light pollution of the city? I doubt anybody can see a single meteor.",
  [21486104] = "Wage earners like me who have to work long hours are not worthy of such romance because we have to get up early for work tomorrow.",
  [21486201] = "Life has killed my dreams and aspirations. I've stopped caring about poems, future, and meteor showers. All I can think about is how to get by.",
  [21486202] = "Can someone please tell the meteor shower to wait a few days and come at the weekend? My work doesn't allow me to stay up late on a working day!",
  [21486203] = "Are there really so many people who are interested in the meteor shower? I think most of them are just copycats.",
  [21486204] = "Nobody but kids would believe that wishes made when holding hands are certain to come true. The fact is that most of those who went hand in hand with each other ended up breaking up.",
  [21486301] = "To see the meteor shower, I caught up on my sleep beforehand during the day. I got everything ready only to find that I misremembered the date!",
  [21486302] = "I advise everybody not to see the meteor shower, because that'll make me the only beholder of it. Being mischievous makes me happy!",
  [21486303] = "Maybe the meteor shower cannot grant our wishes, but it'll give us an unforgettable night.",
  [21486304] = "The entries in the photo contest are all so beautiful. It strikes me that there's no need to see an actual meteor shower, 'cause seeing the photos is enough.",
  [21486401] = "This is the nicest gift for us from the universe this year! Best wishes to everybody who saw the meteor shower!",
  [21486402] = "Still remember the TV dramas we saw in our childhood? Now the time has finally come for us to see a meteor shower. What are you waiting for?",
  [21486403] = "It's been a long time since I last set an alarm to get up on time for a meteor shower. I feel like I've traveled back in time to those heady days of youth.",
  [21486404] = "It was under the meteor shower a few years ago that I met my current boyfriend. Is it acceptable to say this stuff? Anyway, I wanna share this niceness with you guys.",
  [21487101] = "What a lame event. The place was packed with people jostling each other, and I didn't see anything. I swear, I'll never participate in this kind of activity again!",
  [21487102] = "The organizers of the event are a bunch of knuckleheads. They know nothing about organizing activities. It was a very unpleasant experience!",
  [21487103] = "What's the point of playing a movie here? The aurora itself is beautiful enough. Anything man-made is blasphemy to nature.",
  [21487104] = "Frankly, aurora is so rare. I just wanna quietly wait for the aurora to appear. I'm totally uninterested in this kind of rowdy activity.",
  [21487201] = "The organizers hyped up this event as such a big deal only because they wanted to make money. They ruined such a rare aurora.",
  [21487202] = "I'd rather enjoy the pure beauty of the aurora in a quiet spot with my family than participate in any lame event.",
  [21487203] = "This is unbelievable. I should never have come to this stupid movie party. It's so crowded, and the prices of drinks are insanely high!",
  [21487204] = "The many wacky activities only strike me as noisy. I don't even care about the aurora anymore.",
  [21487301] = "Beautiful astronomical phenomena are gifts for mankind from Providence, who wants to see smiles on our faces.",
  [21487302] = "This is a perfect combination of a natural wonder and modern sci-tech. In my eyes, this is what real beauty is like. It transcends the limits of nature and humanity.",
  [21487303] = "I really don't regret having participated in this aurora-night movie party. It's a once-in-a-lifetime spectacular sight.",
  [21487304] = "As a shutterbug, I had such a fruitful night! This day has offered me so many pleasant surprises! Everybody's welcome to go to my home page to see my work!",
  [21487401] = "It's more stunning than I imagined! Its beauty is beyond description! Whoever came up with this idea is absolutely a genius!",
  [21487402] = "What a breathtaking view! I signed up only because I got nothing better to do. Never thought I'd get to see such a beautiful view. It makes this lifetime of mine worthwhile!",
  [21487403] = "I believe this is a night nobody wants to miss out on. It was the most unforgettable thing I've experienced in my life. I was so excited and couldn't get to sleep for a long time.",
  [21487404] = "The view was beautiful, but it was the person I enjoyed the view with that sent my heart aflutter. Will the wish I secretly made under the aurora come true?",
  [21488101] = "With such poor singing skills, you actually had the nerve to go onto the stage. The AI machine is doing almost all the singing for you. Do you dare turn your microphone full on?",
  [21488102] = "What a boring show… It's wasting my time, time that I can put to much better use.",
  [21488103] = "What confuses me the most is why they invited a bunch of pop stars to cheer up people in the afflicted areas. I mean, does any of them know anything about ordinary people's misery?",
  [21488104] = "I'll never support idols embroiled in scandals. We want to see artists who are role models in terms of both artistic prowess and moral integrity!",
  [21488201] = "Am I the only one finding it embarrassing? They're trying so hard to make it sappy, showing a total disregard for the victims' feelings.",
  [21488202] = "It strikes me as nothing but another publicity stunt. Some people got the clicks and good reviews they wanted, but those who were really in need of help got nothing.",
  [21488203] = "What a lame show. Each performance is worse than the last. I can't stand it anymore!",
  [21488204] = "If you wanna see some pretty faces, you won't be disappointed, but if you wanna hear some decent music, I'd advise you to skip this show. It's virtually torture to my ears!",
  [21488301] = "Can we have some more public-good concerts like this? People in the afflicted areas could use our aid and support!!",
  [21488302] = "The concert itself is pretty enjoyable. If this concert can also get people in the afflicted areas some help, it'll be the frosting on the cake.",
  [21488303] = "Whatever the purpose of it is, this concert does have some positive influence on the situation. There can be nothing wrong with fighting for a good cause.",
  [21488304] = "Why didn't those haters contribute something? Chances are that they'll never be able to donate that much money in their whole life, will they?",
  [21488401] = "What an amazing show!! Never thought they'd be able to bring so many of my favorite singers on board. This is so exciting!",
  [21488402] = "My idol is not only beautiful but also philanthropic. She staged the show at her own expense and made such a big donation. Now her haters have to shut their mouths, I presume?",
  [21488403] = "It's really the fantastic line-up I've dreamed of! Never thought they'd be able to get so many superstars on board. Everybody's here for philanthropic work!",
  [21488404] = "I failed to get a ticket and can only watch the live broadcast at home! Such a star-studded concert might really be a once-in-a-lifetime occurrence!",
  [21489101] = "If you want a nightless day, why don't you just go to the North Pole when there's midnight sun? I don't see the point of discussing this question.",
  [21489102] = "May I say there's not a single witty remark in the street interview? People are getting so unimaginative these days.",
  [21489103] = "If it's all daytime, would I have to work around the clock? If it's all nighttime, would I get to rest all year round? If neither is the case, what difference does that make?",
  [21489104] = "The show crew ran out of topics? And they actually bought a spot on the trending topic list. Have they no shame?",
  [21489201] = "I can't be bothered by thinking about that question. There are 24-hour cities everywhere. What's the difference between day and night?",
  [21489202] = "If day and night stopped alternating in non-polar areas, wouldn't that mean the earth had stopped revolving? Are you sure this is not a disaster movie?",
  [21489203] = "I can't think of any difference except lower electric bills. Are there really people willing to discuss this topic?",
  [21489204] = "If it lasts only a day or two, everybody would have their own opinions; if it's permanent, nothing would change.",
  [21489301] = "In that case, the efficiency of generating solar power would probably double. (Lol. That's the only benefit I can think of.)",
  [21489302] = "On the bright side, at least the crime rate would be lower, considering it's broad daylight all the time.",
  [21489303] = "If a day like that really came, I'd probably stay awake to bear witness to every hour of it.",
  [21489304] = "If that happened, would I get to let my kid stay in the nursery school twenty-four seven? Ha ha, just a joke.",
  [21489401] = "Ha ha… One of the guys interviewed on the street was hilarious. I laughed so hard I spat out my food!",
  [21489402] = "Every time I watch a street interview, I see something unexpected. People's wild imaginations can be so intriguing.",
  [21489403] = "Am I the only one wanting eternal night? I love nights so much, 'cause I have so little time for myself!",
  [21489404] = "I can't pull myself out of the comments area. It's packed with comic geniuses. My stomach is throbbing from laughing!",
  [21490101] = "Will anyone actually believe ads? I mean, have there not been enough victims of false advertising and exaggerated commercials?",
  [21490102] = "To be honest, at the thought that those businesses' advertising expenses are eventually paid by consumers, I find it hard not to hate ads.",
  [21490103] = "Either the ad leaflets plastered all over the utility poles, or the earworm mid-roll ads in every TV drama—all ads are skanky!",
  [21490104] = "There's nothing I hate more than the incessant ads on video sites. The most unbelievable part is that the ads wouldn't go away even after I bought a membership!",
  [21490201] = "I suddenly recalled an ancient joke: No mid-roll TV drama in the commercials. Sadly, the ubiquity of ads seems to have been universally accepted.",
  [21490202] = "All kinds of hard ads and soft ads, and the hype on live-streaming channels—is advertising offering us more choices, or making choices for us?",
  [21490203] = "When I was little, I would watch ads with relish, but now, I want to skip the ads but can't...",
  [21490204] = "A sentence just popped into my mind: \"I made that decision against my ancestor's will after all...\"",
  [21490301] = "The show's pretty good. I relived my childhood and learned some knowledge too. But did I misremember, or this show had some mid-roll ads as well?",
  [21490302] = "There's no telling what ads will become like in the future—more acceptable, probably.",
  [21490303] = "Since we can't stop ads from being everywhere in our lives, I'd like to ask you guys to make ads less annoying!",
  [21490304] = "They're not called ads anymore. They're 'product recommendations'. Actually, they're not that bad. Good stuff deserves to be seen.",
  [21490401] = "I was actually kind of moved when I finished watching it. Every one of those advertising slogans is linked to the next. They're overlaid with memories of our past!",
  [21490402] = "I don't know if it's because of the childhood filter or something, but the ad I used to hate strikes me as quite interesting now!",
  [21490403] = "If I'm to name the most impressive ad, it'll surely be Brain of Gold. Put your hands up if you agree with me!",
  [21490404] = "The Binge Boy ad series is the biggest earworm! Put on a spurt, brethren! Beat the upstairs guy's Brain of Gold!",
  [21491101] = "I don't think the reconstruction plan's gonna work. It's been beset with problems from the start. Got the sense it's gonna fall through halfway.",
  [21491102] = "Will someone please do something about those making a mountain out of a molehill and wreaking havoc under the guise of City Observer?",
  [21491103] = "Isn't this a privilege? I don't think it's wise to grant additional powers to regular people.",
  [21491104] = "It strikes me that this will add to the confusion. Is it reasonable to let a group of nonspecialists judge the specialists?",
  [21491201] = "I don't know much about the matter, so I won't comment on it, but I got the sense that they haven't been making much progress in the reconstruction plan...",
  [21491202] = "Well, how will the City Observers supervise it? Unless they make this fair and transparent, the whole thing will be pointless.",
  [21491203] = "I can't bring myself to trust these new statements, and lately there seems to have been more negative news than positive news.",
  [21491204] = "We only see what the press wants us to see. You know what they say—you'll lose if you take it seriously...",
  [21491301] = "Though there are still many unsolved problems, I have great faith in the future of Loveland City. Hopefully this campaign will infuse new vigor into it.",
  [21491302] = "What a socially responsible show. It's really focusing on our biggest concerns. I hope it'll stay this way.",
  [21491303] = "Everybody is the best City Observer. If everyone contributes a little, Loveland City will surely become a better place.",
  [21491304] = "An ordinary Loveland citizen as I am, I'm ready to do my part for our city whenever it needs me to!",
  [21491401] = "Go for it, City Observers! Make Loveland City a better place!",
  [21491402] = "I've been following the reconstruction plan all along. Lately, things have really seemed to take a turn for the better. Looking forward to the completion of the plan!",
  [21491403] = "I'll stay tuned to the show for more info. The reconstruction plan is inextricably linked to the fate of Loveland City. Every one of us should fight for it.",
  [21491404] = "Not until now did I really perceive the power of the unity and cohesion of Loveland City. I wish our city a better future!",
  [21492101] = "I can tell at a glance that it's all hype. I've seen too much of it. These days, there's nothing businesspeople wouldn't stoop to for publicity.",
  [21492102] = "Lately, there have been several businesses shooting to fame this way, which strikes me as kind of shady...",
  [21492103] = "I went to that restaurant once. It was seedy, and the waiter was mean. I'll never go there again, not even if I'm paid to.",
  [21492104] = "The owner doesn't look like a good guy. My bet is there will be a novel plot twist.",
  [21492201] = "I can't shake the feeling that this kind of hype and exposure is not a good thing for an eatery. Such publicity will only victimize it.",
  [21492202] = "I think the interviewer of the show was rude to the eatery owner. The questions were too sharp. The owner was inundated.",
  [21492203] = "People tend to forget the line in the sand after getting famous. No matter what that man is like now, the real trial has yet to come.",
  [21492204] = "I'm kind of scared to be touched now. I was once deeply moved by a story, but the next day, the main character of the story became a streamer and started pitching goods.",
  [21492301] = "In a time like this when almost everybody's after money, it's really admirable of the restaurant owner to selflessly offer help to strangers.",
  [21492302] = "I've been to that restaurant. The food wasn't amazing, but it tasted like home, and the servings were really generous!",
  [21492303] = "No matter what, this kind of behavior is undeniably commendable. It is kind-hearted people like him who are worthy of publicity and fame!",
  [21492304] = "I heard that before we learned of this, the eatery owner had been doing philanthropic work for many years. I believe he's really a kind guy, and this is not a publicity stunt.",
  [21492401] = "Heartwarming deeds will never fail to touch me! The eatery owner's moving actions reduced me to tears several times today!",
  [21492402] = "Boohoo... He's so... I'm crying my eyes out! Will he really be able to make any money if he keeps offering people free lunches in a spot like that?",
  [21492403] = "If the occasion arises, I'll offer help to people who need it as well, warming their hearts a little bit.",
  [21492404] = "I once had a free lunch at that restaurant when I was at the end of my rope. Now I'd like to spread this kindness to more people.",
  [21493101] = "The Special Task Force is becoming something like a boy group. Can we really trust a team that uses their faces to drum up publicity to protect us?",
  [21493102] = "To be honest, I'm not impressed. Is the press exaggerating? I mean, shouldn't we have higher standards for the Special Task Force?",
  [21493103] = "They've been staging more shows by the day, but there have been a lot of people they failed to rescue in actual crises, haven't there?",
  [21493104] = "The Special Task Force is becoming increasingly disappointing. Their special training on the sea island ruined their attractive looks completely. Look how swarthy they are now.",
  [21493201] = "I'm very displeased with the show. The time they spent organizing this useless lecture would've been put to much better use if they gave the Special Task Force more screen time...",
  [21493202] = "I got the sense that the Special Task Force members are a lot hotter than the cameraperson presented them. Let me do the filming! I'm an excellent retoucher!",
  [21493203] = "The filming is such a mess. The camera keeps wobbling. I can't even see the hot guys' faces clearly...",
  [21493204] = "These experts are unbelievably garrulous. They're talking me into sleep, and none of their words are actionable.",
  [21493301] = "I'm grateful to the Special Task Force for their contributions to Loveland City. To protect us, these unsung heroes have been making sacrifices all along.",
  [21493302] = "Anybody who doesn't love competent and handsome guys? I love them!",
  [21493303] = "If only I could go to the venue to see it. Watching it on the screen makes me feel that something's missing...",
  [21493304] = "The captain, my favorite, shows up too little in the footage! The cameraperson's so partial! Don't make a habit of it!",
  [21493401] = "Does any of the Special Task Force members need a girlfriend? I'll recommend myself on a daily basis, just in case.",
  [21493402] = "AAAAARGH! Yet another day's craze for the Special Task Force! This show is virtually a treat for female fans of the Special Task Force. Licked the screen 10,000 times!",
  [21493403] = "I waited hours in front of my phone to see the live broadcast, and I wasn't disappointed. I saw everything I wanted to see! Ha ha ha...",
  [21493404] = "Please make more such shows! These team members represent positive energy. All of them are the most loveable!",
  [21494101] = "Did the Special Task Force really respond immediately? Why do I feel they showed up late every time?",
  [21494102] = "Will these unscrupulous media people stop burying the lead every time? How heavy are the losses? We want to know the truth.",
  [21494103] = "You call this first-hand information? What a joke. Other media have reported this some time ago. You people are so lame.",
  [21494104] = "There's nothing useful in this report. We've known these things for quite some time, haven't we?",
  [21494201] = "The wounded had to answer the reporter's questions after suffering such a severe injury. Poor wretches...",
  [21494202] = "I can't imagine this is a news report from a professional media company. We want the truth!",
  [21494203] = "It's not that I wanna spread conspiracy theories, but the casualty numbers they released are sure as hell underestimated. Looking forward to seeing them discredited.",
  [21494204] = "Why have there been so many natural disasters and human-induced calamities lately? Were they really punishments for mankind from nature?",
  [21494301] = "They've got to ascertain the cause of the fire and make those responsible pay for it!",
  [21494302] = "The Special Task Force showed up like messiahs once again. We can always trust them to have our backs!",
  [21494303] = "Why did the factory suddenly catch fire? Was it human-induced or caused by some kind of mechanical malfunction? I'll wait for an official statement.",
  [21494304] = "The fire must've taken so many lives... I hope there's no fire in heaven.",
  [21494401] = "The Special Task Force are my superheroes! I can't imagine how despairing the fire victims would've felt had the Special Task Force not responded in time!",
  [21494402] = "I've donated some daily necessities and clothing to the fire victims in the hope of tiding them over...",
  [21494403] = "My goodness! I heard the news right after I woke up. I hope they can minimize the casualties!",
  [21494404] = "I can tell from the mere footage how fierce the fire was. That correspondent girl was so brave. Thumbs-up to the crew of the show!",
  [21495101] = "Am I the only one who finds it lame? Novelty does not mean nonsense, and remake does not mean fabrication. This is a downright violation of traditional arts!",
  [21495102] = "Forgive me for my ignorance of arts. I had no clue what they were doing on the stage. I slept through the whole performance...",
  [21495103] = "I really regretted buying a ticket to see it. It was hyped up as a masterpiece, but actually, it wasn't worth the cost of the ticket at all!",
  [21495104] = "I think all these good reviews are from hired trolls. Those actors' make-up was terrible. I didn't have a clue what they were doing up there.",
  [21495201] = "This whole thing's a disaster for the arts industry, an unprecedented retrogression. For the sake of the actors, I'll give it a 1-star rating.",
  [21495202] = "I think it's fine. Actually, if the hype hadn't gotten my hopes up, I would've found it acceptable.",
  [21495203] = "I suspect many people are either pretending to know what they don't know, or parroting other people's remarks. Bad stuff can never become good, okay?",
  [21495204] = "I don't know if you guys like it or not, but I know I don't...",
  [21495301] = "The dancing's beautiful, and the storyline's touching. There seems to be nothing wrong with it, but I feel something's missing.",
  [21495302] = "It's one of the best stage plays I've seen in recent years. I'll watch it again if I get the chance.",
  [21495303] = "I've got to say the producer did an amazing job selecting these dancers. Every one of the characters was so dynamic!",
  [21495304] = "The actors did well enough, okay? If you think they didn't, maybe you should go onto the stage and impress us!",
  [21495401] = "Forgive me for my inability to find any ornate words to describe this performance. After watching it, I could think of only one word: beautiful!",
  [21495402] = "Such arts are too beautiful to exist in the mortal realm! Watching the play made me feel like I was sublimed!",
  [21495403] = "Thought it'd be just average. Never crossed my mind it'd be so good. It's really a must-see. I highly recommend it!",
  [21495404] = "AAAARGH! I was never a big fan of modern dance, but after watching this show, I took an immediate liking to it! Everybody should go see it right now!",
  [21496101] = "What kind of news report is this? None of it makes any sense. I suggest the producer of the show switch careers.",
  [21496102] = "What a lame news report. The camera was too far away from the scene. I can't see a thing in the photos!",
  [21496103] = "I really hate those street racers. They disturb people's lives and might even take lives! How could the likes of them be let onto the expressway?",
  [21496104] = "If I were those youngsters' parent, I would sure as hell teach them a hard lesson for misbehaving like that at such a young age!",
  [21496201] = "I can't believe they're putting such trivial stuff in the news these days. I mean, it's kind of just a civil dispute.",
  [21496202] = "Those street racers did not so much as apologize for disturbing other people's lives. Are they really above the law?",
  [21496203] = "So how was the issue settled exactly? I'm totally confused...",
  [21496204] = "I've seen this in another news report already. Is there no new revelation?",
  [21496301] = "Those cocky street racers chickened out instantly at the sight of the policemen. To be honest, it's hilarious, ha ha ha...",
  [21496302] = "Though it's wrong to cause disturbances, afterward they left as they were told, so they kind of mended their ways.",
  [21496303] = "Those rowdy nuisances finally left. Hopefully, the nearby residents will have a good night's sleep.",
  [21496304] = "If those hooligans kept me from sleep, I would've gone ballistic as well! Calling the police was too lenient for them!",
  [21496401] = "Those street racers are just teenagers. They could use some lessons.",
  [21496402] = "Calling the police is the most reliable solution. The sight of the police cars scared those kids witless...",
  [21496403] = "Am I the only one to notice one of the racers was wearing a yellow-chicken helmet? OMG, it's drop-dead adorable!",
  [21496404] = "Watching those street racers being lectured with their heads down, I couldn't help but give a gloating smile. Am I incorrigible?",
  [21497101] = "This is literally the most embarrassing chat show I've ever seen. It gave me goosebumps the size of beans.",
  [21497102] = "Will the host please stop judging other people's hobbies like that? It's just rude!",
  [21497103] = "Thanks to this show, my boring weekend just became even more boring...",
  [21497104] = "I can't understand why these people are so obsessed with some stars they'll never get to reach, wasting so much time and energy.",
  [21497201] = "I don't usually make comments on people's hobbies, but I really don't see the point in making a show like this.",
  [21497202] = "Is this seriously a chat show? Their remarks are totally irrelevant, and their topics are unrelated.",
  [21497203] = "It strikes me that these people are not in their right minds. Is it possible they've stared at the stars for too long and forgotten they're still on earth?",
  [21497204] = "I barely managed to watch half of it. I wonder how they made an interesting topic so boring.",
  [21497301] = "It's so nice to have enthusiasm for something. I envy these star chasers.",
  [21497302] = "I didn't know different people liked different stars. It's so interesting. I'll learn more about the stories of the stars if I get the chance.",
  [21497303] = "The thought that these stars are actually gigantic faraway planets makes me feel small.",
  [21497304] = "There are so many stars in the universe, and our planet Earth is just one of them. Life is itself a miracle, I have to say.",
  [21497401] = "May I say my favorite star is Uranus? The Planet of Lazy People. It revolves when lying. Well, I'll go and lie down as well.",
  [21497402] = "Gazing into the starry sky really helps you forget your troubles! All the stars in the sky are my friends!",
  [21497403] = "There are so many stars up there. How can anybody love only one of them? Only kids make choices. I want them all!",
  [21497404] = "I took a liking to them when I got my first book on astronomy in my childhood. My favorite star is the shiniest one, the morning star, of course.",
  [21498101] = "Isn't this a bit overdramatic? I mean, they're just conjuring tricks, not real magic.",
  [21498102] = "I can tell at a glance those called onto the stage for interaction were shills. Audience members like us are the only victims of their deception.",
  [21498103] = "Be rational, guys! All conjuring tricks are false, false, false! Important stuff needs to be repeated thrice!",
  [21498104] = "The stage lights made it look mysterious, but the performance was actually nondescript.",
  [21498201] = "I don't see anything impressive about it. Maybe it'd look better if seen live.",
  [21498202] = "The cloak-and-dagger stuff's needless, and all his moves were predictable. It's kind of boring.",
  [21498203] = "To be honest, I kind of regretted having watched it live. It's no different from watching the broadcast, and I had to buy a ticket.",
  [21498204] = "Ha ha ha... The filmed audience members' facial expressions were way too overdramatic. I can tell at a glance they're faking it.",
  [21498301] = "I always believed stuff like hypnosis was kind of deceptive, but after watching the show, I'm not that sure anymore.",
  [21498302] = "The details of the show were full of pleasant surprises. Maybe this is what professionalism of international standard is like!",
  [21498303] = "There are actually people who don't know how famous this master is overseas? Those who call him a charlatan can shut their mouths.",
  [21498304] = "The recent marketing hype is indeed a bit too much, but it's undeniable that the show's a good one.",
  [21498401] = "It's virtually a visual feast!! An indescribably mind-boggling one!!",
  [21498402] = "You've got to watch it live if you can! Of course, getting a ticket is no easy job now...",
  [21498403] = "How come the tickets sold out instantly? I hate scalpers! Boohoo... I want so bad to see the show live!",
  [21498404] = "I took my whole family to see it. It's a show I'll never regret having seen! It's well worth the cost of the ticket!",
  [21499101] = "Multiple participants got injured or lost due to problematic security work. The campaign descended into chaos.",
  [21499201] = "Are they sure an awareness campaign like this is not having the opposite effects?",
  [21499202] = "The forest seems a bit creepy...",
  [21499203] = "A campaign beset by accidents. Maybe the comedy channel would prove more interesting.",
  [21499401] = "The citizens' awareness of forest protection is heightened, and we'll be able to do our job better.",
  [21499402] = "The forest provides oxygen for us. We must keep it out of harm's way.",
  [21499403] = "We'll broadcast the whole campaign live. Stay tuned.",
  [21500101] = "An unscrupulous contest judged by bribed referees. I'll bet the champion's been decided already!",
  [21500102] = "Do they think the audience is stupid? I've seen several goofs so far!",
  [21500103] = "The crew of the show has got to stop being so partial! They took our contestant away. We're done with this stupid competition!",
  [21500104] = "I don't see anything interesting about it, and the recent hype's quite annoying too...",
  [21500201] = "It's a good thing for the contest to be a bit suspenseful, but editing it to whet the viewers' appetites is a bit too much, isn't it?",
  [21500202] = "I can tell from the distribution of screen time who the show's trying to make popular. It's not worth watching anymore.",
  [21500203] = "If they can't level the playing field, then they shouldn't have held this contest in the first place.",
  [21500204] = "Some of the contestants' faces were so recognizable that even I recognized them, but the staff members pretended not to see them!",
  [21500301] = "I love this kind of nervous excitement. The contest is thrilling and electrifying!",
  [21500302] = "I'd very much like to see what the contestants are like after the game. Will the show please release more sidelights?",
  [21500303] = "The contest was pretty enjoyable, but the mid-roll ads that ran at crucial junctures were really annoying.",
  [21500304] = "I've been watching this contest with my friends lately. I'll keep following it until the results are out!",
  [21500401] = "I will not have anybody miss this fantastic show! I'll recommend it to everybody in the world!",
  [21500402] = "I haven't been so fascinated by a contest for a long time. This show's really addictive!",
  [21500403] = "Only earlier today, my 3-year-old daughter asked me how long till Super Disguiser aired.",
  [21500404] = "I was on bad terms with my roommate, but then I discovered he was a fan of Super Disguiser as well, and now we're besties.",
  [21501101] = "Is it really okay to entrust such a task to amateurs? Who will accept responsibility if the cultural artifact gets damaged?",
  [21501102] = "I'd never dare do something like that, 'cause if the artifact got damaged, I'd never be able to get enough money to compensate them...",
  [21501103] = "Using culture and history as a publicity stunt... There really is no depth show producers wouldn't stoop to these days.",
  [21501104] = "I wanna say this whole thing's a big lie. The thing the tourists tried to restore was no cultural artifact, 'cause they'll never let you touch a real cultural artifact.",
  [21501201] = "It's a well-intentioned activity, but due to the organizers' unprofessionalism, the scene became as disorderly as a vegetable market.",
  [21501202] = "Some of the participants are maddeningly clumsy. Will they please stop letting such people touch cultural artifacts?",
  [21501203] = "\"Touch history?\" These days, you can hardly find anybody who has a grasp of history. They're seriously expecting these people to feel history and culture from cultural artifacts?",
  [21501204] = "I'm strongly against such actions. Wherever there's a crowd, things can easily get out of control.",
  [21501301] = "I got a suggestion to make. It'll be better if they offer a commentary about the cultural artifact being restored.",
  [21501302] = "I'd very much like to take my kids there to help them understand the preciousness of cultural artifacts and learn some historical knowledge.",
  [21501303] = "I had the good fortune to see it live. It was an invaluable experience.",
  [21501304] = "There were professionals offering guidance on the scene, so I think it's legit. I'll try it myself if I get the chance.",
  [21501401] = "How nice it must've felt to restore a cultural artifact with their own hands! I'm green with envy...",
  [21501402] = "Those cultural artifacts look precious. Watching people restore them makes me relapse into my old habit of feeling nervous for people...",
  [21501403] = "A friendly reminder for everybody who's watching this video: you're able to breathe freely!",
  [21501404] = "Finally, they're holding an exhibition related to historical artifacts. I'll make sure to go see it in a few days!",
  [21502101] = "The stories on the ranking list are either campy or full of motivational quotes. Were they really selected through a vote?",
  [21502102] = "I can tell at a glance that some of those people's stories are fake. They didn't even bother to adjust the cliché plots, and their stories actually made the list. The vote was sure as hell fixed.",
  [21502103] = "This show is getting increasingly disappointing. I can tell from the theme it's not worth watching...",
  [21502104] = "The person I hate the most depicted me as a villain in their contribution, and it actually got accepted. I'm so gonna give it a bad review!",
  [21502201] = "These people are masters of fabrication. You'll lose if you take it seriously.",
  [21502202] = "Did the editor even read the contributions? I actually saw two stories with almost identical plots!",
  [21502203] = "I've stopped expecting to see factual recounts, but will these people please make their fabrications a bit more interesting? They bored the hell out of me!",
  [21502204] = "Is this a lame story competition or something? 'Cause each of these stories is lamer than the last...",
  [21502301] = "Life brooks no 'if'. Some missed things stay in the past forever, and your only option is to move on.",
  [21502302] = "I wanted to share my story but didn't know where to start. Eventually, I had no choice but to subdue my mixed emotions.",
  [21502303] = "I hope that someday, when I'm old, I'll get to light a cigarette and tell stories of the past to my offspring as well.",
  [21502304] = "Now that I think about it, I got quite a past too. I have stories. Do you have wine?",
  [21502401] = "The story at the top of the list literally reduced me to tears. I saw myself in her...",
  [21502402] = "I'm a highborn lady hated by my parents, ostracized by my brothers, and abandoned by my fiancé all because of an impostor. Follow my account and stay tuned for my plan of vengeance!",
  [21502403] = "We got so many amazing storytellers here. I enjoyed the stories so much! Please keep up the good work, masters! More stories!",
  [21502404] = "I know some of the stories are fabrications, but it doesn't matter. I'm a nerd and I love nerdy stories!",
  [21503101] = "Lately, every one of my friends has shared this mini-app on social media. I'm sick of it. Never thought this show would piggyback on it for publicity as well.",
  [21503102] = "I've had enough of these experts' remarks. All they ever do is criticize this and that, as if the whole world had to listen to them.",
  [21503103] = "Well, people just do this for fun, don't they? Who would take it seriously? Is this show trying to tell us what to do?",
  [21503104] = "Why is this show always so ill-informed about popular memes? This mini-app has long since become outdated in my city.",
  [21503201] = "Sending the link to this mini-app to my friend, I feel like a dog that got kicked when walking along the road.",
  [21503202] = "I think many things exist for a reason. For example, horoscope. Its interpretations strike me as quite accurate.",
  [21503203] = "These days there's really nothing show producers wouldn't stoop to for publicity. I think only grade school students would fall for this kind of divination...",
  [21503204] = "Not everything that can't be explained with science should be categorized as superstition, for we know so little about the universe.",
  [21503301] = "One of my colleagues is very superstitious and obsessed with such stuff. I tried to talk him out of it, but he never listened.",
  [21503302] = "I'm grateful to the show for sharing this knowledge. This kind of seemingly harmless stuff might invade our minds over time. We should watch out for it.",
  [21503303] = "I didn't know there was a mini-app like this. After watching the show, I especially tried it out. It's not bad!",
  [21503304] = "I'm a Tarot-lover. If you want your fortune told, feel free to contact me. I'm a master!",
  [21503401] = "This mini-app's actually on TV! All my friends and I have been playing it. It's pretty interesting.",
  [21503402] = "Actually, I'm also 'conditionally superstitious'—I believe good divination results and ignore bad ones.",
  [21503403] = "I'm gonna Share this video to my dear mom. She's crazy about this divination app lately!",
  [21503404] = "Make sure to beware of mini-apps like this, guys. I once got all my savings stolen through a mini-app simply because I offered it much of my personal info.",
  [21504101] = "The vlogger's performance during the show was plain, and its rating was unsatisfactory.",
  [21504201] = "So it's indeed another rehash? I'm sick of the overhype.",
  [21504202] = "A video like this actually went viral online? Well, someone got really lucky.",
  [21504203] = "Not worth publicizing. It seems this topic has outlived its popularity.",
  [21504401] = "It's like an electrifying modern version of Cinderella! I freaking love it!",
  [21504402] = "Maybe this kind of storyline and narrative tempo will strike the viewers as more acceptable. It's worth learning.",
  [21504403] = "Share it on other platforms immediately! Give it more publicity! It'll surely go viral again!",
  [21505101] = "Isn't this long overdue? I'm confused why they waited until now.",
  [21505102] = "People are actually receiving praise for doing their jobs. The public is being unbelievably tolerant these days.",
  [21505103] = "They call this 'first-hand information'? I've seen it hundreds of times on other sites.",
  [21505104] = "Why are they putting mid-roll ads in such serious news? Is there no depth they wouldn't stoop to for money?!",
  [21505201] = "There's no need to overpraise it. They should at least wait until the operation is rounded off...",
  [21505202] = "The show's a whole mess. There's no useful information in it whatsoever.",
  [21505203] = "The only info we ordinary people have access to is what's in the news. Maybe there's a lot we're not supposed to know.",
  [21505204] = "I hope the show will reveal more details of the operation. I'm bewildered by the available info.",
  [21505301] = "I hope the competent authority will keep up the good work and make sure lawbreakers have nowhere to hide.",
  [21505302] = "I feel proud to be a Loveland citizen! This is my first time realizing how lucky I am to be a native of Loveland City!",
  [21505303] = "The camera crew of the show put in a lot of effort as well. It was no easy job.",
  [21505304] = "I've been following the news on the progress of the Sweeping Action. I hope things will go well with it.",
  [21505401] = "Watching the show really gets my blood going!! I'm so proud to be a Loveland citizen!",
  [21505402] = "We regular citizens should do our part and cooperate with the government to make sure lawbreakers have nowhere to hide!",
  [21505403] = "Is this efficiency for real?! I tip my hat to all those who have contributed to this operation!",
  [21505404] = "It never crossed my mind that someday the scenes in those anti-mafia TV dramas would be re-enacted in real life. I'm so excited!",
  [21506101] = "Their work is indeed tiring, but at least it's well-paid. There are people in other lines of work more deserving of sympathy...",
  [21506102] = "As a service worker, I'll be the first to disagree. I get used as a punching bag every day and earn the lowest pay.",
  [21506103] = "Watching the show, I don't see anything tiring about their work. Instead, I kind of envy them. What's going on?",
  [21506104] = "Will you please stop playing the victims? Today's viewers have long since developed immunity to this finesse...",
  [21506201] = "You know what they say—we earn a beggar's income but worry about a billionaire's business...",
  [21506202] = "Are shows so easy to make now? Well, tomorrow I'll film how a dustman spends his day, which I guarantee you it will be more poignant than this.",
  [21506203] = "Aren't you guys newspeople as well? Well, you surely are sympathetic toward your fellow practitioners, but who will feel sympathy for laborers like me?",
  [21506204] = "Sorry, it's not that I'm unsympathetic. I'm just too tired to sympathize with anybody because I have to work 12 hours a day, 6 days a week...",
  [21506301] = "Isn't this exactly what wage earners' life is like? I see so much of myself in them!",
  [21506302] = "Sometimes, when faced with a dickwad at work, I really wanna quit my job, but to make ends meet, I have to take it lying down.",
  [21506303] = "There's nothing that upsets me more than videos or articles about the real situation blue-collar workers are in. Talking more about it will reduce me to tears...",
  [21506304] = "It seems many walks of life are just appealing on the surface and actually entail little-known hard work.",
  [21506401] = "Finally, someone's speaking up for us newspeople! This is exactly what I do on a workday! Watching this makes me wanna cry!",
  [21506402] = "I'm still in college, a student of journalism. I feel like I'm seeing my future...",
  [21506403] = "Though life is fraught with setbacks, we need to stride forward. Go for it, blue-collar workers!",
  [21506404] = "I see Loveland City at 5 AM every single day, hoping to build the life I want through hard work.",
  [21507101] = "I don't think this will work. The chance of recovering the swindled money is next to zero...",
  [21507102] = "I don't know how they have the nerve to brag about their efficiency when their hunt for the culprits has been unfruitful for so long.",
  [21507103] = "Am I the only one who feels the fraud victims are rich blockheads? They wouldn't have been swindled if they weren't greedy.",
  [21507104] = "Given that they're still on the loose, the chance of catching them is slim. They've probably fled overseas.",
  [21507201] = "My family began to have money problems because of financial fraud. Even to this day, we still haven't gotten our money back.",
  [21507202] = "I've watched the news but still don't know the outcome. What's the point of broadcasting news like this?",
  [21507203] = "It strikes me that many people are providing fake clues in an attempt to get the bounty, which serves only to add to the police's workload.",
  [21507204] = "Some people will never learn unless they get conned. This is kind of a lesson for them.",
  [21507301] = "There seem to have been more and more cases of financial fraud lately. Be careful, everybody. Investment is not without risk!",
  [21507302] = "Let me remind you one more time! There's no such thing as a free lunch! When you feel like you're about to hit pay dirt, it's most likely you're about to fall into a trap!",
  [21507303] = "To make money, you need to take baby steps at first. Not having been conned so far only means you haven't encountered a con game intended for you yet.",
  [21507304] = "Justice might be late, but it'll always be there. There's nowhere those crazed criminals can run that the police won't find them!",
  [21507401] = "I'm positive I'll never fall victim to any financial fraud if my bank balance remains 0.",
  [21507402] = "I hope the police will catch those criminals soon and recover the swindled money! So many families have fallen apart because of them!",
  [21507403] = "Am I the only one tempted by the 'handsome rewards'? Will I strike it rich if I chance on a wanted criminal?",
  [21507404] = "Some frauds target nobody but elderly people behind the times. I hate their guts! I hope they'll all be brought to justice soon!",
  [21508101] = "I visited it and was disappointed. The taste of the food has changed, and so has everything else.",
  [21508102] = "The so-called heartwarming reminiscence and reopening are nothing but publicity stunts. The taste we remember is irrecoverable.",
  [21508103] = "I don't know why people are lining up in front of such a small eatery. The food is just average.",
  [21508104] = "The current prices are unbelievable. The great popularity has indeed changed the owner's original aspiration some time ago.",
  [21508201] = "A few days ago, a friend asked me to go to that restaurant to check in with him, but I declined. The crowdedness alone is enough to deter me.",
  [21508202] = "To be objective, it is only yourself and what you felt at that time that you are nostalgic for, not the taste of the food.",
  [21508203] = "I waited in line for a long while on a hot day only to discover one thing—better to miss than to meet!",
  [21508204] = "For those of you who wanna go there because of the food you remember, heed my advice: drop the idea. They got a new chef.",
  [21508301] = "I won't be able to spare the time in the next few days, but I'll make sure to go there and check in on the weekend, just for the sense of nostalgia.",
  [21508302] = "At that time I was a student, but now I'm a parent. I wanna take my kid there and tell him about my past.",
  [21508303] = "How the food tastes doesn't matter anymore. The name of the restaurant alone is enough to reduce me to tears.",
  [21508304] = "I wanna ask at what time the restaurant is relatively less crowded. I'm really not a big fan of waiting in line...",
  [21508401] = "It's the same recipe, the same taste! I was only a kid when I last dined at this eatery. Time really does fly.",
  [21508402] = "Talking with the restaurant owner alone gives me a strong sense of nostalgia. It's like stepping back in time!",
  [21508403] = "How I wish I could turn the clock back! I know it's impossible, but reliving those days in my mind from time to time is also nice.",
  [21508404] = "I'm so happy this little eatery has become popular. It's deserving of it. I wish the owner a booming business!",
  [21509101] = "Due to inadequate publicity and the unimpressive show arrangements, few people came to see the lantern show.",
  [21509201] = "It's so boring, far removed from the lantern show I imagined. I wish I had gone to see a movie instead.",
  [21509202] = "Stalls in this place are unprofitable. All the money I invested went to waste.",
  [21509203] = "Publicity seems unnecessary. It'll be better if they focus on minimizing the losses.",
  [21509401] = "I had an unforgettable night. If they stage another show like this, I'll participate again!",
  [21509402] = "All my wares sold out shortly after I set up my stall. It seems I should prepare a bigger stock next time!",
  [21509403] = "Put in more publicity effort. The lantern show of Loveland City deserves to be beheld by everybody.",
  [21510101] = "The results of the investigation were sure as hell tampered with. Whoever fabricated the data went way too far with their fabrication.",
  [21510102] = "No means of communication can change its nature. Now I've got a cellphone, but I have to stand by 24/7. It's so frustrating!",
  [21510103] = "I hate bosses who don't know personal boundaries. Do any of you know how exhausting it is to have to be constantly ready for a video conference?",
  [21510104] = "Nevertheless, if you only communicate with your boss online, you might not recognize them when you see them offline, which can be quite embarrassing!",
  [21510201] = "Not having to meet people face to face is just a natural outcome of the development of technology. There's no need to over-read it.",
  [21510202] = "The old system isn't entirely without its advantages. Sometimes, meeting people face-to-face is much easier. With typed messages, you have to carefully consider your wording.",
  [21510203] = "I'm not saying the current way is bad, but it feels less solemn and less ritualistic than the old way, which is rather lamentable.",
  [21510204] = "As a pathetic wage earner, I'd say it's got nothing to do with me. I think changing workplace norms is a job for subsequent younger generations.",
  [21510301] = "Online communication is amazing, because I get to play dead when my boss wants me for something. By the way, I hate those communication apps that show whether a sent message has been read!",
  [21510302] = "Maybe someday we won't even have to go to work and can work from home. That'll make our work schedules much more flexible.",
  [21510303] = "I advise the government to introduce some new policies to define the boundaries between life and work during the online handover of work stuff so that they won't take up too much of our rest time.",
  [21510304] = "You've got to be kidding me. There are still people who have meetings in actual meeting rooms? I thought the whole world had adopted digital management!",
  [21510401] = "I'll unhesitatingly give it my full support! Face-to-face work reports are literally killing me!",
  [21510402] = "Please enforce it throughout the world right away! Right now! Immediately! I've had it up to here with endless meetings!",
  [21510403] = "I wonder when this mode will be adopted in our company. I'm okay with never seeing my boss's face ever again.",
  [21510404] = "It's about time someone improved the workplace rules a little. Lowly workers like us also want things to be better. Go for it!",
  [21511101] = "Is that really necessary? It doesn't seem any different from the old way…",
  [21511102] = "I've gone there to see it. The machine happened to malfunction, and my backpack got stuck in it. It's even more inconvenient than the old one. They shouldn't have replaced it.",
  [21511103] = "The devices have indeed been upgraded, but the security screeners are so mean. They scare me every time I see them.",
  [21511104] = "How many more times are they going to hype this up? They shouldn't overdo it, otherwise, it'll serve only to have the opposite effect.",
  [21511201] = "They finally got new machines. The old ones were unbelievably frustrating, though the new ones don't really seem much better.",
  [21511202] = "Does anybody else feel that the new devices have a noticeably higher failure rate than the old ones? Did they not even do a test run before deploying them?",
  [21511203] = "There's a big difference between imagination and reality. Honestly, having gone there and seen the machines with my own eyes, I'm very disappointed. They can hardly be called advanced.",
  [21511204] = "The new devices filled the subway station with a funky odor. I wonder if it's harmful to pregnant women or children…",
  [21511301] = "The subway station in front of my house got those new security check devices as well. The mere sight of them brightens up my day!",
  [21511302] = "This is a great thing that benefits everybody. I feel that Loveland City is getting better and better. I feel proud when my out-of-town friends come to visit.",
  [21511303] = "The new devices do make the station look brand-new. Going through security feels much more pleasant now.",
  [21511304] = "I feel that the new devices are pretty practical. They make things much easier, and the security screeners are nice. It's a very pleasant experience.",
  [21511401] = "I've long since heard they'd replace the security check devices. After they were installed, I immediately went to check them out. They didn't let me down!",
  [21511402] = "The infrastructure in Loveland City is truly amazing! This city is getting increasingly more habitable! I'm so happy I'm a Lovelander!",
  [21511403] = "I can tell from the pictures that the devices are quite advanced. I'll be able to try them out the next time I go on a business trip. Looking forward to it!",
  [21511404] = "Ever since the new devices were installed, my kids have never complained or cried during trips again. They even demanded to go through the security check for a second time!",
  [21512101] = "One minute it seems to have a point, but the next it seems pointless. I feel that all news reports are like this these days…",
  [21512102] = "Even licensed media are using such clickbait titles now? This is virtually a bluff and deception.",
  [21512103] = "After so many days, their accomplices are still at large? The Special Task Force is getting more inefficient by the day.",
  [21512104] = "I thought they'd all been caught. It never crossed my mind that his accomplices were still out there. How could the nearby residents sleep at night?",
  [21512201] = "It turns out today's news reports are just like domestic movies—a suspenseful beginning, a ridiculous end.",
  [21512202] = "Will this never end? It's been in the headlines for so many days. The mere sight of it bugs me.",
  [21512203] = "I read the news report for a long while but still couldn't understand the ins and outs. Maybe I have poor comprehension…",
  [21512204] = "How could those criminals be so unruly? It's hard to believe such an outrageous violent, incident could happen in an age like this.",
  [21512301] = "Can't believe the case happened near my home. I hope they'll catch all the culprits soon. If they don't, I'll always feel jumpy outdoors.",
  [21512302] = "Have faith in the Special Task Force and Loveland City. Every single criminal will be brought to justice!",
  [21512303] = "I've been following this case all along. The reports of the show are very detailed. Looking forward to seeing some follow-up.",
  [21512304] = "This kind of horrific violence must be met with severe punishment! Those criminals must not receive any leniency!",
  [21512401] = "The show's crew was in the front line all along. Thumbs up to them for their bravery!",
  [21512402] = "We must not let our guard down unless the criminal's accomplices are caught. Anybody with information should come forward and help the police!",
  [21512403] = "The Special Task Force was so efficient during the investigation! Their presence in the city is so reassuring! I hope they catch the guy's accomplices soon!",
  [21512404] = "The news report depicts the whole process of the manhunt by the police. It turns out we've been enjoying a stable life because some others have been making sacrifices for us!",
  [21513101] = "I'm really speechless. The promo video is completely incomprehensible. This kind of high-end exhibitions are indeed out of the ordinary people's league.",
  [21513102] = "My friend said he saw it once, but it was so boring. Looks like there's a reason it has been postponed for such a long time.",
  [21513103] = "I was looking forward to it, but after watching this promo, I suddenly lost interest in it. It strikes me as unimpressive.",
  [21513104] = "It's hyped up as a high-end, mysterious event, but actually, there's nothing special about it. It's just a publicity gimmick.",
  [21513201] = "This is definitely the worst one ever. I think this was my last time attending it.",
  [21513202] = "I heard they'll gift some of the reviewers with free tickets, but I'm not leaving this review to get a ticket. I won't go there, even if they gimme a free ticket.",
  [21513203] = "We shouldn't call anything bad without trying it first. I've tried it. It's indeed boring.",
  [21513204] = "They call it an experiments exhibition, but actually, it's not as high-end as it sounds. Maybe only grade school students will find those experiments intriguing.",
  [21513301] = "Three years ago, I had the good fortune to participate in this exhibition, and it was a very rewarding experience. I hope I'll learn something new by seeing it again this year.",
  [21513302] = "I'd never say no to such a rewarding activity. The tickets are kind of hard to come by, though. If only they could gimme one for free.",
  [21513303] = "It's definitely not my fault that I failed to get a ticket. Can't the organizers raise the quota a little or extend the exhibition by a few days?",
  [21513304] = "A grand occasion. I believe many sci-tech enthusiasts have long been looking forward to it. I'm looking forward to it as well.",
  [21513401] = "It's coming! It's coming! At long last, it's coming! I've been waiting for so long, and now it's finally coming!",
  [21513402] = "Please! Please look at me! I didn't act quickly enough during the free-for-all. Please gimme a free ticket!",
  [21513403] = "As the worst student, I wanna go there and bathe myself in knowledge as well. I heard it'd be quite interesting. Looking forward to it!",
  [21513404] = "Ahhhhhhhhh! Why is it still not the day of the exhibition?! I can't wait any longer! My mental state￥%……&",
  [21514101] = "The escape room is a botched job, and the puzzles are unbelievably simple.",
  [21514201] = "Whoever has tried it will never wanna try it again.",
  [21514202] = "The puzzles in the escape room are virtually an insult to my intelligence.",
  [21514203] = "Somebody should consider making a video of it—\"Worst Escape Room Ever.\"",
  [21514401] = "It's the most interesting escape room I've ever tried. Every detail is an embodiment of the designer's meticulousness!",
  [21514402] = "No wonder they call it \"the most challenging escape room.\" The puzzles are very difficult, and it's quite an immersive experience.",
  [21514403] = "There are many escape rooms in the city, and I've tried them all. This one's truly matchless! Everybody should come and try it!",
  [21515101] = "Here's a note of caution for those of you who haven't seen this show: it's very boring. I'll bet you anything you can't watch it for ten minutes without falling asleep.",
  [21515102] = "So much of the so-called knowledge they offer in the show is incorrect. They got the nerve to call themselves archeologists?",
  [21515103] = "The pace of the edited show is too slow. Maybe this kind of show is not for me, after all.",
  [21515104] = "All I saw was a bunch of people walking in a pitch-dark cavern. I didn't feel any of the awe that I expected the relics to make me feel.",
  [21515201] = "Are these people really exploring relics? Do we know for sure that they're not using a cellar to fool the audience?",
  [21515202] = "Are the show's crew really on such a tight budget? They really should upgrade their equipment a little. The footage is so dark that I can hardly see anything.",
  [21515203] = "Being focused on knowledge doesn't mean the show has to be boring. Stuff like this is not worth seeing at all.",
  [21515204] = "I've always been a lover of exploration shows. Never thought this one would be such a botched job. I'm very disappointed.",
  [21515301] = "I love it. I hope they'll make more of such entertaining and rewarding programs.",
  [21515302] = "The guests are perfect for the show. Their interaction with each other alone makes the show quite enjoyable. I hope they won't be replaced.",
  [21515303] = "A very fun show. I like lying on my couch and watching them dig around in the vast ruins!",
  [21515304] = "The show's perfect except for the frequent product placement. I've always been a lover of exploration shows.",
  [21515401] = "This kind of immersive viewing experience is amazing. I feel as if I were exploring the ruins myself!",
  [21515402] = "I was fascinated. The show's too short to satisfy my appetite. I wanna time-travel to the day when they'll air the next episode.",
  [21515403] = "He's not like an archeologist, more like my humorous, funny old baby! I love his way of speaking!",
  [21515404] = "Facts prove that only a meticulous enough producer can produce a good show. The crews of the other shows should keep that in mind.",
  [21516101] = "I wonder how you guys managed to make a show so boring and vulgar. Every second of it is ridden with bias.",
  [21516102] = "The editor botched up the tempo. I don't know what kind of story they're trying to tell. It's just so confusing.",
  [21516103] = "This is my first time seeing photoshopped pictures used in this type of show. They would've received a lot less criticism had they shown a tiny little bit of sincerity.",
  [21516104] = "This show ruined the beautiful images of small towns in my mind. It revealed all the ugly sides of them.",
  [21516201] = "It's undeniable that such beautiful and affluent towns do exist, but as far as I know, most towns are a lot less idyllic than we think.",
  [21516202] = "The way I see it, shortly after the show aired, this place will become a tourist attraction, and the locals will start opening rural restaurants. In an age like this where exposure brings wealth, no place can stay idyllic forever.",
  [21516203] = "Towns are indeed more affluent than before, but there are still many problems. For example, the issue of poor educational and medical conditions still remains unsolved.",
  [21516204] = "I think it's fake. Everybody in the show seems to be following a script. If only things in real life could go as smoothly as they do in the script.",
  [21516301] = "I would never dare spout off about going back to my ancestral home to raise pigs if things go south. It turns out I'm not even fit to do that.",
  [21516302] = "Finally, we got a show with a realistic outlook. Towns are entirely different from the usual stereotype now.",
  [21516303] = "I wanna live there after I retire. It'll be best if I can get a house with a little yard where I can grow my own vegetables.",
  [21516304] = "So even rural villages have become affluent. Does that mean I'm the only one in poverty now?",
  [21516401] = "My friend asked me why I was watching people raise pigs. I said I didn't know, that I just couldn't help it!",
  [21516402] = "I'll try to learn some skills beforehand so that if someday I have to go back to my hometown to raise pigs, I'll get to do it with oozing confidence!",
  [21516403] = "I really envy those who get to live this kind of simple, down-home country life in which every day is vigorous. It's entirely different from my life as a migrant worker.",
  [21516404] = "No wonder more and more highly educated people are going back to rural areas. It turns out outstanding people can shine anywhere!",
  [21517101] = "So many of those dangers could've been avoided, but these people walked right into them. I think they shouldn't have named this show Into the Wild. They should call it the Suicide Squad.",
  [21517102] = "They're making more and more such wilderness survival shows, each worse than the last.",
  [21517103] = "I wouldn't say anything if they had an original script. The problem is even their script is a plagiarism. If they say it's a coincidence, I won't buy it.",
  [21517104] = "These guests are being way too dramatic. Their stagy reactions are kind of funny.",
  [21517201] = "There are too many similar shows. The novelty has worn off, and I don't see anything special about this one.",
  [21517202] = "Production of this kind of show shouldn't be encouraged, 'cause it's really dangerous for regular people to venture into the wilderness.",
  [21517203] = "I really dislike it, but I'm also curious about what other ridiculous stuff they'll add to the next episode, which makes me kind of reluctant to give up on it.",
  [21517204] = "The worm-eating part is so gross. Do they not know how disgusting that is to people who are eating their meals?",
  [21517301] = "Lately, I've become crazy about wilderness survival shows, and this one's very good compared with the others. The scenes seem quite real.",
  [21517302] = "They did a good job building up tension, but I wanna see the team encounter some greater difficulties.",
  [21517303] = "All the team members are pretty good, and they don't act like babies, which is a pleasant part. Those in the other show are disgustingly stagy.",
  [21517304] = "It's a good time killer when there's no good variety show available. You don't have to use your brain to derive pleasure from watching it.",
  [21517401] = "A wilderness survival show actually got my blood going! The cohesion and unity of the team are truly amazing!",
  [21517402] = "I don't envy them for the money they're making this way, 'cause I might not survive a single day on that uninhabited island.",
  [21517403] = "Nobody will disagree if I call this the best survival show, I presume? Other shows stand no comparison to it!",
  [21517404] = "I learned a lot of useless knowledge from watching the show. It might never come in handy, but at least I get to brag to my friends about it!",
  [21518101] = "I can tell at a glance that they're advertising. This airline's customer service is notorious.",
  [21518102] = "I'm sorry, but I don't get the point… If someone accosts me during a journey, I'll only end up being too awkward to utter a word.",
  [21518103] = "Yeah, there are so many tourists that the locals can't get any tickets… I've been mad about it, and this just makes me even angrier!",
  [21518104] = "It's so, so, so embarrassing… The only thing more embarrassing than it is that I've seen was a comedy sketch performed by everybody in my company, including my boss.",
  [21518201] = "Are there really so many things that can happen during flights? How come my flights comprise only three steps: boarding the plane, sleeping, and disembarking?",
  [21518202] = "This show is so boring. I don't see anything interesting about it. Is it that I have poor comprehension?",
  [21518203] = "Watching this show cost me my appetite for today's dinner. Those who wanna lose weight are in luck.",
  [21518204] = "Maybe the show's meant to present that kind of interpersonal harmony, but clearly, they failed.",
  [21518301] = "It turns out there are so many details on the planes that I've never noticed before. I'll keep my eyes peeled during my next flight.",
  [21518302] = "You don't need to look carefully to see subtle goodness. Maybe it's right under our noses all the time.",
  [21518303] = "I love this kind of story that happens in nondescript circumstances. They're heartwarming and worth reliving for a long time.",
  [21518304] = "I once received help from a stranger during a journey as well. That feeling was hard to describe with words.",
  [21518401] = "These people are all so kind! Welcome to Loveland City, and enjoy your stay!",
  [21518402] = "I was afraid of traveling by air, but watching this show helped me overcome my fear. I'm going to give it a shot!",
  [21518403] = "The flowers in Loveland City are in full bloom in this season, and the locals are very hospitable. People from all around the world are welcome to visit Loveland City!",
  [21518404] = "If nothing else, the plane food this airline offers is so, so, so, so amazing! I strongly recommend it!",
  [21519101] = "It was loosely regulated, and the whole place was in a mess. There was even a fistfight.",
  [21519201] = "What a boring game. I should've just slept at home instead.",
  [21519202] = "So it's true that games are fun only if you play them with like-minded people.",
  [21519203] = "Did I lapse into an awkward silence just now? I'll cut that part out when I get back. Nobody needs to see it.",
  [21519401] = "It feels good to come out and relax. Social activities turn out to be less difficult than I imagined.",
  [21519402] = "What a fun day! I hope more people will feel the pleasure of playing board games!",
  [21519403] = "The ambiance here is pretty good. The rating of this one is secured!",
  [21520101] = "May I venture to say that the techniques they teach in the show are not practical at all? Be careful not to be misled by them!",
  [21520102] = "It's supposed to be a serious show, but they made a mess of it. I don't think it's okay to take this kind of thing lightly.",
  [21520103] = "Why didn't they hire a professional team to do it? The instructors didn't take the teaching seriously, and their answers were perfunctory.",
  [21520104] = "This is the worst teaching I've ever seen. They're virtually toying with the audience's lives…",
  [21520201] = "I thought I could learn something, but after watching the show, I'm still confused. Who am I? Where am I…?",
  [21520202] = "Is this a comedy show or something? The guy started laughing halfway through first aid. It doesn't look like a science show at all.",
  [21520203] = "A whole day's work is tiring enough. Why did I have to see a show like this? Is this divine retribution for my slacking at work?",
  [21520204] = "It strikes me as useless. I mean, we don't need it when there's no accident, and when an accident does happen, we won't be able to react in time.",
  [21520301] = "I'll Favorite this and share it to my family chat group. It might come in handy someday.",
  [21520302] = "I've Favorited a whole lot of articles about how to survive disasters like earthquakes. I hope I'll never need that knowledge.",
  [21520303] = "It's admirable of them to have made a practical show so interesting. I can tell they've put a lot of effort into it.",
  [21520304] = "I'm a landlubber, and I'm always scared of getting into water. Knowing how to save myself makes me feel a lot better.",
  [21520401] = "Look what an amazing show I've found! Tell me I'm super smart!",
  [21520402] = "The boys and girls on the rescue team are so hot! I love them!",
  [21520403] = "Such interesting and rewarding shows are something of a rarity now. I'll share it with everybody I know!",
  [21520404] = "As a professional lifeguard, I can answer for it that the professor's demonstration in the show is truly professional.",
  [21521101] = "Even God cannot contradict an expert's words. What does it take to have fewer experts in our world?",
  [21521102] = "AAAAARGH! This show is awful. It gives me an urge to dox the show's crew!",
  [21521103] = "I watch shows for pleasure or knowledge, not to get inculcated with values.",
  [21521104] = "There are many rumors I can't say for sure are true, but I'm positive the one mentioned in this show is true.",
  [21521201] = "I don't care if this show is pointless or lacking in depth. It just strikes me as boring and unenjoyable.",
  [21521202] = "I got the sense that this topic is gaining too much popularity, and every media company's trying to piggyback on it.",
  [21521203] = "They want the show to have depth, but they lack the right attitude, which is a problem every show seems to have.",
  [21521204] = "They repeated a lot of opinions from others but none of them hit home. Isn't this echoing others' views as well?",
  [21521301] = "Too many people are servile in real life and tough-talking online. They don't care if their remarks will hurt anybody or not.",
  [21521302] = "I hope the price for starting rumors will be upped someday. Those people need to be reminded that defamation on the Internet is subject to legal consequences.",
  [21521303] = "However, most people won't be able to break their habits of echoing others' views until they themselves fall victim.",
  [21521304] = "I don't dare believe any rumors online anymore. Starting a rumor is easy, but scotching it is not.",
  [21521401] = "I couldn't agree more! I hope there will be less misinformation online so that there can be more sincerity.",
  [21521402] = "How can I not praise a show that has such great depth! Beware of unfounded rumors, guys!",
  [21521403] = "I've long since learned to stay quiet on the Internet, 'cause anything you say might prove hurtful to someone.",
  [21521404] = "I've seen with my own eyes how an ordinary piece of information got distorted step by step by people who relayed it. Hopefully, more people will stand up for victims.",
  [21522101] = "A lame show spreading problematic values. I've reported it to stop it from victimizing more people.",
  [21522102] = "They call it a discussion but allow only opinions they agree with to be expressed. Isn't this a kind of bullying too?",
  [21522103] = "I totally disagree with the opinions of the show's crew. As for the reason, I think everybody knows.",
  [21522104] = "As a media company, they should stay neutral and rational. Don't they think it's a bit inappropriate to have such a subjective point of view?",
  [21522201] = "Every coin has two sides, and there are certainly pros and cons to doxing. It's not worth discussing.",
  [21522202] = "The expert in the show is unbelievable. Their speech is entirely nonsensical.",
  [21522203] = "I don't care what they do. It's none of my business. I just came along for the ride.",
  [21522204] = "Seen from a legal perspective, those famous martial artists in the olden days were all murderers. Real justice should be about intention, not action.",
  [21522301] = "If justice had no boundaries, many crimes would be committed in the name of justice…",
  [21522302] = "There have been more and more \"online judges\" lately. Is this really a good thing for our society?",
  [21522303] = "I hope those who dox people will have a taste of their own medicine.",
  [21522304] = "Important things should be repeated thrice. It's illegal to dox people! It's illegal! It's illegal!",
  [21522401] = "Are those who dox people really serving justice? They just derive pleasure from punishing people!",
  [21522402] = "Nobody but law enforcement has the right to mete out punishment. I hope those people will do the right thing.",
  [21522403] = "Remember those incidents online where the truth eventually became unascertainable? If you don't know the ins and outs of it, don't try to be the judge.",
  [21522404] = "Unbelievable. Do those trolls really see themselves as gods who get to judge people? Wake up. You're just bullies.",
  [21523101] = "I don't see anything special about the views. They're not much different from each other.",
  [21523102] = "They overdid the filter thing. Landscapes are supposed to be presented unadorned. Filtering them serves only to make them look unreal.",
  [21523103] = "The cameraperson is so incompetent. They didn't even present one-tenth of the beauty of the view. I can do a better job with my eyes closed.",
  [21523104] = "I was looking forward to a cable car ride, but now, having watched the show, I'm determined not to try it.",
  [21523201] = "It's a total lie. Everybody who's been there knows it's not like that at all. You have to wait in line for long hours. It's a terrible experience.",
  [21523202] = "What the heck is wrong with the cameraperson? Even the pictures I took with my cellphone are better than this.",
  [21523203] = "They're kind of exaggerating. I've been to most of the places filmed in the show, and they're not as beautiful as these people say they are.",
  [21523204] = "I've never sat in a cable car, and I don't see why I should. Having my feet above the ground makes me feel unsafe.",
  [21523301] = "No written knowledge can substitute for what can be learned through practice. Seeing enough beautiful places makes me realize how humble I am.",
  [21523302] = "Having watched the show, I think I know what kind of graduation gift I should give myself.",
  [21523303] = "Every view is a gift from nature. I hope everybody will see the beauty of our world.",
  [21523304] = "I can't believe I'm thinking of trying it despite my acrophobia. The view is just too stunning to be missed out on.",
  [21523401] = "It's beautiful! Forgive me for my small vocabulary. I don't have the right words to describe how awed I am!",
  [21523402] = "Trust me, it's absolutely amazing to take a cable car ride! And it's addictive!",
  [21523403] = "A cable car ride is like slowly walking into a painting of the landscape. That feeling is virtually indescribable. Everybody should try it!",
  [21523404] = "This show is amazing! The beauty is really breathtaking! I'll visit all these places the first chance I got!",
  [21524101] = "The topic is unpopular. Hardly anybody's talking about it.",
  [21524201] = "Got a tight study schedule and no time for group chat.",
  [21524202] = "Work is exhausting enough. Can't be bothered to deal with colleagues in the chat group in off-hours.",
  [21524203] = "If I got the time, I'd rather spend it supporting my idol.",
  [21524401] = "We spend the last day of every vacation \"discussing\" homework in the chat group.",
  [21524402] = "Whoever criticizes my boss with me is a good friend of mine!",
  [21524403] = "The coterie chat group is like a home to me. All its members are my sisters!",
  [21525101] = "I disagree with the opinions of those in the show. I mean, nothing's really safe these days.",
  [21525102] = "That expert talked on and on, but their viewpoint remained ambiguous. It's virtually a waste of the audience's time!",
  [21525103] = "The escape tricks mentioned in the show are mostly nonsense. The only tip that's kind of useful is to stand against the wall with slightly bent knees.",
  [21525104] = "I think this kind of stuff is common knowledge now. Was it really necessary to make a show about it?",
  [21525201] = "In many old housing developments, there is really nobody maintaining the elevators. I would rather take the stairs than the elevator if I lived in a place like that.",
  [21525202] = "It's easy for them to say. Who can be not panicking in a situation like that?",
  [21525203] = "I really loathe the host of this show. When will they be replaced?",
  [21525204] = "May I venture to say that the expert they invited is downright unprofessional? Anybody with a bit of expertise can tell.",
  [21525301] = "This is a great thing. They're attaching importance to elevator security. Our company even specially organized a safety training session.",
  [21525302] = "Many people are worried that the elevator might drop from a high floor straight to the bottom, but actually, the probability of that is next to zero. You don't have to worry about that.",
  [21525303] = "I keep hearing about incidents like that, and I was worried I might suffer the same misfortune. Now it seems my worries were needless.",
  [21525304] = "It's part of human nature to fear the unknown, but actually, many facts are far removed from what our instincts tell us.",
  [21525401] = "I've been in a falling elevator before! Watching the number on the display decrease made me feel as if time had slowed down…",
  [21525402] = "People who live on high floors cannot go on with their life or work without an elevator. Now we finally got a show disseminating knowledge in this regard.",
  [21525403] = "My aged mother believes elevators are dangerous and would rather take the stairs. Now I finally got something to convince her of!",
  [21525404] = "Taking the elevator always gives me the willies. Now that I know how it works, I can finally dismiss my fear!",
  [21526101] = "That was one severe goof. I think it could be deemed a serious filming accident…",
  [21526102] = "Does the producer think the audience is stupid? Anybody with eyes can see through their lame disguise.",
  [21526103] = "What a trashy show! I should never have had the slightest expectation of it.",
  [21526104] = "I thought they'd made some great breakthroughs in disguise techniques after so many years. It never occurred to me that they were still using the same old tricks used in TV dramas I used to watch in my childhood.",
  [21526201] = "I got nothing against the show, but the sound effects they added during post-production are totally unnecessary, and they're not funny at all.",
  [21526202] = "They should've at least learned some professional knowledge before producing the show. It's riddled with mistakes, which is utterly unacceptable.",
  [21526203] = "I expected to get my mind blown by some super-duper disguise skills, but the show turned out to be a disappointment as great as my expectation…",
  [21526204] = "Such crappy and long-winded shows are something of a rarity now. I could use its hypnotic effects.",
  [21526301] = "I was astonished. It turns out that disguise skills can really work miracles. I used to believe they were a lie.",
  [21526302] = "It turns out the best way to disguise is not to wear a cool overcoat as people do in TV dramas. It's blending in with the crowd.",
  [21526303] = "Watching the show made me realize disguise skills are not as mysterious or futuristic as I imagined. This is a very rewarding show.",
  [21526304] = "The disguise techniques the master imparted on-site are very useful. My boyfriend failed to recognize me.",
  [21526401] = "Disguise skills are so cool! It's always been my dream to become a master of disguise!",
  [21526402] = "An amazing show! I watched every episode the moment it aired! Looking forward to the surprises the next episode has to offer!",
  [21526403] = "When I was watching TV dramas as a kid, I always wondered why the protagonists could make themselves unrecognizable simply by wearing a mask…",
  [21526404] = "When my friend recommended this show to me, I disbelieved him, but now I'm a big fan of it!",
  [21527101] = "I watched it for a long while but still couldn't understand. It's full of nonsense.",
  [21527102] = "I don't know why this topic is so popular. What does some rich guy's auction have to do with us?",
  [21527103] = "The so-called insider is full of lies. They're just dying for exposure.",
  [21527104] = "Am I the only one uninterested in this kind of auction? I don't see anything special about it.",
  [21527201] = "When I saw the title, I thought something big had happened. After watching the video for a minute… I'm out of here.",
  [21527202] = "However enviable someone else's life is, it's theirs. We should just focus on building our own lives.",
  [21527203] = "Whoever described the venue for a private auction as a paradise must be living a harsh life…",
  [21527204] = "I hate it when a show keeps me in suspense like this. They should've just spat it out. I'll give it a bad review as punishment.",
  [21527301] = "He's telling the truth. I'll testify for him as the big chandelier at the venue for the auction.",
  [21527302] = "The story sounds pretty real, and it has rich details. If they add some corny, wealthy family secrets to it, it'll be even juicier.",
  [21527303] = "It's surprisingly interesting. I'll keep following it. Though it's probably a fabrication, I'm a nerd, and I love this kind of stuff.",
  [21527304] = "I find it rewarding to dabble in domains out of my league. At least it gives me motivation to keep striving.",
  [21527401] = "Is this how rich people seek pleasure? I feel like I'm peeking into a new world!",
  [21527402] = "Hurry up, insider! Do I have to take a cab to your house, put a knife to your throat, and coerce you into disclosing it?!",
  [21527403] = "Ha ha! I love this kind of dramatic and faintly adorable way of narrating. I feel like I'm listening to another me!",
  [21527404] = "This is the world I dream of living in! When will my best friend get rich overnight?!",
  [21528101] = "They call a place with nothing but a bunch of doohickeys a museum? This really broadened my horizons.",
  [21528102] = "Peculiar gimmicks are piling up here. They're all just tools capitalists use to exploit the unwary.",
  [21528103] = "Am I the only one finding this kind of museum saccharine and embarrassing? Is romantic love the only thing that matters in life?",
  [21528104] = "I don't quite understand youngsters' stuff like this. I thought museums were for cultural artifacts only.",
  [21528201] = "My friend dragged me there once. I found it boring. All exhibits were common, nondescript things.",
  [21528202] = "Maybe I'm dispassionate by nature. I've never had any of those intense emotions. Memories don't matter much to me.",
  [21528203] = "There are a lot of things we can experience in life. If we keep dwelling on the past, we'll never be able to move on.",
  [21528204] = "I actually saw a letter for me from my ex in the museum. It's so disgusting. Did he forget how he used to treat me?",
  [21528301] = "I love the ambiance of the museum. It's very quiet. Everybody seems to be immersed in their own recollections.",
  [21528302] = "It brought back a lot of memories. Looks like I need to check on those old things of mine when I get back.",
  [21528303] = "Maybe some people don't understand, but only by being here will you know how nice this place is.",
  [21528304] = "Memories are beautiful only because they cannot be re-enacted. We should cherish the present, for it too will become a memory.",
  [21528401] = "I was reduced to tears after seeing two cabinets of exhibits! It turns out everybody has something buried in the deep recesses of their mind that they prefer not to recall.",
  [21528402] = "I saw a story almost identical to mine. It turns out I'm not alone in this world.",
  [21528403] = "This museum is so therapeutic and heartwarming. It brought back so many nondescript but unforgettable memories.",
  [21528404] = "I think we live to create memories, which, beautiful or not, are proof of our lives.",
  [21529101] = "The facts of the case are still unclear. Many people present expressed doubts about it.",
  [21529201] = "It seems there are still many questionable points in the case. The investigation needs to be resumed.",
  [21529202] = "Is someone trying to complicate the situation to profit from it or playing at this matter?",
  [21529203] = "Another twist at the press conference, the truth remains a mystery!",
  [21529401] = "All crimes met with punishment, and the Loveland is heading for a better future!",
  [21529402] = "The criminals are finally in custody! Fantastic news!",
  [21529403] = "Justice served, Loveland City will embrace a brighter future!",
  [21530101] = "They call it \"a thorough investigation\" when it actually is \"all for the show.\" Nobody will ever care about the situation the grassroots are in...",
  [21530102] = "Is the situation in all industries not bad enough? I wonder how long it'll take for things to get better for me.",
  [21530103] = "May I say something as a guy majoring in flip phone repair? Flip phones \"graduated\" from the market before I graduated from college...",
  [21530104] = "Each new generation excels the last one. The age thresholds enterprises set for recruitment are getting lower and lower. Will middle-aged people's employment issues ever be solved?",
  [21530201] = "I'd like to market myself a little. I'm an industry-wrecker. I changed my job six times, and all six companies collapsed. If there's a rival company you don't like, feel free to contact me.",
  [21530202] = "At the age of 30, I wanted to become a gatekeeper to avoid wasting the next 30 years of my life, but it never crossed my mind the gate-keeping industry was getting competitive too—two 27-year-old guys were vying with me for the position.",
  [21530203] = "This expert is so unprofessional. That information is 10-odd years behind the times. It's utterly misleading!",
  [21530204] = "I think money shouldn't be the only thing we consider when choosing a career. Figuring out what you're passionate about is the most important.",
  [21530301] = "I'm not fussy about my future career. My biggest dream is to punch holes in saltine crackers in a food factory.",
  [21530302] = "Does everybody feel their industry is the most unpromising?",
  [21530303] = "Choosing the wrong career can really be as disastrous as being born into the wrong family. Think twice before making a decision, guys!",
  [21530304] = "It basically revealed everything that different industries are suffering from. You don't see many shows like this one around these days. It's worth staying tuned to.",
  [21530401] = "Next year I'll have to pick a major. I feel lucky to have watched this show. It taught me a lot!",
  [21530402] = "Every day I feel I can't stand my job anymore, but after seeing the situation in the other industries, I shut my mouth and get my ass back to the workplace.",
  [21530403] = "They said what everybody in my industry wanted to say! I'm going to recommend this show to everybody I know!",
  [21530404] = "I discovered that many people held misconceptions about my major, so let me get this straight one more time: computer majors really don't know how to repair computers!",
  [21531101] = "Next time someone asks me why I don't want to be a boss and whether it's because I don't like it, I'll tell them, \"That's right. I don't like that.\"",
  [21531102] = "What's the big deal about being the boss? Bosses have to work too, don't they? My dream is different. I dream of becoming an immortal.",
  [21531103] = "I tried that, and I bitterly regretted it. They say a boss earns several million bucks a day, but how come my bank account didn't receive a penny?",
  [21531104] = "Projects like this one can never give you the pleasure of being a boss. Ordinary people can hardly even imagine it.",
  [21531201] = "I can only say wage earners' wallets are being targeted again. A good meal is much more worth buying than this thing.",
  [21531202] = "If I really become a boss, I'll never hire anybody like me, 'cause I'm the only one knowing how good at slacking I am.",
  [21531203] = "Am I the only one who never has this kind of dream? Apart from anything else, no matter how strong a company is, it'll soon collapse if someone like me becomes its owner...",
  [21531204] = "People would never want to be a boss if they knew what it's like to be a boss. They only want to be the kind of boss in their imagination.",
  [21531301] = "The \"employees\" in it don't seem to be very professional. I don't see any grievances typical of an employee on their faces!",
  [21531302] = "There really are no services business owners can't provide, only ones you can't think of...",
  [21531303] = "This service sounds pretty nice. You get to enjoy the pleasure of being a boss without having to endure the pressure. I'll give it a try as well when I can spare the time!",
  [21531304] = "It's pretty good. Next time someone tells me I don't know how to look at things from a boss's perspective, I'll just say I've been a boss before, and it's no big deal.",
  [21531401] = "This is my first time hearing about a project like this! Where's their morality? Where's their sense of responsibility? Where's their parlor?",
  [21531402] = "Here's a joke. Our boss tried the \"One-Day Boss\" thing as well. Maybe we were so rebellious he felt under needless pressure.",
  [21531403] = "It's nice to be a boss, but you should be careful not to become addicted to it. We need to be down-to-earth to get on with our lives!",
  [21531404] = "I've tried it. The \"employees\" in there were so genial. They never argued with their boss, and they were all surprisingly nice!",
  [21532101] = "Traveling is getting boring as well. There's so much haste you just can't calm down to enjoy the pleasures of traveling.",
  [21532102] = "A piece of advice: if you're going on a tour, make sure you go with the right companion or your tour will end up torturous! I'm speaking from experience here!",
  [21532103] = "Am I the only one finding the food mentioned in the show awful? Tourists should think twice before jumping on the bandwagon.",
  [21532104] = "The souvenirs we buy always end up getting thrown away. Most of them are useless. They only make us more experienced in being swindled.",
  [21532201] = "Actually, all places are the same, but there are always people believing that the life they want is elsewhere, and they always crave faraway stuff.",
  [21532202] = "The most tiring moment during travel: posting pictures to Moments before phone IP changes.",
  [21532203] = "I loathe the special forces-style tourism that many people are recommending. On the surface, you get to experience a lot, but in fact, the only thing you feel is fatigue.",
  [21532204] = "People typically travel to escape reality, but regrettably, after the transient getaway, they always have to come back to face what they have to face.",
  [21532301] = "I've always envied those senior citizens traveling in groups. I want a life like that when I'm old too.",
  [21532302] = "When traveling, I quite often find myself torn between the ideas \"I wanna stay here forever\" and \"I wanna go home right now.\" It's so weird.",
  [21532303] = "Actually, if you don't have the luxury of going traveling, you can just tour around your city. You'll see things you've never noticed before as well.",
  [21532304] = "I really regret not having gotten myself things as keepsakes when I was traveling. It strikes me that even a mere photo would mean a lot to me.",
  [21532401] = "All the small things I got when traveling and brought back home are precious to me! They're like my charging station! Every one of them represents a beautiful time!",
  [21532402] = "I suddenly want so badly to go traveling! I wanna eat a lot of goodies! I wanna see things I've never seen before! I wanna elope with someone to the moon!",
  [21532403] = "If you travel to all places and enjoy all kinds of stuff to your heart's content when you're young, then when you get old, you'll find that you have no regrets.",
  [21532404] = "Pictures I took when traveling have covered a whole wall. My goal is to leave my footprints on every inch of the earth's surface!!!",
  [21533101] = "These lanterns are unbelievably ugly. At the exhibition, they scared my puppy, and it kept barking. I seriously doubt the judges' competence.",
  [21533102] = "It's okay for lanterns to be earthbound, but they shouldn't be scary. There's a limit to being offbeat, you know?",
  [21533103] = "Lantern contests are losing popularity by the year, and each of the lanterns they make is worse than the last. They're not worth seeing at all.",
  [21533104] = "Emmm, I can't believe they made a lantern like this the prize winner, but on the other hand, it did make us laugh and give us some fun.",
  [21533201] = "It's not as large-scale as I imagined, and the venue was rather primitive. It's not worth a trip.",
  [21533202] = "I wanna single out the organizers and criticize them. The management was a disaster. A lantern caught fire and burned some other entries.",
  [21533203] = "I got nothing special to say, but it was kind of windy on the day of the contest, and the sight of everybody braving the wind was kind of funny.",
  [21533204] = "The lanterns were nondescript, and the way they awarded the prizes was arbitrary. The organizers probably didn't put too much effort into it.",
  [21533301] = "Many lanterns in the contest were quite innovative. They lent a modern air to conventional lanterns and made my eyes light up!",
  [21533302] = "The sight of the sea of lanterns instantly made me feel like I was traveling back in time, and I suspected that hundreds of years ago, Loveland City was probably just as lively as this.",
  [21533303] = "This is my first time attending an event like this. I've never seen so many lanterns before. It's quite a spectacle!",
  [21533304] = "It surprised me that apart from lanterns, they also prepared many performances. The lantern dance impressed me the most. The dancing girls were stunning!",
  [21533401] = "In the venue!! Every lantern is gorgeous, and some of them are quite distinctive. In a word, this is a visual feast!!",
  [21533402] = "The lanterns are beautiful but not as beautiful as the people here! The girls in the venue are quite pleasing to the eye as well. Enjoy the beauty of the lanterns, guys! Wish you all the best!",
  [21533403] = "Making lanterns is a tradition in Loveland City and a symbol of feelings we can never forget. I hope these cultural elements will be passed down from generation to generation.",
  [21533404] = "I invited the one I had feelings for to enter the lantern contest with me. Though we didn't win any prizes, I feel the event brought us closer. Thank you, lantern contest!!",
  [21534101] = "The topic didn't trigger much response. Hardly any people participated in the discussion.",
  [21534201] = "What's missed is missed. I don't wanna rake up the past.",
  [21534202] = "Dwelling on your regrets is no good. It serves only to add to your vexation.",
  [21534203] = "Topic not worth discussing. No subsequent traffic support will be offered.",
  [21534401] = "If only I had said everything I wanted to say at that time. Things might not have ended any differently, but at least I'd have no regret.",
  [21534402] = "If I could do it all over again, I think I'd be willing to try a different life.",
  [21534403] = "The topic became more popular than expected. It's advisable to add some fuel to the fire.",
  [21535101] = "I seem to remember that another show once did a similar project. Is it just a coincidence?",
  [21535102] = "What a boring program. Even math classes never made me feel so drowsy...",
  [21535103] = "I thought they got something solid to offer, but after chattering for a long while, they still didn't get to the point. It's an utter waste of time!",
  [21535104] = "When did the threshold of educational shows become so low? I mean, these guys are trying to palm off the audience with stuff known to even grade school students.",
  [21535201] = "If you spent 10 minutes familiarizing yourself with this show, then congratulations; you've wasted 10 minutes of your time...",
  [21535202] = "I think they kind of over-interpreted it. If even flipping a coin has to be so complicated, then there will be no simple stuff in the world.",
  [21535203] = "I think they kind of came out at the small end of the horn. I mean, they whetted the audience's appetite at the beginning, but the answers they offered at the end were so perfunctory.",
  [21535204] = "Am I the only one who never makes decisions by flipping a coin? It just makes you look so irresponsible with your life.",
  [21535301] = "I flip a coin because I don't want to think! Why would I think so much about flipping a coin?!",
  [21535302] = "This show is as helpful to me as always. My mom asked me why I was taking notes on my knees when watching a show!",
  [21535303] = "Darn it. My head itches. I think I'm growing brains! Knowing so much doesn't keep my mind from going blank when I flip a coin.",
  [21535304] = "Would anyone really make an important decision by simply flipping a coin? I won't. I'll flip the coin many times and let the average decide.",
  [21535401] = "My lucky coin really helped me make a lot of the right choices! So I guess God does exist!",
  [21535402] = "It reminds me of the customized rubber dice I prepared for multiple-choice questions on exam papers. Put your hands up if you did the same thing!",
  [21535403] = "I simply wanted to watch a show, but some knowledge sneaked into my head in a despicable way!",
  [21535404] = "Not many people carry a coin around these days, I presume? But it's okay. I'll recommend to you guys a coin-flipping simulator. It's super handy!",
  [21536101] = "Animal lives matter, but don't human lives? Lately, there have been so many incidents in which people got injured by animals...",
  [21536102] = "Recently I've read a news report about the damage stray cats are causing to the ecological environment. I don't think animals like those deserve any sympathy.",
  [21536103] = "I don't understand, so I'll just ask. If we feed stray cats, there will be more and more of them, won't there? Is it really the right thing to do?",
  [21536104] = "I don't like irresponsible shows like this. These people appeal to your sympathy, but they don't really think.",
  [21536201] = "Lately, there have been many frauds using stray animals to trick people. Is this some kind of con game as well?",
  [21536202] = "Many animals eat better than humans do these days. If you wanna show kindness, why not show it to the children in disaster areas?",
  [21536203] = "I don't quite understand why people are being nice to animals but apathetic to humans these days.",
  [21536204] = "My neighbor's dogs are so noisy they've been giving me sleepless nights. I really can't bring myself to like dogs...",
  [21536301] = "Whoever abandons their pet animals is bound to get their comeuppance! Think twice before deciding to keep a pet, guys!",
  [21536302] = "Rationally speaking, it's indeed wrong to feed animals indiscriminately. Of course, it'll be best if you can take them to get neutered!",
  [21536303] = "Programs about stray animals are few and far between these days. I hope these piteous fluffy little creatures will get more attention.",
  [21536304] = "It's very difficult for stray animals to get unpolluted water in cities, so please offer them some clean water if you chance on them.",
  [21536401] = "Boohoo... It pains me to see that these poor little angels are still homeless. I hope they get a happy life!",
  [21536402] = "My sweetie used to be a stray as well, but now it's grown into a 13-pound meowing beast!",
  [21536403] = "There's a stray animal cafeteria in our housing estate. At least the local stray cats don't have to worry about food anymore!",
  [21536404] = "There are many cats and dogs in our school, and they're well-fed and getting really fat, but I still hope they'll get home someday.",
  [21537101] = "Efficiency-wise, working from the office is better. I don't understand why people are becoming too lazy to go outdoors...",
  [21537102] = "Whether employees get to work remotely depends on their boss. Anyway, my boss has to supervise me working.",
  [21537103] = "Staying indoors for too long rusts your mind. We need face-to-face communication from time to time.",
  [21537104] = "I don't quite understand the pros of working from home. Maybe staying indoors 24/7 makes rent more worthwhile...",
  [21537201] = "I think the workplace atmosphere is necessary. Working from home entails too many temptations, and they keep you from staying focused!",
  [21537202] = "Am I the only one feeling that working from home is worse than working from the office? I mean, there should be a boundary between work and life.",
  [21537203] = "They exaggerated the pros of working from home in the show. Actually, only by working from the office can you find the pleasure of slacking off.",
  [21537204] = "Why should I pay extra electricity bills to work for the boss? In no circumstance will I bring home any work that can be finished in the workplace!",
  [21537301] = "Working remotely is perfect for people with social phobia. They won't have to read their colleagues' faces anymore, 'cause they won't have to see them.",
  [21537302] = "As a service worker, I really envy those people, 'cause people like me have to serve customers face-to-face. Maybe I should consider changing my job and switching to the online service industry.",
  [21537303] = "Current state of people working remotely: appear unemployed most of the time; hardly dare to sleep before the deadline.",
  [21537304] = "I told my boss I wanted to work from home, and he asked me if I meant I wanted to carry home the bricks I was supposed to transfer...",
  [21537401] = "I can't imagine how happy I'll be if I don't have to punch in on a daily basis! I hope that day will come soon!",
  [21537402] = "I've been working from home for a year now! It feels like I'm living in a dream, and life has become enjoyable again!",
  [21537403] = "I've been working from home due to my leg injury for two months. Now I've recovered, but I find myself completely unwilling to go back to the workplace...",
  [21537404] = "Thank you, sci-tech! Sci-tech makes my life better! It's so cool not to have to go to work!",
  [21538101] = "Am I the only one finding those things ugly? The handiest tools are the simplest and plainest ones. The flashy exterior is totally unnecessary.",
  [21538102] = "I finally know why today's kids are having trouble focusing on their studies. These things are unbelievably detrimental.",
  [21538103] = "So underachievers do carry more stationery. It's said a top student keeps only two pens in their pocket.",
  [21538104] = "It's just a marketing gimmick of businesspeople coveting the money in students' wallets. Showmakers should really stop publicizing this kind of despicable practice.",
  [21538201] = "Times have changed, and the stationery we used to be familiar with has turned into stuff we don't recognize after all...",
  [21538202] = "Some stationery became less handy instead. Attractive appearance needs to be combined with practicality.",
  [21538203] = "I think I saw this \"Sitting-Position Pen\" thing ten years ago. I can't believe they're publicizing it again and calling it innovative.",
  [21538204] = "It's good-looking but of low quality. Don't ask me how I know. Do you know how it feels to have the tip of your pen fly off your desk when doing homework?",
  [21538301] = "Darn it! There's no way I'm allowing such stationery to hit the shelves! Because there was no such thing around when I was little!",
  [21538302] = "Wow! They got so many school supplies I've never seen before! Can a student tell me if they're real?",
  [21538303] = "Watching the show makes me wanna buy some of those things, but on second thought, I don't really have any use for them.",
  [21538304] = "At last, I get to lecture my kids by saying \"We didn't get to have these when we were little\" as my parents did to me so often!",
  [21538401] = "Many of the school supplies are too childish for grade school students to have. They're perfect for adults, though!",
  [21538402] = "I don't really need those things, but I'm tempted anyway! They're virtually my ultimate childhood dream!",
  [21538403] = "If someday I have a son, I'll definitely buy these things for him and make him the coolest boy in his class!",
  [21538404] = "Many of the products are pretty imaginative. I can't help admiring their designers' fertile imagination.",
  [21539101] = "The interview received middling reviews and didn't attract much attention.",
  [21539201] = "Looks like people still hold many misconceptions about journalism...",
  [21539202] = "Compared with the thriving personal media, conventional news media does seem to have outlived its usefulness.",
  [21539203] = "The show is well-meant, but it can't improve ratings.",
  [21539401] = "It's never occupation that's great. It's the people working hard in their positions.",
  [21539402] = "Hats off to those honorable journalists! We'll blaze a trail in journalism as well.",
  [21539403] = "You don't have to be in the spotlight to be a hero. The view count has said everything.",
  [21540101] = "When watching the beginning of it, I thought it was a suspenseful show. I didn't know it had such a hilarious ending...",
  [21540102] = "It's a typical bad-movie gimmick. I thought only movie makers used this trick. It never crossed my mind newspeople would use it as well.",
  [21540103] = "The show's crew seems desperate for high ratings. There are not that many urban rumors. Some people are making it look like there are.",
  [21540104] = "Is there still anything trustworthy? I excitedly clicked this link, and all I got to see was this?",
  [21540201] = "I guessed the ending when I saw the beginning. TV shows are so cliched these days.",
  [21540202] = "How come I've never heard of this rumor before? I think the show's crew made the whole thing up.",
  [21540203] = "Would anyone really believe these absurd rumors? Don't forget that animals are not allowed to become supernatural creatures in Loveland City!",
  [21540204] = "Actually, what you guys can find out might not necessarily be the truth. This is all I have to say. You can figure out the rest by yourself.",
  [21540301] = "This matter is proof enough that a lie if repeated often enough, will be accepted as truth. Maybe all those urban rumors were started this way.",
  [21540302] = "Thumbs-up to the show's crew's meticulous and scientific attitude, despite the surprising results...",
  [21540303] = "I watched the whole show with my eyes partially obscured by my hands. I was both scared and fascinated. Fortunately, there's no ghost in the footage.",
  [21540304] = "It never occurred to me the frail-looking journalist girl was so daring. Hats off to her!",
  [21540401] = "At last, a show revealed the truth of this matter! I was so frightened I stayed indoors for several days!",
  [21540402] = "Old people's tales tell us that if you encounter \"another you\" and they ask you strange questions, make sure not to answer them!",
  [21540403] = "What a surprising ending! But it also tells us there's nothing supernatural in the world.",
  [21540404] = "I've experienced it! It scared me witless, but when I found out the truth, I didn't know whether I should laugh or cry.",
  [21541101] = "I can't imagine what our world will be like in the future. Will we see groups of people wearing VR goggles run amok on the street?",
  [21541102] = "If there's a virtual world where everything's perfect, who would care about the real world?",
  [21541103] = "I'm not looking forward to it. Nobody knows what's on the other side of this sci-tech door.",
  [21541104] = "This can hardly be called a surprise. They've been researching this for so many years. It's about time they achieved something.",
  [21541201] = "I suddenly feel it's kind of scary. If we could switch between reality and virtual reality at will, would we be able to differentiate them?",
  [21541202] = "Virtual reality will always be virtual. It's okay to use it for fun, but we mustn't become obsessed with it.",
  [21541203] = "Darn it. I got the sense that the plot of The Matrix is about to happen in the real world...",
  [21541204] = "I can answer for it that there are still many practical problems to solve, so don't get your hopes up.",
  [21541301] = "Science and technology are indeed developing faster than we imagine. The world depicted in sci-fi movies is not that futuristic anymore.",
  [21541302] = "I've always thought this kind of high-end technology is nothing but a vague concept. Is it really going to come true?",
  [21541303] = "Apart from games, this technology can also be applied to many other things, which will radically change our lives!",
  [21541304] = "I'm grateful to the show for the knowledge it taught me. Science is really miraculous. It can give us everything we want.",
  [21541401] = "Holographic simulation games are so cool. I've been looking forward to them for a long time. I can't wait for us to meet in another world!",
  [21541402] = "Have you guys ever thought of the blood-curdling possibility that the world we live in is actually virtual?",
  [21541403] = "I'm getting holographic-online-game-novel vibes right now! It never crossed my mind that someday I'd get to see the world depicted in fiction!",
  [21541404] = "If this technological barrier is broken, will we be able to go anywhere we want?",
  [21542101] = "Was it really just an energy burst? I can't shake the feeling that the authority's keeping something back from us.",
  [21542102] = "I don't know what to say. The populace has been tolerant enough toward Evolvers.",
  [21542103] = "Those Evolvers are too dangerous. They're like bombs that can detonate at any moment. I'll stay as far away from them as I can.",
  [21542104] = "Would it kill them to put more details in their reports? They told us nothing except when and where it happened.",
  [21542201] = "Having caused an incident like that, the Evolver will probably be expelled from the company.",
  [21542202] = "Did that really happen? I don't see any reports on any other platform. I hope it's not misinformation...",
  [21542203] = "Yet another Evolver incident. Would it kill them to get a grip on themselves and stop causing trouble to normal people?",
  [21542204] = "Such incidents are getting increasingly frequent. Does our world still have a future?",
  [21542301] = "It's regrettable to have to see such news early in the morning. I hope nobody got hurt...",
  [21542302] = "Was it a chance event or premeditated? They must ascertain the truth!",
  [21542303] = "This company strikes me as shady as well. What does it do? How come I've never heard of it before?",
  [21542304] = "It's said energy undulation spread to every corner of the building. Some people mistakenly believed there was an earthquake.",
  [21542401] = "That was so dangerous! Fortunately, the situation was tackled in a timely manner. I hope there're no casualties...",
  [21542402] = "I was nearby at that time. The Special Task Force responded immediately. It makes me feel really safe!",
  [21542403] = "There seem to have been several similar incidents lately. Make sure to keep your guard up when you're out there, everybody!",
  [21542404] = "Latest news: the situation has been brought under control, and nobody got hurt. Let's try to be more understanding and tolerant.",
  [21543101] = "I'm not bothered. So long as I got nothing but walls at home, my house will never catch fire.",
  [21543102] = "Is it really that difficult to make an educational video interesting? My school made me come here to watch it.",
  [21543103] = "The video's too short, and I feel there's so much more knowledge it should've included. Even I know more about the subject.",
  [21543104] = "There are several goofs, which means the filming was taken lightly...",
  [21543201] = "I found multiple incorrect demonstrations in the video. An educational video supposed to be a lifesaver in certain circumstances shouldn't have included so many flaws in it.",
  [21543202] = "The fire exit in my apartment building is blocked by sundries. I don't dare imagine what will happen if there's a fire.",
  [21543203] = "Take enough precautions and nothing will go wrong, so stop being a worrywart.",
  [21543204] = "If the fire's small, you don't need to run; if it's big, you won't be able to outrun it. It's all for a psychological placebo...",
  [21543301] = "I once watched a video of an actual fire. The chance to escape could be really fleeting! Never take fire safety lightly!",
  [21543302] = "Watching the video makes me feel I need to keep a fire extinguisher in my house and have a smoke detector installed.",
  [21543303] = "Thanks for the tips. I think they should include this in a grade school textbook. It's very practically useful.",
  [21543304] = "I got a great awareness of security, and after watching the video, I bought another batch of fire safety equipment.",
  [21543401] = "Make sure to follow the fire safety rules, everybody! Whoever experienced an actual fire knows that a fire exit is a lifesaver!",
  [21543402] = "Following the fire door rules is being responsible for your life and property. Do not take any chances!",
  [21543403] = "I'm going to learn some fire prevention knowledge too. It really can be helpful at a crucial juncture!",
  [21543404] = "I shared it to my family chat group. This is the kind of stuff I'd call useful and worth Favoriting and sharing!",
  [21544101] = "The audience criticized the show as scripted, and the ratings plummeted.",
  [21544201] = "Having watched this show is the kind of fate I want most to change.",
  [21544202] = "What a terrible viewing experience. Their script is lamer than those foreign psychic shows.",
  [21544203] = "Facts prove that many con games are conducted under the guise of psychology.",
  [21544401] = "Never thought fate could be verified in this way. It opened the gate to a new world for me!",
  [21544402] = "For a moment, I really felt that a deity had come to the show!",
  [21544403] = "Seeking the future in psychology... You guys have made it happen.",
  [21545101] = "How is this any different from the detectives I know? Please do not imagine what the audience imagines.",
  [21545102] = "These days many detectives are unbelievably unethical and snoop on their clients. They're unworthy of this.",
  [21545103] = "I don't know what this show is about. A boring day of a detective?",
  [21545104] = "I fell asleep halfway through the video. Boring shows like this are few and far between these days.",
  [21545201] = "They're kind of being one-sided. As far as I know, not all detectives are like this.",
  [21545202] = "Ironically, the show just turned the usual stereotype of detectives into another stereotype.",
  [21545203] = "The show's such a disappointment. Gimme back the handsome detective in my mind's eye!",
  [21545204] = "I felt like I watched a domestic detective movie, a really lame one...",
  [21545301] = "Detectives are actually maintaining justice and peace in their own ways.",
  [21545302] = "Real detective work is quite cognitively complex. I really admire those working as detectives.",
  [21545303] = "Though he's not as handsome as I imagined, at least I got a more vivid image of detectives in my mind now.",
  [21545304] = "Like people, an occupation needs to be looked at from many different perspectives. I'm grateful to the show for showing us what detectives are like when seen from different perspectives.",
  [21545401] = "Reality is always more exciting than movies and TV dramas. Detectives are no exception!",
  [21545402] = "I love the scene of the detective bickering with his colleagues. It makes them look like a team!",
  [21545403] = "It's the kind of detective's life I've never imagined. When he fished out all kinds of little props, I was astounded!",
  [21545404] = "The show always offers something funny when I least expect it. A very interesting program!",
  [21546101] = "I've lost count of how many lame movies this director has directed. The mere sight of this name makes me lose interest.",
  [21546102] = "They had the nerve to try to evoke nostalgia in the viewers when they couldn't even get their story straight. It's disgusting.",
  [21546103] = "This is literally the most boring movie I've seen this year...",
  [21546104] = "I cried after watching this movie, not because the plot was touching but because the money I spent on the ticket was wasted.",
  [21546201] = "This is my first time finding a movie so boring I can't even bring myself to finish the narrative version of it. I think I'll pass on this.",
  [21546202] = "Let me recommend another movie about food to you guys. Comparison can cause the greatest harm. It's a lot better than this one.",
  [21546203] = "I thought crawfish were unhealthy food. Why are they so popular?",
  [21546204] = "The ending makes me feel like my hot pot is taken away when I'm enjoying it...",
  [21546301] = "Crawfish is really a temptation hard to resist! Watching this movie makes my mouth water!",
  [21546302] = "Food movies with a good plot like this one are something of a rarity these days. Its ending is a bit hasty though.",
  [21546303] = "Nothing gets on my nerves more than when my favorite actor co-stars with my least favorite actress. Luckily, the plot is not too bad.",
  [21546304] = "The movie glows with life. It reminds me of my favorite food stall in my childhood.",
  [21546401] = "Watching this movie actually made me feel hungry. I'll make sure to treat myself to a crawfish hot pot tomorrow!",
  [21546402] = "I'm really impressed by the knife work of the cook in the movie. I thought this kind of scene existed only in manga!",
  [21546403] = "Halfway through the movie, tears trickled from the corners of my mouth...",
  [21546404] = "I hereby declare I've personally selected this movie as the best movie this year for making meals appetizing!",
  [21547101] = "I've had enough of these memetic expressions. They call everything bug-exploiting when it's actually just low cunning.",
  [21547102] = "There are so many confusing terms on the Internet these days. Will someone please tell me what this word means?",
  [21547103] = "Maybe different people have different concepts of bug-exploiting. I don't get why the showmaker thinks this is funny.",
  [21547104] = "Sometimes overdoing the humor part serves only to have the opposite effect. This is a little advice I'm giving to the show's crew.",
  [21547201] = "I've seen many of the jokes in other shows, which is why they're no longer funny to me.",
  [21547202] = "Many of the so-called \"bugs\" are just lapses in memory. They're not worth studying.",
  [21547203] = "Compared with blindly pursuing hot topics, I'm more inclined to spend my time on more rewarding topics.",
  [21547204] = "The recent shows are so similar to each other. You can never make a good show through imitation.",
  [21547301] = "I can't shake the feeling that our dreams are bugs of life. Some things we see in our dreams happen in real life too.",
  [21547302] = "Let me tell you a secret bug. If you wanna go somewhere, carry a ladder and pose as a repairman, and nobody will try to stop you!",
  [21547303] = "I don't know if you guys have ever felt it this way, but the existence of mankind is a bug in this world!",
  [21547304] = "Please don't imitate any of the actions in the show. If you try to exploit a bug in real life, you might \"get your account blocked.\"",
  [21547401] = "Who can say no to watching a stupid show after work? I hope there'll be a new release soon!",
  [21547402] = "The biggest bug I've encountered: I slept for only another few minutes after my alarm clock went off, but I woke up to find two hours had passed!",
  [21547403] = "Do any of you understand this, sisters? My bestie and I each found a part-time job during the summer vacation. She puts up flyers, and I clean them. We're a perfect team!",
  [21547404] = "Many shots in the video are so Otomads! But I love them! Please gimme more!",
  [21548101] = "Given how lame the PV is, it's safe to say the game is a boring one.",
  [21548102] = "I'm speechless. Are they sure they're publicizing their product, not defaming it? They should've given it a bigger budget.",
  [21548103] = "I don't know what to say about this video. It has this beauty that makes me feel like I sat up in bed too fast in the morning and nearly blacked out...",
  [21548104] = "??? Is it you, Odyssey? Blink if you're abducted.",
  [21548201] = "I waited a year, and this is what I got? Please leave my world with your PV, Odyssey.",
  [21548202] = "I was kind of looking forward to it. These people really know how to deter gamers with promo videos.",
  [21548203] = "It's okay for hype videos to be creative, but they're not supposed to kill potential players' enthusiasm. I hope all gaming companies can understand this.",
  [21548204] = "Having watched the video, I just wanna ask one question: were the team who made this PV secretly working for a rival gaming company?",
  [21548301] = "I was uninterested in this game, but this video gave me a sudden urge to try it.",
  [21548302] = "The launch date was postponed by a long time, and I decided to give up on it, but after watching the PV, I found myself eager to play it again!",
  [21548303] = "You see that hands-on video? The image quality is stunning! And the stages seem really fun!",
  [21548304] = "My classmate recommended it to me multiple times, but I was uninterested. Today, having watched the video, I found myself fascinated by it. I hope my classmates won't beat me up.",
  [21548401] = "I'm very displeased with this game, 'cause it's kept me waiting for too long. I'll get vindictive unless they offer me enough in-game perks!",
  [21548402] = "I can't stand it anymore! A stupid question I ask daily: is this the day of Odyssey's public test? If not, I'll come back tomorrow!",
  [21548403] = "I warn you, Odyssey. Get online right now if you know what's good for you!",
  [21548404] = "Now this is what we call our dream game! I, a college student, hereby profess my hunger to play it, with my real name attached below!",
  [21549101] = "Contestants of both sides made thoughtless remarks, which greatly jeopardized the enjoyability of the event.",
  [21549201] = "It seems neither side did any in-depth research on AI technology.",
  [21549202] = "A debate competition without any tension is not a successful one.",
  [21549203] = "I'd rather watch a movie at home than waste my time here.",
  [21549401] = "A wonderful contest. It makes me think more about the boundaries of AI technology.",
  [21549402] = "This is the best debate competition I've watched lately! It gives me an urge to become a contestant myself!",
  [21549403] = "Contestants of both sides are surprisingly imaginative! I didn't know a debate competition could be as wonderful as a good movie.",
  [21550101] = "No wonder the traffic's been so heavy lately. It's affecting regular citizens' lives.",
  [21550102] = "Not everybody is a rock fan. Some people need to dial it down a bit...",
  [21550103] = "I don't know why anybody would listen to people yelling. It's sheer noise!",
  [21550104] = "Some singers are so despicable and I can't understand why so many people like them. It's an utter insult to rock music.",
  [21550201] = "I knew their camera would focus on those popular bands. Would it kill them to give a chance to niche singers?",
  [21550202] = "Some bands are much better at buying topic popularity for marketing purposes than they are at music...",
  [21550203] = "Having the spirit of rock music is a good thing, but isn't it about time someone fixed the noise problem?",
  [21550204] = "Be that as it may, shouldn't they at least tell us how much longer the music festival will be postponed?",
  [21550301] = "No matter what, a band that still stages pro bone roadside shows these days is definitely enthusiastic enough.",
  [21550302] = "I can almost see how electrifying the music festival will be on that day. I'm beginning to look forward to it!",
  [21550303] = "I got to know many good bands in the event, and my playlist is now almost full.",
  [21550304] = "I'm not a rock fan, but the atmosphere still infected me. Maybe I'll try to learn more about it.",
  [21550401] = "This is what music should be like! Our youth will never end so long as there's rock!",
  [21550402] = "I was deeply touched by the show, and I'm grateful to these bands for showing me the meaning of \"Rock forever.\"",
  [21550403] = "It's true what they say: youth is priceless! I actually got to enjoy a live-house show in front of the office building of my company!",
  [21550404] = "I've been a rock fan for many years, and the show brought tears to my eyes! The best era of our own has finally arrived!",
  [21551101] = "Nowadays each new game is more boring than the last. None of the game designers seems to be serious about their work anymore.",
  [21551102] = "The launch of this game was delayed for so long before its open beta test. Are there really people wanting to play it?",
  [21551103] = "The image quality makes me feel like I'm playing a 10-year-old game. Are they sure this game is ready for an open beta test?",
  [21551104] = "I wonder how much money they've invested in the advertising of this game. I mean, it's basically everywhere...",
  [21551201] = "It's too time-consuming for my liking. I think I'll try looking for a more casual game...",
  [21551202] = "The texture of the graphics is pretty good, but it's not gamy enough, or maybe I just had unduly high expectations of it.",
  [21551203] = "So this is what they give us after such a long wait? Maybe they spent their entire budget on publicity.",
  [21551204] = "Why didn't they hire a more professional vlogger for the game test? Such a performance is beyond lame...",
  [21551301] = "An excellent test. I've decided to jump on the bandwagon after watching it.",
  [21551302] = "I discovered a great game. Come and play it with me! @Hempflower",
  [21551303] = "Can I play it on my computer? I really wanna play it but I don't have the required device QAQ...",
  [21551304] = "It looks fun but also seems too difficult. Waiting online for a knowbie to power-level me!",
  [21551401] = "There you are! I wanna play this game right here, right now! Please don't be an ingrate!",
  [21551402] = "If you're also a player of Odyssey, then we're siblings who have never met!",
  [21551403] = "I'll recommend this amazing game to everybody! You won't regret buying it. Odyssey is worth every penny!",
  [21551404] = "Is this the day of the open beta test of Odyssey? Oh, it's not. Well, I'll come back and ask again tomorrow.",
  [21552101] = "I opened this post expecting to get some inside scoop, but it's an utter click-bait title.",
  [21552102] = "I have bad vibes about companies that came out of nowhere. They strike me as incompetent.",
  [21552103] = "I once bought a product of this company, and it was just average. I won't buy anything else made by them.",
  [21552104] = "The crew of the show is sparing no effort to publicize the game. Are they paid to do that?",
  [21552201] = "I got the sense that this company always belittle their competitors in their marketing campaigns. I don't like it when they do that...",
  [21552202] = "If you knew who's supporting this company behind the scenes, you wouldn't have found this surprising.",
  [21552203] = "I can't shake the feeling that they're trying to build an image of an Insta-famous company for themselves. They should focus on improving their skills if they wanna achieve more.",
  [21552204] = "How influential this company has become lately is undeniable, but when it comes to the number of patents and their true value, well, anybody in the industry knows the truth.",
  [21552301] = "All recent hit tech products seem to be from this company. Looks like they really know their stuff.",
  [21552302] = "After learning the perks this company offers its employees, I began to regret not having studied harder.",
  [21552303] = "Isn't this my dream workplace? I'm gonna send my resume to them!",
  [21552304] = "I suddenly noticed that several of the mini-apps I've been using were developed by this company! Respect!",
  [21552401] = "Have you noticed that lately, even the competition between tech companies has begun to intensify? It's okay. The more intense, the better! I hope they'll fight each other!",
  [21552402] = "Lately, I've replaced all my electronic devices with Infinite products. They're very handy, and they'd be even better if their prices drop a little.",
  [21552403] = "Never thought I'd learn about this company in this way. The food in their canteen looks really good!",
  [21552404] = "The chip they've invented lately is really awesome. I'm using it already. You got my support, domestic products!",
  [21553101] = "Listening to the awkward conversation between these guests distresses me more than working in front of my superior.",
  [21553102] = "I know they wanna make the talk more profound, but they should've taken into consideration how the general audience felt about it...",
  [21553103] = "Right now I don't feel like conversing with the future. I just wanna go back in time 20 minutes and tell myself not to watch this program!",
  [21553104] = "It strikes me that compared with these experts in different fields, children's imagination would probably make this show more interesting.",
  [21553201] = "Our world might not necessarily become better in the future. I think we should just live in the present.",
  [21553202] = "The conversation makes me feel drowsy. This kind of talk show does require more interesting souls.",
  [21553203] = "Though it's just imagination, they shouldn't overdo it. I feel that they're making things up in order to create memes.",
  [21553204] = "It sounds absurd. What if the end of the world comes sooner than they predicted?",
  [21553301] = "I can't even imagine what I should eat in two hours, let alone the future world...",
  [21553302] = "A very interesting show. I couldn't help smiling when I heard an opinion I also had.",
  [21553303] = "My greatest wish is for the future world to be free of illness and disaster.",
  [21553304] = "I wonder if many years ago there were also a group of people imagining life in the age we're now in.",
  [21553401] = "All the guests have so many good jokes to share! Before clicking this video, I thought it'd be a serious program, but when I finished watching it, my stomach hurt from laughing...",
  [21553402] = "I feel like I've opened up a whole new world! I'm indeed too unimaginative!",
  [21553403] = "I hope the footage of this show will be preserved for 100 years so that people will know if any of the predictions eventually come true!",
  [21553404] = "The experts' imagination is really admirable. I wish all you guys' wishes would be fulfilled!",
  [21554101] = "Many of the shared songs proved not worth recommending, which sparked a storm of bad reviews online.",
  [21554201] = "I'd rather work overtime than listen to these songs.",
  [21554202] = "Today's youngsters' taste in music really concerns me.",
  [21554203] = "There are reasons why some songs' play counts remain low.",
  [21554401] = "Little-known amazing songs discovered! I can't stop favoriting them!",
  [21554402] = "What makes this show matter something is that it brings some excellent but niche musicians into the light.",
  [21554403] = "Many songs went viral after the show aired, as shown by the streaming numbers on music platforms.",
  [21555101] = "They exaggerated it in the show. It's actually dirty, messy and lousy. Go see for yourself. It'll make you speechless!",
  [21555102] = "Many open-air markets have become embroiled in rigged scale scandals. Are there serious people still daring to go to those places?",
  [21555103] = "It used to be pretty good, but lately, a lot of influencers have gone there to make videos for exposure. It's unbelievable.",
  [21555104] = "Please stop publicizing it, media companies. I'm begging you. A lot of the stalls offering discounts are overcrowded now...",
  [21555201] = "The reporters interviewing these stall owners seem a bit uncouth. They even littered right in front of the camera...",
  [21555202] = "The mere sight of crowded places like this makes me dizzy. Can anybody really stand being in there?",
  [21555203] = "This place has become an Insta-famous go-to destination. I can't even buy sugar-coated haws without waiting in line.",
  [21555204] = "They were so friendly only because you guys were carrying a camera. That's not their usual attitude to customers.",
  [21555301] = "Open-air markets seem to be more interesting than I imagined. I'll go check them out when I get the chance.",
  [21555302] = "Regrettably, the crew of the show did the filming in the daytime. Actually, the place is more fun at night.",
  [21555303] = "I'd recommend the open-air market in the west of the city. The fried cakes in there are divine. I can eat six of them in a row!",
  [21555304] = "It's been a long time since I last went to a busy market like this. Watching this show makes me feel like I traveled back in time to my childhood.",
  [21555401] = "Is there anybody who loves wandering in this kind of market as I do? It always seems to brighten up my day!",
  [21555402] = "Isn't it the one near my home? Things in there are insanely cheap, and you can even play cards in it!",
  [21555403] = "Everybody in the market looks so carefree. That's how you enjoy your life!",
  [21555404] = "Online shopping has lost its appeal for me ever since this kind of market appeared. I feel tempted to go there whenever I can spare the time.",
  [21556101] = "Nowadays many so-called sightseeing ships are terrible. The food is awful and you can easily get seasick. Don't ask me how I know.",
  [21556102] = "Someone definitely paid them to make this show. There's no way I'm letting them swindle me!",
  [21556103] = "Are sightseeing boats really as boring as the show says they are? I was thinking of giving it a try, but now I've dropped the idea.",
  [21556104] = "The food on the ship looks so unappetizing, but the guest has to pretend otherwise and praise it. I feel sorry for him.",
  [21556201] = "As someone prone to seasickness, I find it confusing. The mere sight of the scenes in the show makes me feel dizzy...",
  [21556202] = "I'm really tempted to quit now, guys. The novelty kept me going for an hour, but after it wore off, I just stayed still at a loss for what to do.",
  [21556203] = "I was on that sightseeing ship once. Many of the recreational services and drinks required additional payment. It's daylight robbery!",
  [21556204] = "It looks pretty good. If any of you have tried it, please tell me its price to disillusion me.",
  [21556301] = "Why didn't I think of it? I'll go for this one the next time I go out to play. Let me mark it first!",
  [21556302] = "Enjoying sceneries and music from aboard a pleasure ship sounds pretty romantic, but I wonder how much it'll cost.",
  [21556303] = "Does anybody know if it's safe? I can't swim, but I feel tempted after watching the video.",
  [21556304] = "I happen to be having trouble deciding where to party with my friends this month. Chartering a pleasure ship sounds like a pretty good choice.",
  [21556401] = "Buy a single ticket and get unlimited access to all the facilities and so much good food? I don't believe it unless you say Loveland citizens don't lie to Loveland citizens!",
  [21556402] = "How did you know I was planning a tour? The big data really does leave us with no privacy!",
  [21556403] = "This kind of pleasure boat is really impossible to say no to! And there's so much food on it! I'm gonna try it again when I get the chance!",
  [21556404] = "Producer of the show, my wallet is empty now! Why are you still enticing me like this?",
  [21557101] = "It's downright alarmist! I made some predictions through the methods taught in the show, but none of them was accurate!",
  [21557102] = "Isn't this kind of stuff in grade school textbooks? They seriously made a show out of it?",
  [21557103] = "I used to be a big fan of your show, but now it's getting increasingly childish. What a disappointment.",
  [21557104] = "Would you please get us another expert? This one looks so shifty and like a fraud!",
  [21557201] = "Forecasting the weather through clouds... Well, it's only a kind of reference. Maybe you'll get it right if you're lucky enough.",
  [21557202] = "I can't believe that even in 2023 there are still people disseminating pseudoscience. I've reported this.",
  [21557203] = "Well said, but I prefer to watch the weather forecast...",
  [21557204] = "I feel that science shows should disseminate more practical stuff instead of such unrealistic things.",
  [21557301] = "It really can be used to make accurate predictions of future weather? Well, I've got to impress my friends with it, haha!",
  [21557302] = "I've been a cloud-gazer since my childhood, and now I got one more reason to gaze at the clouds. I'm so happy!",
  [21557303] = "This show is really useful. I feel that I discovered the secrets of the cloud by accident!",
  [21557304] = "A science show with much childlike interest. It's perfect for 300-month-old kids like me.",
  [21557401] = "I saw a super-cute cloud on my way home from work today. It looked like a large chicken drumstick!",
  [21557402] = "Does nobody feel that it's super romantic to see the clouds with your significant other? You also get to predict the weather while you're at it. Perfect!",
  [21557403] = "Ever since I learned how to predict weather through the clouds, I've never had to watch the weather report again. How very smart I am!",
  [21557404] = "The seemingly inaccessible clouds actually have so much to tell us. It would seem everything in the world has an adorable side.",
  [21558101] = "Their newness is just temporary. I bet it won't be long before they return to normal.",
  [21558102] = "A failed revamp. I don't see a shred of practicality.",
  [21558103] = "The insinuation of inadequate budget that the show is riddled with discomforts me. They should drop the idea of revamping if they don't have enough money.",
  [21558104] = "Am I the only one feeling that the revamp made them even uglier? They look inexplicably out of place.",
  [21558201] = "I think they should hire a more professional designer. Such nonsensical changes are ridiculous.",
  [21558202] = "They're barely different from before the revamp, except that they look a bit cleaner.",
  [21558203] = "Isn't this a waste of time? Does this world have nothing better for you guys to do?",
  [21558204] = "...I don't respect it or understand it or wanna comment on it. I hope the crew of the show know what they're doing.",
  [21558301] = "Turning a discarded factory building into something like this was no easy job. Thumbs-up to the crew of the show.",
  [21558302] = "Proper maintenance is just as important as the revamp. I hope the involved departments will do their jobs so that the efforts of the show crew will not go to waste.",
  [21558303] = "Such a revamp really means a lot. I'm honored to bear witness to the process of it.",
  [21558304] = "It's about time I revamped my old houses. I owe the show thanks for granting me the motivation!",
  [21558401] = "You've got to be kidding me. The show crew did it for real! I was actually touched when I saw the fruit of their work!",
  [21558402] = "Forgive me for snickering at the sight of the guests laboring around. It's really fun to watch other people working!",
  [21558403] = "It's nothing short of a miracle! I can't find the right words to describe it! The crew of the show are awesome!",
  [21558404] = "Can anybody tell me if it's the same place? I can't believe it!",
  [21559101] = "The drill was a total mess. It failed to generate the effects described in the publicity campaign.",
  [21559201] = "My teacher says that a drill is a serious matter, but now it seems that's not the case.",
  [21559202] = "A farce, a complete waste of time.",
  [21559203] = "This kind of show is far below the broadcasting standards of our station. I think we should shelve the matter of cooperation until next time.",
  [21559401] = "I learned a lot of useful knowledge. I'll tell my parents about it when I get back.",
  [21559402] = "If everybody sees this show, rescuing people from disasters will probably be much easier.",
  [21559403] = "The publicity campaign proved surprisingly fruitful. Make immediate arrangements for the show to air.",
  [21560101] = "Many business owners put the tag \"Winter Exclusive\" on their old products and then double the prices. What a bunch of profiteers!",
  [21560102] = "I never go to those so-called \"Insta-famous restaurants.\" The food is awful, and you have to wait in line to get it.",
  [21560103] = "I went to this shop only days ago. It was an utter disappointment. Don't let their ads fool you, guys.",
  [21560104] = "In my eyes, roast glutinous rice cake is the only winter-exclusive food. All other foods are ineligible for the title!",
  [21560201] = "Yesterday I saw a winter-exclusive ice cream shop by the roadside. It's utterly insane!",
  [21560202] = "There are exclusive foods available throughout the year. Business owners only care about money and they don't give a damn what season it is!",
  [21560203] = "Please stop peppering me with ads about good food like this. It's a real torment 'cause I'm watching my weight.",
  [21560204] = "Winter-exclusive foods are just hot pots or super sweet stuff. It's clichéd. Drinking hot water is a better choice.",
  [21560301] = "This show makes viewers feel hungry. I was so touched tears trickled out of the corners of my mouth...",
  [21560302] = "Before watching it: I don't believe there's any food that can tempt me. After watching it: I want that! I want that! I want that!",
  [21560303] = "I can almost smell the aroma from behind the screen. Winter is all about enjoying good food!",
  [21560304] = "I want every detail of these foods sent to me within 3 minutes! And I'm not asking!",
  [21560401] = "I'd like to recommend an amazing dessert shop. The winter-exclusive Snowman Cakes are matchless! Try it and you'll know what I mean!",
  [21560402] = "In winter, without hot cocoa, I'll be as lifeless as a pack of instant noodles without a flavor packet.",
  [21560403] = "There are so many good foods about winter: sugar-coated haws on a stick, sugar roasted chestnuts, roast sweet potatoes, hot milky tea...",
  [21560404] = "Having seen this leaves me no choice. I'll pick a lucky weekend at random to give it a try!",
  [21561101] = "It's false, false, false! Important stuff needs to be repeated thrice! I tried it when I got back, and it was utterly useless!",
  [21561102] = "This is just a very new way of marketing. Don't think I can't tell you people are advertising!",
  [21561103] = "What the heck? The pictures used for the comparison have obviously been photoshopped. I would change my surname to yours if that thing was really that effective.",
  [21561104] = "There are really people believing this? Well, their cerebellum must've become vestigial from overuse of the Internet.",
  [21561201] = "Don't they think it's not right to fool the audience this way? There's nothing producers of shows won't say to sell their goods.",
  [21561202] = "Okay, okay. Next, you'll send a link of the shopping cart, right?",
  [21561203] = "If these things are such good cleansers, what's the point of having laundry detergent?",
  [21561204] = "Whoever buys it will regret it. It's not as effective as they say it is in the show...",
  [21561301] = "It's indeed kind of effective, but if you don't have any in your house, there's no need to go out especially to buy some. This is just a sort of recycling, anyway.",
  [21561302] = "If I had found this video sooner, I wouldn't have had to go home to change clothes because of a mere coffee stain.",
  [21561303] = "Now this is the kind of useful show that we really need. I'll stay tuned for more.",
  [21561304] = "I wanna know if it helps to add some of that when doing laundry in a normal way. It looks pretty effective in the show.",
  [21561401] = "I can't believe the secret cleaning method I've been keeping for so many years has been divulged like that! Darn it!",
  [21561402] = "Actually, it's all about the application of a principle of chemistry. I don't know any details, because I made it up.",
  [21561403] = "Miraculous! The stains are really gone! Will I never have to worry about staining my clothes anymore?",
  [21561404] = "I'll try it when I get home! This better not be a lie, producer of this show!",
  [21562101] = "Am I the only one who hates snow? The coldness, wetness, and slow traffic it causes are really annoying!",
  [21562102] = "Workers don't have time to be sentimental about the weather. We have to go to work, no matter how heavy the snow is.",
  [21562103] = "Sappy remarks like \"traveling together amid the snow betokens being together till your hair whitens\" are really annoying. Please call me the master of anti-sappiness!",
  [21562104] = "I'm not at all in the mood for snowscape. Is your bed not warm enough?",
  [21562201] = "The brats in the neighborhood ruined the snowman I made. There's nothing good about snowy weather.",
  [21562202] = "Why is everybody acting like a litterateur after the snow? Am I on the wrong set?",
  [21562203] = "Snow has come, but the one promising to see it with me has gone...",
  [21562204] = "I regret having forgotten to eat dumplings on the first day of winter. The weather is literally freezing my ears off.",
  [21562301] = "The moment I walked out, I spotted a couple of cute snow ducks in front of my house. Is this a pleasant surprise of winter?",
  [21562302] = "Finally, there's snow in Loveland City! I'm gonna go out and play in the snow!",
  [21562303] = "The snowscape is indeed beautiful, but we need to put on more clothes to prevent colds.",
  [21562304] = "Snowy weather makes it nice to drink a cup of hot tea around the hearth. Some dessert would make it even more perfect.",
  [21562401] = "I woke to find that it was snowing outside! I put on my cotton-padded coat and, slipping and staggering, ran downstairs to see the snow!",
  [21562402] = "The campus has been occupied by grotesque snowmen! Snow is super fun!",
  [21562403] = "I remember that in my childhood, whenever it snowed, my grandmother would put a couple of sweet tangerines above the stove...",
  [21562404] = "I saw a kid keep his head tilted backward with his mouth open to let the snowflakes fall into it, and I couldn't help but follow suit. The snowflakes tasted sweet!",
  [21563101] = "Is there really no punishment for spreading rumors? These days TV programs are no better than those conscienceless news.",
  [21563102] = "If so many flowers are not suitable, why not directly tell us not to put any flowers in our bedrooms?",
  [21563103] = "How can natural floral fragrances be harmful to health when those who use essential oils to help with sleep are fine? I beg to differ.",
  [21563104] = "The flowers deemed unsuitable for bedrooms in the show—I sleep with them in my bedroom every day, and I sleep like a baby.",
  [21563201] = "Actually, it also has something to do with our tolerance to it, which differs from person to person. It is a trifle improper to jump to conclusions like that.",
  [21563202] = "The other day I saw an article saying that floral fragrance helps with sleep. Who should I believe?",
  [21563203] = "I never put flowers in my bedroom, so I don't care.",
  [21563204] = "I really dislike floral fragrance. Who can understand me? The smell makes me dizzy and nauseous.",
  [21563301] = "I see. No wonder I couldn't get to sleep those days. Culprit found!",
  [21563302] = "It turns out there's so much to learn about adding fragrance to our bedrooms. I've been doing it wrong this whole time.",
  [21563303] = "Friendly advice: many flowers are toxic to pets. Those of you who keep pets at home should keep this in mind!",
  [21563304] = "I took the advice of the show, put the right flowers in my bedroom and, as expected, slept like a baby that night.",
  [21563401] = "I can smell a faint fragrance by my window every summer night. Does anybody know what flower gives that off?",
  [21563402] = "Watching this show saved me a lot of melatonin! I'm really grateful to the crew of the show!",
  [21563403] = "Now I know how important sleep quality is. I'll favorite all those methods that help with sleep!",
  [21563404] = "Floral fragrance really cheers you up! And flowers are quite pleasing to the eye too.",
  [21564101] = "The scientificity of the survival methods demonstrated in the show was questioned, and the show was facing a PR crisis.",
  [21564201] = "It's no good learning those things. I'll just resign myself to my fate.",
  [21564202] = "Dissemination of impractical survival methods is disregard for people's lives.",
  [21564203] = "We only accept and broadcast high-quality, responsible programs.",
  [21564401] = "Thanks for making this show. If that day really comes, I'll know what to do.",
  [21564402] = "If everybody tried to save themself with the methods demonstrated in the show, the success rate of rescue missions would probably be much higher.",
  [21564403] = "Increase media coverage of this show. I won't allow anybody not to have watched such a good show.",
  [21565101] = "Will they please reduce the pop-up ads a little? Accidentally clicking an ad during such an intense scramble for tickets is terribly frustrating!",
  [21565102] = "A singer's concert being the most-searched topic for so long is kind of an act of hogging public resources, isn't it?",
  [21565103] = "The price of scalped tickets has become absurd. Will someone please do something about it?",
  [21565104] = "They want us to pay to watch it online? Their hunger for money must've driven them insane...",
  [21565201] = "The concert has been overwhelming my news feed. Why is every media company piggybacking on Kiro's popularity?",
  [21565202] = "None of the purchase channels can last more than 1 second before it becomes jammed. Will they please streamline the website a little?",
  [21565203] = "Those of you who have managed to get tickets, will you please stop showing off? It's really maddening!",
  [21565204] = "What does this device do? Is the organizer really not trying to swindle more money out of us for the tickets?",
  [21565301] = "After failing to get an in-person ticket, I immediately went to the website to buy a ticket for the online concert without lamenting for a single moment!",
  [21565302] = "I strongly advise everybody not to go to the concert, because I have to work overtime that day. [Tearstorm] ",
  [21565303] = "It's not that I can't afford a ticket to the venue. It's just watching it online is better value. (Actually I overslept and didn't get a ticket...",
  [21565304] = "There are actually tickets for watching it online. Kiro is spoiling his fans! Kiro is worth it!",
  [21565401] = "There's no way I'm missing the last stop! Wait for me, Kiro!!!!",
  [21565402] = "Good news: those who failed to get a ticket will be able to watch it online. Better news: I got a ticket!!!",
  [21565403] = "[Squeak like a marmot] [Faint with excitement] [Wriggle and crawl] These were my reactions when I snagged a ticket.",
  [21565404] = "How did you guys know I won a ticket to the concert in the lottery? Come and get your share of my good luck, sisters!",
  [21566101] = "The price of each generation of the product is higher than that of the last, but its performance has barely changed. I'm not buying it.",
  [21566102] = "Having a Golden Apple makes you superior these days? I can't believe there's a hierarchy among electronic device users now.",
  [21566103] = "The new product seems poor value. I think I'll stick to my old one till it breaks...",
  [21566104] = "The product launch was a bit boring. It stood no comparison with the awe-inspiring launch of the first generation.",
  [21566201] = "Sometimes having only one big fish in the pond is not a good thing. I hope more competitive tech companies will emerge.",
  [21566202] = "It strikes me that Infinite has been less dedicated to production since it gained popularity. Its marketing campaigns are getting increasingly frequent, though.",
  [21566203] = "Everybody seems to be using Golden Apple now and I'm getting bored of it. It doesn't seem as good as people say it is.",
  [21566204] = "The price is as exorbitant as always. I can only say that Infinite never swindles poor people.",
  [21566301] = "I have a premonition that if you gift your significant other with a Golden Apple 4, they'll scream with excitement!",
  [21566302] = "Leaving aside its upgraded performance, its improved portability alone is enough to get me to buy the product.",
  [21566303] = "I woke to find that the 4th generation of Golden Apple had been launched. I'm a college student. Please gimme one for free!",
  [21566304] = "I've added it to my Wishlist. For the latter half of the year, it'll be my motivation for working hard!",
  [21566401] = "What? Improved portability? Does that mean I'll be able to play Odyssey on a subway train?",
  [21566402] = "The product launch was a killer! The time I spent waiting on the channel was worthwhile. It was heavy with high-tech vibes!",
  [21566403] = "New Infinite products never fail to surprise me, and this one's no exception!",
  [21566404] = "It's drop-dead amazing that players can enter the game anytime, anywhere! You really know how to empty my wallet, Infinite!",
  [21567101] = "How did this happen exactly? Would it kill them to offer us a definite explanation?",
  [21567102] = "With such media groups who like to fabricate and exaggerate things, Loveland City will probably descend into panic again.",
  [21567103] = "What the heck? I thought there would be a UFO or something like that. This is all it has to offer?",
  [21567104] = "I think it's fake. They kind of overdid the photoshopping, didn't they? It doesn't look like something that can happen in the real world.",
  [21567201] = "It's hard not to be reminded of the recent rumors. Is the world really coming to an end?",
  [21567202] = "When I saw that thing, my first reaction was: did another love rat just swear to God?",
  [21567203] = "I think it's about time the crew of the show upgraded their equipment. The blurry footage makes me dizzy.",
  [21567204] = "I suddenly become worried, and I keep having this feeling that this weather might be an omen of something...",
  [21567301] = "It was really an astounding scene. To photograph it, I got bedraggled. Worse still, I caught a cold when I got back...",
  [21567302] = "When the sky suddenly darkened, I really thought the end of the world was coming...",
  [21567303] = "I kind of sympathize with the reporters in the front line. They had to work overtime in such weather. They must be paid extra!",
  [21567304] = "It's so horrifying... I feel lucky to be indoors at that time...",
  [21567401] = "I was there! I can testify that all the photos are real! It was a blood-curdling scene!",
  [21567402] = "I'm grateful to those in the front line for their aid, and to the brave correspondents for taking risks to shoot precious footage for us.",
  [21567403] = "I don't know why, but I kind of like this vibe. It's like an immersive experience of a 4D disaster movie!",
  [21567404] = "I'll take a wild guess. Was it caused by a cultivator trying to pass the celestial trial to achieve immortality?",
  [21568101] = "The doctor says if you have a cold and don't take any medicine, you'll recover in a week; if you take the right pills, you'll recover in 7 days.",
  [21568102] = "It clearly takes only a good night's sleep to cure a cold, but they actually made a show to discuss it. I really admire such spirit.",
  [21568103] = "As a med student, I gotta say: do not believe a single word of that. Their method will serve only to make things worse!",
  [21568104] = "These experts' remarks make a lot of sense because I can't understand any of them.",
  [21568201] = "What a joke. My boss will never grant me a leave of absence just because I have a cold. I won't get any chances to have a rest cure.",
  [21568202] = "They offered no definite methods to differentiate many of the symptoms mentioned in the show. I suggest they be more specific about it.",
  [21568203] = "Who knows the reason? This head doctor looks so much like my superior I feel a constriction in my chest whenever I hear his voice...",
  [21568204] = "That's too much trouble. If I take all the pills, one of them has got to cure me, right?",
  [21568301] = "It's pretty practical. I suggest they make another show about the prevention of colds—nip it in the bud.",
  [21568302] = "When I was little, I liked the sweet cold medicine so much that I always looked forward to catching a cold. I don't know if there are other people who did the same thing like me.",
  [21568303] = "I keep hearing the phrase \"suit the remedy to the disease.\" Now I know what it really means. This one's worth favoriting.",
  [21568304] = "I have a cold, sisters. I'll try the method mentioned in the show, and I'll come back to tell you the results in three days!",
  [21568401] = "I'd only just caught a cold when I saw this show. The timing was perfect! It's cold lately, and many people I know have caught a cold.",
  [21568402] = "No wonder cold medicine feels ineffective. So this is the reason! The Internet does have some useful stuff to offer!",
  [21568403] = "I'll mark this first! It'll come in handy next time someone I know catches a cold.",
  [21568404] = "Cold is an ailment, but it can lead to many complications. Don't take it lightly, guys!",
  [21569101] = "The topic is unpopular. Hardly anybody's talking about it.",
  [21569201] = "Thrilling as movies are, I think there are hardly any opportunities for us to be heroes in real life.",
  [21569202] = "It seems rather unnecessary for us to discuss this issue.",
  [21569203] = "Maybe it'll be better to switch to a more mundane topic.",
  [21569401] = "Be it in movies or in real life, heroes will always be the most stirring theme.",
  [21569402] = "We're not heroes, but we stand ready to give up everything to protect our people and their property.",
  [21569403] = "Who hasn't, at some time or another, dreamed of becoming a hero?",
  [21570101] = "What a lousy video. It's virtually harming the Special Task Force's image with the populace!",
  [21570102] = "The stall looks a bit unhygienic. Does the food really not give the Special Agents stomach upset?",
  [21570103] = "Why is the boss always poker-faced? I never dine in a restaurant whose customer service is poor, no matter how good the food is.",
  [21570104] = "I once dined there. They seem to season their food with inferior spices to make it spicy. It gave me diarrhea!",
  [21570201] = "To be honest, the spicy hot pot in this eater is really unsatisfactory. At least it's not to my liking.",
  [21570202] = "Today's show makers actually dare piggyback on the Special Task Force's popularity? They've got balls!",
  [21570203] = "I think eating that stuff late at night every day is unhealthy. I'm concerned about the Special Agents' health.",
  [21570204] = "Does nobody feel it's kind of weird that the Special Task Force has been frequently involved in shows and this kind of news?",
  [21570301] = "The one below my flat is the only spicy hot pot eatery I'll ever recommend. I've been dining in it since my childhood!",
  [21570302] = "I've always had this question: do you guys add sesame sauce when you have a spicy hot pot?",
  [21570303] = "I hate veggies, but I can eat two big bowlfuls of veggies in one breath if they're cooked in a spicy hot pot!",
  [21570304] = "A moment ago I was dithering over what to have for dinner, but now I've made a decision. I'll order a spicy hot pot!",
  [21570401] = "I like spicy hot pot as much as the Special Agents do! Rounding that off, I = a Special Agent (Not!",
  [21570402] = "I can't help but picture the usually serious and handsome Special Agents wolfing spicy hot pot at the stall. Adorable!",
  [21570403] = "The sight of the warmly yellow gleam of the lamplight at the spicy hot pot stall alone makes me feel warm. How can anything be more therapeutic than a bowl of spicy hot pot?",
  [21570404] = "Does this mean I might chance on some Special Agents if I go to that stall at a late hour? I suddenly got a bold idea!",
  [21571101] = "The related departments are always still investigating, and the truth will stay unknown forever...",
  [21571102] = "I've been seeing panic-stricken faces everywhere I go. Will someone please do something about it?",
  [21571103] = "Since no conclusion has been drawn, they should've kept quiet about it. What a waste of our time.",
  [21571104] = "It strikes me as fake. I mean, back in that year, a lot of people claimed to have seen UFOs...",
  [21571201] = "The authorities are having a very hard time, too. They're trying to find a way to gloss over this.",
  [21571202] = "They still haven't figured it out? Do they really have to wait until someone gets hurt or killed to take the matter seriously?",
  [21571203] = "There are a lot more others who saw oddities apart from these. The crew of the show can't even collect gossip properly.",
  [21571204] = "I've always been a materialist, but now I can't help wondering if ghosts really exist.",
  [21571301] = "I woke to find my chicken drumstick had been reduced to a bone. Does that count? Oh, my cat ate it. Well, forget it.",
  [21571302] = "Weren't there a lot of people looking forward to seeing a miracle? Now it has really appeared. Why are you scared?",
  [21571303] = "Finding out the truth will take time. Please calm down, everybody.",
  [21571304] = "Am I the only one finding it miraculous? At least there hasn't been any danger so far.",
  [21571401] = "Here comes a witness! I didn't feel any fear when I first saw it. Actually, I was kind of awed!",
  [21571402] = "The crew of the show reacted so quickly! You have my attention. I'll stay tuned for more!",
  [21571403] = "Unbelievable. The chat group of my family is filled with wild guesses. Some are even talking about aliens...",
  [21571404] = "I suggest they make another couple of shows specially to scotch the rumors. After all, scotching rumors is much harder than starting them.",
  [21572101] = "So the culprit was, for the nth time, the undulation of Evol, right? It strikes me that they're pinning everything on Evol undulation these days.",
  [21572102] = "Do you people feel that the public are easy to fool? We need a plausible explanation!",
  [21572103] = "I feel that they really regard this damn thing as a foolproof booster of popularity. I mean, how many similar shows have they made out of it?",
  [21572104] = "They talked on and on for so long but I still don't know what happened. They're no better than those marketing accounts.",
  [21572201] = "Things are getting increasingly confusing. I wonder if there's a twist coming.",
  [21572202] = "That's unlikely. I saw bright firelight from the foot of the hill that day...",
  [21572203] = "They had me stare at the screen for half an hour when they could've clarified the matter with one remark. What a waste of time.",
  [21572204] = "Didn't they ascertain the truth yesterday? They had the nerve to release it a day later and call it news.",
  [21572301] = "No matter what, I'm glad there's no casualty caused. I hope no harm will come to anybody.",
  [21572302] = "I was greatly relieved when I heard the announcement from the authority. There's indeed nothing more beautiful than a false alarm.",
  [21572303] = "The pheasants, hares, and wild goats on the hill: That was so close. I nearly thought I died.",
  [21572304] = "No matter what, wildfires are dangerous. Make sure not to barbecue on a hill, guys!",
  [21572401] = "I'm glad nobody got hurt! The firelight on the hill was definitely an omen of everything going perfectly in the next year!",
  [21572402] = "Ha-ha! It's actually a false alarm! The animals on the hill must be confused too!",
  [21572403] = "It suddenly feels like a big twist in a TV series! How very thrilling! Fortunately, the ending is a happy one.",
  [21572404] = "Only yesterday I posted a message in Moments cursing the arsonist, but I woke up this morning to be told it was all a misunderstanding.",
  [21573101] = "I don't see anything inspiring in the show. On the contrary, it strikes me they're taking advantage of those affected.",
  [21573102] = "Will you media people stop making things worse, please? I can tell members of the rescue team are having a really hard time.",
  [21573103] = "I loathe the show's attitude toward the disaster. Not everything can be used for recreational purposes.",
  [21573104] = "That's quite some sweet talk, but I haven't seen any actual action. How come none of them made any donations to the affected people?",
  [21573201] = "I can't shake the feeling that there have been increasingly frequent natural disasters lately. Is doomsday really coming?",
  [21573202] = "We all know what it's like, but getting sappy on it is really unnecessary...",
  [21573203] = "Exactly when will this damnable rain stop? Is it going to spread to other areas?",
  [21573204] = "Even such a serious program has mid-roll ads in it. Have you media people no conscience?",
  [21573301] = "Earlier today I donated some supplies to the victims through the show in the hope of helping them out.",
  [21573302] = "I saw a lot of doctors, paramedics, firefighters, and Special Agents striving themselves in the front line, and I wanna say to them: thank you for your service.",
  [21573303] = "This flood has the attention of hundreds of thousands of Loveland citizens. I hope the disaster will soon come to an end.",
  [21573304] = "I've been in the TV station waiting for news reports all day long. I hope there won't be any more casualties!",
  [21573401] = "A very stirring show! Seeing these in a time like this is quite heartwarming!",
  [21573402] = "It brought tears to my eyes! Loveland citizens have always been so optimistic and tenacious. We'll never yield in any circumstance!",
  [21573403] = "Disasters will only make us more united! I'm proud of being a Loveland citizen!",
  [21573404] = "I really feel like crying when I see front-line workers making sacrifices out there! They're the most loveable people!",
  [21574101] = "The topic sparked little discussion, and the post soon sank.",
  [21574201] = "If I could see into the future, I would, naturally, make sure every decision I make is the right one.",
  [21574202] = "It seems pointless to talk about whether we regret something or not, given how old we are.",
  [21574203] = "Looks like not many people are interested in this topic. It's hardly worth discussing.",
  [21574401] = "\"Making the choice\" matters more to life than \"making the right choice\" does.",
  [21574402] = "Looking back on the past, I feel that the choices that I made and later deemed \"wrong\" were actually not bad.",
  [21574403] = "The hashtag #Life's Fork became a trending topic overnight, and its popularity stays stubbornly high.",
  [21575101] = "If it were really so easy to make money with We-Media, nobody would go to work.",
  [21575102] = "Please stop publicizing such stuff, 'cause many grade school students are dreaming of becoming influencers and no longer want to go to school.",
  [21575103] = "Those who keep dreaming of easy success will only end up falling prey to other people's schemes.",
  [21575104] = "Who would willingly share their secret to wealth with others? Use your brain...",
  [21575201] = "After watching it, I feel that this thing is not for people like me who prefer simple stuff. Getting a job would be a better choice.",
  [21575202] = "If I had seen this a few years back, it'd be very useful to me. But now, I can only say it's like an expired winning lottery ticket.",
  [21575203] = "In the age of We-Media, everybody's fantasizing about achieving success, but actually, those who did succeed are few and far between.",
  [21575204] = "As someone who has started a new business and failed, I find this sales pitch very unconvincing...",
  [21575301] = "Overall, this one pretty much covers everything, but starting a business is not without risk. It's advisable to think twice before making a decision.",
  [21575302] = "I started doing We-Media from scratch after losing my job, and I have to say that success is indeed possible if you have a strong will.",
  [21575303] = "When the opportunity of the era comes, everyone who seizes it is admirable.",
  [21575304] = "A very practical strategy guide. Even if you have no ambition to become a famous influencer, making some extra money by doing side work at home can be pretty nice.",
  [21575401] = "Darn it! I wish I'd seen this sooner! I wouldn't have suffered so many setbacks had I seen this useful strategy guide sooner!",
  [21575402] = "I once got swindled by a conscienceless pre-paid course seller, and I've lost hope in it. Never thought I'd find a new continent today.",
  [21575403] = "Please enter my Favorites folder to gather dust! Tee-hee, maybe someday it'll come in handy, who knows?",
  [21575404] = "I've been searching for a strategy guide about making money via We-Media like this for quite some time. Now I finally found one!",
  [21576101] = "The way this streamer eats is kind of unpleasant. I don't know why they're so popular...",
  [21576102] = "Is popularity really worth sacrificing your health for? They seem to have a hard time eating!",
  [21576103] = "I'm confused so I'll ask: who's watching this kind of mukbang? 'Cause I can't stand watching it for a second.",
  [21576104] = "I opened it thinking it'd boost my appetite, but it had the opposite effect. It's suitable for those seeking to lose weight.",
  [21576201] = "I watched for a long while and found that most of the time the streamer was talking instead of eating. It's kind of disappointing.",
  [21576202] = "Lately, several big-eater streamers have developed health problems. You should be cautious, streamer.",
  [21576203] = "Seeing as how they eat so much but are still so thin, they're definitely using emetics. Anyway, don't take it too seriously.",
  [21576204] = "The foods the streamer's eating—are they really tasty? Why do those things look utterly unappetizing to me?",
  [21576301] = "This streamer is virtually an example to follow for all foodies like me. I'll make sure to eat more and more!",
  [21576302] = "How I wish I could sit by the streamer's side and dine with them! Could anyone make my dream come true?",
  [21576303] = "All the foods on the table today are my favorites. Watching this makes both my mouth and my eyes water...",
  [21576304] = "Why do I feel the food the streamer's eating is kind of problematic? Not sure. Please mail it to me so I can examine it.",
  [21576401] = "The streamer has such an amazing appetite!!! I can eat three more bowls of rice than usual while watching this!",
  [21576402] = "I like this kind of streamer who does nothing but eat quietly. Those noisy ones are virtually spiritual pollution!",
  [21576403] = "You're my favorite electronic piggy on the Internet! What are you having for dinner today, sweetheart?",
  [21576404] = "I watch this every day. The streamer's menu determines what I'll have for dinner tonight, 'cause the food looks so yummy!",
  [21577101] = "I won't believe a single word of those exaggerations from the media, 'cause I don't wanna be disappointed again.",
  [21577102] = "What's the point of inventing this alarm and the likes of it? I want our world to be Evol-free.",
  [21577103] = "If Infinite is capable of this, why didn't they invent this thing sooner? If they had, maybe those incidents wouldn't have happened.",
  [21577104] = "Some company appears to be overdoing its marketing. Be careful. It might backfire.",
  [21577201] = "They're hyping it up when it hasn't even been officially launched yet. I hope the product proves worthy of these compliments eventually.",
  [21577202] = "It's a product designed to generate profits, not a divine tool devised to save the world. It'll do you good to see this from a rational perspective.",
  [21577203] = "The range of the alarm device's detection and the minimum intensity of Evol it can detect are still unknown. I think I'll sit tight and watch for a little while longer.",
  [21577204] = "Nobody wants to speak up for Evolvers? I'll have to be even more cautious from now on, lest I trigger anybody's alarm.",
  [21577301] = "I've long since heard of this research. I'm waiting for a product launch!",
  [21577302] = "Though a bit worried that there might be some kind of blocking device designed to counter the alarm in the future, at least for now I can sleep tight!",
  [21577303] = "I just wanna ask: will I be able to buy one of those things as an individual and install it in my house?",
  [21577304] = "The media are hyping it up like crazy, but I only trust your news reports. I hope you won't let me down!",
  [21577401] = "The mere sound of the name Infinite is reassuring enough. This company never ceased to surprise us!",
  [21577402] = "Fantastic! There have been thousands of rumors about Evol detectors, and this time I can finally dismiss my doubts!",
  [21577403] = "You can trust Infinite in any circumstance, really! Will I never have to worry about the danger of Evol getting out of control again?",
  [21577404] = "I'm so excited. This invention is an inspiring good thing for both Evolvers and regular people!",
  [21578101] = "Is this some kind of new means of hype? Never thought even a CEO needed to construct their image.",
  [21578102] = "You may take my word for it: if a CEO who cooks does exist, I'll reverse my name to be my new name! (My name's Bob",
  [21578103] = "I think it's some media speculation again. Remember the rumor saying the CEO of LFG was an Evolver? It's really ridiculous.",
  [21578104] = "Even if the owner of the restaurant was God, I would still blacklist it because of their poor service.",
  [21578201] = "Just skip to the last step. Some company is about to launch some new project and could use some exposure, right?",
  [21578202] = "I know that in your fantasies all company presidents are omnipotent, and cooking is far from a problem for them. (Manual dog head",
  [21578203] = "How much did you Souvenir people pay them? I, the owner of Yao's Bun, will pay you triple!",
  [21578204] = "Am I the only one who doesn't care about the restaurant or the president? It's none of my business, anyway.",
  [21578301] = "I took a closer look and I was like: isn't it the restaurant right below my apartment which always stays closed? I've never been so close to a company president.",
  [21578302] = "A mere restaurant is causing so much fuss. I can only say that some CEO is indeed at the top of the commercial hierarchy.",
  [21578303] = "Does nobody else find the name of the restaurant's seasonal menu adorable? It surprises me the president has a girlish side.",
  [21578304] = "Please stop being so enthusiastic, guys. If it goes on like this, I'm afraid the CEO would haul the restaurant to their shoulder and flee overnight.",
  [21578401] = "So the bossy CEO in romantic fiction has come alive! I could use a CEO who cooks well!!!",
  [21578402] = "The good news is: that I actually had a meal cooked by the CEO! Bad news: I also gave the CEO a bad review with my own hands.",
  [21578403] = "Employees of a certain company, you guys are in for a treat, 'cause your CEO might literally be a good \"firer.\"",
  [21578404] = "The CEO aside, don't you guys think today's show radiates strong detective movie vibes? The show crew really knows their stuff!",
  [21579101] = "Ratings of the show on the major websites dropped to 1-star merely two days after it aired.",
  [21579201] = "I didn't see any plot twists. Watching this kind of mini-series is virtually a waste of my life.",
  [21579202] = "The shots of the food are unbelievably perfunctory. They make the foods look awfully unappetizing.",
  [21579203] = "Its lameness is kind of its strength too, 'cause at least it provides materials for roast videos.",
  [21579401] = "I was reduced to tears. I kind of see myself in the protagonist! Maybe I'll achieve a twist ending of my own if I hang in there for a little while longer!",
  [21579402] = "The foods in those scenes are so tantalizing! I wish I could magic myself into the screen and wolf down them all!",
  [21579403] = "This one deserves to be seen by everybody! If I had to rate it, I'd give it full marks!",
  [21580101] = "If I remember right, a certain Bazaar used to be notorious for its abundance of counterfeits. Now they're whitewashing it. Do they think the Internet has no memory?",
  [21580102] = "Give your ad division a break, Grand Bazaar, 'cause I need you to tell me this first: how many people's support do I have to get before I can withdraw the money?",
  [21580103] = "Don't fall for it, guys. The other day I bought a pair of shoes from Grand Bazaar and they turned out to be counterfeits, and worst still, the seller blocked me!",
  [21580104] = "Genuineness of goods aside, it took logistics a month to make the delivery of my last order, and it's not even home delivery. Trashy service!",
  [21580201] = "The promised red packet rebate is nowhere to be seen. I should've known platforms that advertise couldn't be trusted.",
  [21580202] = "I uninstalled the app after using it only once. Their customer service team is full of lies.",
  [21580203] = "I don't dare give any of those sellers a bad review, 'cause they'll harass me over the phone. Grand Bazaar will stay on my blacklist forever.",
  [21580204] = "I suspect that those hyping up this software have never used it. The user experience is awful.",
  [21580301] = "They say Grand Bazaar's customer service is awesome, and that they offer you refunds whenever you want them to. I'll give it a try when I get back.",
  [21580302] = "Perfect for lazy people like me. I can place an order simply by tapping a button, and the quality of the product is guaranteed.",
  [21580303] = "Having tried it once, I'm positive this platform will be a smash hit. Business people who really put themselves in customers' shoes can't be too bad.",
  [21580304] = "Now I do only three things when I'm at home: eat, sleep, shopping in Grand Bazaar.",
  [21580401] = "My treasure is finally about to be discovered? I've long since found that products in Grand Bazaar are much cheaper, and everything I've bought from it is genuine!",
  [21580402] = "So you've finally brought yourself to advertise, my Bazaar? When I recommended it to my friends the other day, they were all astounded and said they'd never heard of it.",
  [21580403] = "Astounding! The handbag I ordered on a certain Bay is so much cheaper here! I'll cancel my order and place a new one here right now!",
  [21580404] = "I hereby declare that from this day onward, Grand Bazaar will be my shopping paradise! Who doesn't love a shopping platform that offers good prices and quality assurance?",
  [21581101] = "I don't see the point in making this show. If all you can do after being robbed in a game is complain, then maybe games are not suitable for you.",
  [21581102] = "My favorite guest kept getting their lines robbed. The producer's partiality is way too obvious.",
  [21581103] = "These guests all seem to be forcing themselves to make conversation. My time will be put to better use if I play a video game instead of listening to their nonsense.",
  [21581104] = "The contents of the show are nonsensical, and the comments section is a mess. It's a perfect example of a failed show.",
  [21581201] = "You overthink it. The existence of the gains earnable from robbery means the development team encourages this kind of behavior. The malice you face is not solely from players.",
  [21581202] = "Is this really worth discussing? What fun is it to play games if robbery is not allowed?",
  [21581203] = "In-game robbers are not necessarily evil. Some people just enjoy playing the villain in the virtual world.",
  [21581204] = "I think those speaking up for bandits should go straighten their worldview first.",
  [21581301] = "Actually, since the development team allows this playstyle, there's no need to keep criticizing it. In video games, the strong are always in the right.",
  [21581302] = "Today I sent some players who attempted to rob me into prison! It's so fulfilling!",
  [21581303] = "But then again, robbing those \"studio players\" who sabotage the game environment is, in a sense, chivalry, isn't it?",
  [21581304] = "It's advisable to offer newbies some protection, 'cause it really feels awful to get robbed in the early game.",
  [21581401] = "Ha ha... The guests' bizarre opinions are drop-dead hilarious! I can listen to them chat for a year and not get bored!",
  [21581402] = "I suggest all major gaming companies come and learn. All these are what players like us truly feel!",
  [21581403] = "Aargh! I got robbed of my package again! Those damnable robbers! I hope their behavior will be met with more severe punishment!",
  [21581404] = "I robbed people and got robbed as well, and I totally agree with the methodology in the show, 'cause you can't play it without taking risks!",
  [21582101] = "Why do collection in a hardcore game? It's just inopportune.",
  [21582102] = "No matter what you're after in games, players who are unaware of in-game mechanisms and hold teammates back in dungeons will never grow on me.",
  [21582103] = "Isn't the normal playstyle a playstyle as well? Why do I feel people deem it inferior now?",
  [21582104] = "The show crew is obviously impartial. It's okay if you wanna fawn on those weird players, but please leave normal players like us out of it.",
  [21582201] = "Of course video games should include more than one playstyle, but it's totally unnecessary to feel proud of these \"unconventional\" playstyles.",
  [21582202] = "But will those niche players please stop polluting the PvP environment? Being teamed up with them is a real disaster.",
  [21582203] = "I don't understand, respect, or agree with it. There are tons of other games in which players can collect appearances, do sightseeing, and grow crops. Why not play those games instead?",
  [21582204] = "Those so-called \"casual players\" are just using that name as a fig leaf for their weakness. Let them keep it.",
  [21582301] = "The greatest charm of the game lies in diversity. Those who laugh at other people's playstyles are being played by the game.",
  [21582302] = "The show crew said what I wanted to say: I can play the game however I want so long as it doesn't cause trouble to other players.",
  [21582303] = "I didn't know there could be so many playstyles in this game. I'm gonna give them a try when I get back!",
  [21582304] = "I turned from a power-seeking player into a casual one. Experiencing different pleasures the game has to offer is a joy as well!",
  [21582401] = "I was subjected to doubts from other players for collecting in-game items as well, and now I can finally throw my chest out!",
  [21582402] = "Chatting and sightseeing with my friends in the game is my favorite thing to do! Who said martial arts games are all about fighting?",
  [21582403] = "I'm not the only one who logs into the game daily simply to water the crops, I presume? Every time I harvest, I feel a great sense of accomplishment!",
  [21582404] = "I'm a power-seeker in the game, but many of my friends in the game focus on taking pictures of in-game scenery and collecting appearances, and we all have a bright future!",
  [21583101] = "Facts prove that no matter how hard you try to evoke nostalgia in a show, it won't work if the show is of inferior quality.",
  [21583102] = "I miss the shows I watched in my childhood. They're not as boring as this one.",
  [21583103] = "There's no need to keep reminiscing about childhood. Besides, not everybody had a happy childhood.",
  [21583104] = "They want it to be both heartwarming and funny. Facts prove that combining the two leads to the loss of both.",
  [21583201] = "I've never had any secret wonderlands, and I don't understand why anybody would wanna discuss such a childish topic.",
  [21583202] = "There's nothing worth remembering about my childhood, and I don't ever wanna remember what I was like in my childhood.",
  [21583203] = "As a child grows into an adult, their secret childhood wonderland will gradually become the grave of their childhood, I think.",
  [21583204] = "I was in a bad mood, and watching this show successfully reminded me of my childhood friend with whom I've severed ties. Now I feel even worse.",
  [21583301] = "Those who have a secret wonderland must also have a happy childhood. I don't seem to remember ever having a place like that...",
  [21583302] = "It feels like only yesterday I was climbing trees and walls and wreaking havoc everywhere I went. When on earth did I grow up?",
  [21583303] = "It's not that our secret childhood wonderlands had miraculous powers. It's just we have more things to worry about as adults than our secret wonderlands can hold.",
  [21583304] = "My secret wonderland seems to have changed after I grew up. It's become my home, one I've been painstakingly building.",
  [21583401] = "I'm grateful to this show for bringing back memories of my beautiful childhood. Time is really a miraculous thing!",
  [21583402] = "Ha ha! My secret wonderland is probably no more, but all my childhood friends are still around, for which I'm very thankful!",
  [21583403] = "Who said kidults couldn't have their own secret wonderlands? I, a 300-month-old baby, am stealthily snacking in my secret wonderland!",
  [21583404] = "My secret wonderland is my mom's embrace. Having my arms around my mom is enough to dismiss all my vexations!",
  [21584101] = "The show received middling reviews after airing.",
  [21584201] = "Consumers should have the freedom to make their own choices. They don't deserve moral blackmail.",
  [21584202] = "It's harder and harder to make money by selling physical genuine books. Selling pirated books is much more profitable.",
  [21584203] = "Websites providing pirated content are impossible to defend against. There's nothing we could do.",
  [21584401] = "Boycott of piracy must be more than just a slogan, and putting it into action requires collective efforts of us all.",
  [21584402] = "Is physical printing about to be rejuvenated?",
  [21584403] = "Fellow avid readers who actively report piracy sites will receive Reader Tokens from the platform as rewards.",
  [21585101] = "Is it from a registered media channel? I can tell at a glance this name list is fake. It can't be any more absurd!",
  [21585102] = "Some \"superstar\" is among the nominees too? Is this whole thing a fix? 'cause their new song really sucks!",
  [21585103] = "In the country of the blind, the one-eyed man is king, you know. In all previous years competition for the award was insane, but this year all nominees are clowns!",
  [21585104] = "Some artist is getting so excited over a mere nomination. If they really win the award, it'll really mark the end of mainland showbiz.",
  [21585201] = "Is this nomination list real? There are so many rumors on the Internet I don't know which one to believe...",
  [21585202] = "Such secrecy over a mere nomination is totally unnecessary. All those media speculations make me feel exhausted.",
  [21585203] = "Am I the only one who finds this whole nomination thing boring? I can tell at a glance a certain artist is the only possible winner of the award, and all other nominees are guaranteed also-rans.",
  [21585204] = "It surprises me even the Celestial Hare Honor has been in decline. Finding a good song on the ranking list is getting increasingly hard.",
  [21585301] = "Have you guys noticed? This year's nominations are pretty well deserved. All finalists are true warriors!",
  [21585302] = "What should I do? Everyone on the list is my favorite. No matter which one of them wins the award, I'll be equally happy!",
  [21585303] = "I wanna grab a time machine and time-travel to the day of the award ceremony. All this waiting is killing me!",
  [21585304] = "The day of the award ceremony happens to be my birthday. I've got only one wish, and that's to see him standing on the podium.",
  [21585401] = "This media group is the first to release news of it, I presume? I did the right thing by pinning my hopes on this one, and now I got a head start over my fellow gossip-lovers!",
  [21585402] = "I got a wild guess in my mind! But I don't dare give voice to it at the moment!",
  [21585403] = "AAAARGH! It's so stressful to be in this phase! What do you guys think? Is Kiro the most promising candidate this year?",
  [21585404] = "I've begun to wonder what my idol will be wearing at the award ceremony, but whatever he wears, he'll always be the shiniest star!",
  [21586101] = "The most boring award ceremony ever. As for the winner... I can only say: congrats.",
  [21586102] = "Not even a fraction of Kiro's real charm is presented in the footage. They could choose not to film it if they couldn't find a competent cameraperson, and the producer could choose not to make this show if they didn't know how to make it right.",
  [21586103] = "The Celestial Hare Honor has lost the glamor it used to have. I wouldn't have watched it had I known beforehand.",
  [21586104] = "This is unbelievable. There's hardly any close-up of the award winner. Even the host got more close-ups than he did.",
  [21586201] = "Am I hallucinating? The award ceremony strikes me as a bit boring. Even the speculations and anticipation in the few preceding days were more enjoyable than this.",
  [21586202] = "The couple of nominated movies all strike me as a bit lame. Did nobody make any decent movies this year?",
  [21586203] = "Falling over, scrambling for the central position, darkening the face on the podium... it surprises me nobody displayed any of those traditional skills today. It's kind of disappointing.",
  [21586204] = "The nomination for Best Supporting Actress really confuses me... If I remember right, she can't even memorize her lines, and the only line she knows is \"1, 2, 3, 4.\"",
  [21586301] = "The result is unsurprising, 'cause sooner or later everybody would see how hard he's been working.",
  [21586302] = "I feel like crying. Watching him stand on the podium makes me feel like I was watching him make his debut when he was a teenager. I hope Kiro will stay true to his original aspirations forever.",
  [21586303] = "The winner of the award is not the only one who deserves the applause. All those who have been striving on the path of music are equally deserving of it.",
  [21586304] = "This is destined to be an unforgettable night. I sincerely feel happy for Kiro, and I hope his career gets more and more successful.",
  [21586401] = "Tonight all the spotlight and honor belongs to Kiro! Please repeat this with me aloud—Kiro is worthy of it all!!",
  [21586402] = "Kiro the shiniest star! Kiro the love of my life! Kiro the one and only superstar!",
  [21586403] = "Kiro shines wherever there is a stage! See you at your concert, Kiro!",
  [21586404] = "Boohoo! Who's crying so hard? Oh, it's me! I, a female believer, will eat a balanced diet for the rest of my life if that's what it takes for Kiro's path to be always carpeted with petals!",
  [21587101] = "I almost thought this game was a goner. Buying such topic popularity is the only thing they can do now.",
  [21587102] = "You think releasing a commoner strategy guide can erase the fact that you've been fawning on whales? What you should do is pull those pay-to-win items from the shelves first.",
  [21587103] = "No matter how many 0-pay strategy guides they release, it won't make any difference. Zero-pay makes things a lot harder in the game. It's an undeniable fact.",
  [21587104] = "Is this strategy guide useful? Oh, it's for 0-pay players. Forget it then. I'm not a 0-pay player.",
  [21587201] = "The author of the strategy guide gained popularity, and the gaming company got players to spend more time in the game. You guys are the only ones believing you got the better of the gaming company.",
  [21587202] = "It's just about earning resources at the cost of time instead of money. Simple as that. You just have to decide how much your time is worth.",
  [21587203] = "I started feeling dizzy after following it for only a few minutes. If 0-pay makes things so tiring, I'd prefer to pay!",
  [21587204] = "Did they release this 0-pay strategy guide because they thought little of players like us who paid? I don't believe a mere strategy guide can be as useful as a monetary investment.",
  [21587301] = "I finished watching the strategy guide overnight. So this is how martial artists in the olden days felt when they came across a martial arts tract!",
  [21587302] = "Tomorrow I'll start following this strategy guide, and I won't miss a shred of the resource obtainable in the game!",
  [21587303] = "If you haven't read it yet, I suggest you do it right now. You're guaranteed to benefit from it!",
  [21587304] = "Right now I'm very worried that the gaming company might do something about it. After all, getting things for free feels really good, and if you keep doing it, you'll keep feeling good!",
  [21587401] = "What? A commoner strategy guide? I used to despise such stuff, but now I'm watching the video frame by frame to learn from it.",
  [21587402] = "This strategy guide is virtually a godsend for 0-pay players! I'll never have to worry about running out of in-game resources anymore!",
  [21587403] = "This strategy guide is like a slap across the face of those who criticized Odyssey as a pay-to-win game! Who said Odyssey was for poor people?",
  [21587404] = "I haven't seen such a player-oriented strategy guide for a long time! And you, my friend, you're a true hero!",
  [21588101] = "My daily question: did Odyssey and its development team die today?",
  [21588102] = "Did you people grab a random guy from the street and make him a streamer? Low commentating speed, inability to understand hotshot players' moves... Even I could do better than he does.",
  [21588103] = "This format is unbelievable. Have they forgotten all about the fairness of e-sports?",
  [21588104] = "Why do they have to make a video game tournament look like a talent competition? I firmly oppose fan club culture invading the gaming industry!",
  [21588201] = "Some of them strike me as average. How come they're still among the top-rankers? Is there some kind of hidden agenda involved?",
  [21588202] = "I can only say that a humorous commentator would've made this match twice as enjoyable.",
  [21588203] = "Will you please stop adding needless segments to create suspense? This is an e-sports competition, not some third-rate suspense movie.",
  [21588204] = "Actually, the championship was decided long before you guys started speculating about it. I got insider knowledge.",
  [21588301] = "It's been a long time since I last watched such an electrifying e-sports competition. Looking forward to it!",
  [21588302] = "Cello Eats No Apple's last move was drop-dead mind-boggling. Is that really possible?",
  [21588303] = "I've been an Odyssey player all along. Never thought watching other players have a competition could be so thrilling. I'm getting addicted to it!",
  [21588304] = "Odyssey has been gaining popularity like crazy. I hope more newbies will join the party. I can't wait to deck some rookies!",
  [21588401] = "AAAARGH! What a bloodbath! The streamer I've been following finished first place!!!!",
  [21588402] = "Is Cello Eats No Apple really KEY's apprentice? Does anybody have the inside scoop?",
  [21588403] = "Every one of the participating streamers is so mysterious and so charming! I can't wait to know who they really are!",
  [21588404] = "These video game streamers are so irresistible! They each have their own skill set and allure. I love them all!",
  [21589101] = "After the news was released, many viewers criticized it as a blatant lie.",
  [21589201] = "Whisk off KEY. Some obscure streamer needs to stop leeching off his popularity.",
  [21589202] = "Has Odyssey's turnover been plunging or something? Otherwise, why are they using this kind of fake news to get exposure?",
  [21589203] = "I think it's all a misunderstanding, so clear off, guys.",
  [21589401] = "KEY the spendthrift has actually become a \"commoner streamer\"! Is this The Frog Prince coming alive?",
  [21589402] = "What a feast of juicy gossip! Everybody's welcome to join Odyssey, an amazing game.",
  [21589403] = "Want a recap on how KEY blew his cover? Come to the channel tonight...",
  [21590101] = "Nowadays class reunions are more like flaunting competitions. Why would I go to any of them?",
  [21590102] = "I went to one, and I still feel terribly embarrassed whenever I recall what it was like. Pretending to be close is really tiring.",
  [21590103] = "Stop kidding yourself. You wouldn't have to wait until a class reunion if you really wanted to hang out with them.",
  [21590104] = "A class reunion is virtually a large-scale torturing session for introverted people, almost as torturous as sitting beside your boss at a team-building dinner party.",
  [21590201] = "The mood among these chatting guests is so award. Are they having a class reunion?",
  [21590202] = "There's nothing worth remembering about my school days, so there's no point meeting any of the people from back then.",
  [21590203] = "Did the producers run out of topics for their shows? If you wanna go, go; if you don't wanna go, don't go!",
  [21590204] = "In my experience, all those who do well love it. Others hate it.",
  [21590301] = "I tend to accept the invitation if any of my close friends will be there, 'cause the worst-case scenario would be me only talking to those I'm close to.",
  [21590302] = "Reminiscing about the past with people from the past would be enough. They wouldn't be able to understand any part of your subsequent life, 'cause they played no part in it.",
  [21590303] = "I had some indescribable feelings after meeting those I hadn't seen for a long time. Yeah, I'm the one who's only just returned from a class reunion.",
  [21590304] = "If my first love goes, I'll be sure to go. I want him to see how much better off I am without him!",
  [21590401] = "How did you know I was going to a class reunion? I'm kind of excited now that I'm about to see my erstwhile classmates who I haven't seen for a long time!",
  [21590402] = "The most heartwarming class reunion I've had was at the campus. It was really like traveling back in time.",
  [21590403] = "I think I'll nerve myself to say what I didn't have the courage to say back then, though my words might only be responded to with a non-committal smile.",
  [21590404] = "The guests' stories about class reunions are hilarious! When I get famous, I'll startle them that way as well!",
  [21591101] = "Putting it on the news won't solve any of the problems. The scammers have escaped, and the victims have fallen victim.",
  [21591102] = "What on earth have you media people been doing? So many cases have happened, and you're only just beginning to take it seriously?",
  [21591103] = "The pixelation of the victims' faces is so perfunctory. Are they sure this won't cause victims trouble?",
  [21591104] = "It's arrant nonsense. How could anybody fall prey if they can tell a scam when they see one?",
  [21591201] = "Wasn't this on the news a long time ago? They're rehashing stuff yet again.",
  [21591202] = "There wouldn't have been so many victims had they reported this sooner. These media people are all Monday morning quarterbacks.",
  [21591203] = "I don't have to finish watching this to know that all problems remain unsolved. I've gotten used to it.",
  [21591204] = "This might make me sound unsympathetic, but I still wanna say: that nobody would be able to swindle you if you're not greedy.",
  [21591301] = "The investment industry is really fraught with pitfalls. Don't think you're the luckiest one.",
  [21591302] = "I would rather be tricked by a love rat than a swindler! Leave my wallet off your target lists if you know what's good for you, scammers!",
  [21591303] = "This show has really been a great help for a lot of people, and it facilitated many victims' efforts to get justice. Thumbs-up to you guys!",
  [21591304] = "Why is the scam company still not closed? I hope they'll be brought to justice and return the money to the victims soon.",
  [21591401] = "Keep your guard up, everybody! Don't think all the victims are fools. That's what I thought till I myself fell victim. T T",
  [21591402] = "I feel so lucky to see this show. I almost got swindled! I have to say frauds are getting scarily deceitful these days.",
  [21591403] = "Everybody needs to keep their guard up. Don't let the con men swindle your hard-earned money!",
  [21591404] = "Only earlier today I received a call from a scammer asking me to make investments. I rebuked him with the words I learned from the show! It felt so good!",
  [21592101] = "The most important thing about a show is not what purpose it serves, but whether the viewers will deem it worth watching, which you people clearly failed to realize.",
  [21592102] = "All these people ever do is lecture the populace. If they got time for this kind of stuff, why have they still not brought the criminals to justice?",
  [21592103] = "I know you guys are just trying to finish your job, but it doesn't have to be so perfunctory, does it?",
  [21592104] = "I should never have had any expectations of this show. The moment I opened this video, I wished I hadn't...",
  [21592201] = "I haven't seen such a hypnotic show for a long time. It'd be nice to play this on a loop at bedtime.",
  [21592202] = "Who was it that made such a boring show? It's virtually a waste of viewers' time.",
  [21592203] = "Please try to keep your mouths shut from now on, experts, 'cause none of your words are worth hearing!",
  [21592204] = "I opened this thinking I'd be able to learn some cyber security knowledge, but my brain seems to be knowledge-proof!",
  [21592301] = "The teacher's wording is vivid, and the crew put a lot of effort into the show. Such well-intentioned law-publicizing shows are something of a rarity these days.",
  [21592302] = "May I suggest that the lecturer put on a hat? His forehead reflecting light keeps distracting me.",
  [21592303] = "A safety lecture suitable for all ages. I learned a lot from it.",
  [21592304] = "Every time I watch a good show like this, I feel that law-publicizing work is indeed beneficial. It can help a lot of people.",
  [21592401] = "This is my first time watching such a lovely law-publicizing show! They're putting young people in charge of such serious shows now?",
  [21592402] = "If all previous safety lectures had been like this one, nobody would've watched any TV series.",
  [21592403] = "I only wanna ask: will there be a sequel to this mini-series? I'm not the only one expecting a sequel, I presume?",
  [21592404] = "Ha ha... It's hilarious! I would've saved it for New Year's Eve had I known a law-publicizing show could be so funny.",
  [21593101] = "They gave themselves away right at the start of the show. If I'm not mistaken, this is an Odyssey ad.",
  [21593102] = "Being able to discuss a relatively profound topic in such a boring way is kind of impressive too...",
  [21593103] = "Impossible. I wonder if you've ever heard of the medical term—\"electronic impotence.\"",
  [21593104] = "In fact, if you think deeper, the electronic world is not really that good. Eventually, it'll feel just as boring as the real world.",
  [21593201] = "Actually, it's no good running away. If you don't do well in the real world, chances are you won't do any better in the electronic world either.",
  [21593202] = "To be honest, I don't care much about the future of humanity, but it doesn't mean you get to pollute my eyes with such a boring show.",
  [21593203] = "Maybe the world we live in is actually a virtual one. We just haven't realized it yet.",
  [21593204] = "This psychologist is full of nonsense. None of their words made any sense.",
